// Tata bahasa + terjemahan Indonesia (otomatis via Google Translate).
export default [{"pattern":"A あるいは B","meaning":"Indicates alternatives; 'A or B', 'either A or B'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan alternatif; 'A atau B', 'A atau B'.","formation":"Phrase A + あるいは + Phrase B","formationId":"Frase A + あるいは + Frase B","examples":[{"jp":"今日は映画を見るあるいはショッピングをする予定です。","romaji":"Kyou wa eiga wo miru aruiwa shoppingu wo suru yotei desu.","en":"Today, I plan to either watch a movie or go shopping.","id":"Hari ini, saya berencana untuk menonton film atau berbelanja."},{"jp":"彼女は英語あるいはドイツ語で話すことができます。","romaji":"Kanojo wa eigo aruiwa doitsugo de hanasu koto ga dekimasu.","en":"She can speak either English or German.","id":"Dia bisa berbicara bahasa Inggris atau Jerman."},{"jp":"僕らはコーヒーあるいは紅茶を飲むのが好きです。","romaji":"Bokura wa koohii aruiwa koucha wo nomu no ga suki desu.","en":"We like to drink either coffee or tea.","id":"Kami suka minum kopi atau teh."},{"jp":"この仕事は正社員あるいは契約社員として働くことができます。","romaji":"Kono shigoto wa seishain aruiwa keiyaku shain toshite hataraku koto ga dekimasu.","en":"You can work as either a full-time employee or a contract employee in this job.","id":"Anda dapat bekerja sebagai karyawan penuh waktu atau karyawan kontrak dalam pekerjaan ini."}]},{"pattern":"A。おまけに B。","meaning":"Expresses that in addition to A, there is also B; 'moreover', 'besides', 'not only', 'but also'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan bahwa selain A, ada juga B; 'apalagi', 'selain', 'tidak hanya', 'tetapi juga'.","formation":"Sentence A + おまけに  + Sentence B","formationId":"Kalimat A + おまけに + Kalimat B","examples":[{"jp":"彼は遅刻した。おまけに宿題も忘れた。","romaji":"Kare wa chikoku shita. Omake ni shukudai mo wasureta.","en":"He was late. Moreover, he forgot his homework.","id":"Dia terlambat. Apalagi dia lupa pekerjaan rumahnya."},{"jp":"このアパートは狭い。おまけに家賃が高い。","romaji":"Kono apaato wa semai. Omake ni yachin ga takai.","en":"This apartment is small. Besides, the rent is high.","id":"Apartemen ini kecil. Selain itu, harga sewanya tinggi."},{"jp":"彼女は仕事が忙しい。おまけに子供も小さい。","romaji":"Kanojo wa shigoto ga isogashii. Omake ni kodomo mo chiisai.","en":"She is busy with work. Not only that, her children are also small.","id":"Dia sibuk dengan pekerjaan. Tak hanya itu, anak-anaknya juga masih kecil."},{"jp":"昨日は雨が降った。おまけに風も強かった。","romaji":"Kinou wa ame ga futta. Omake ni kaze mo tsuyokatta.","en":"Yesterday it rained. In addition, the wind was strong.","id":"Kemarin hujan. Apalagi anginnya kencang."}]},{"pattern":"A。さて B。(A. Sate B.)","meaning":"Indicates a sudden change or shift in the topic or situation; 'now then', 'well', 'so'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan perubahan atau pergeseran topik atau situasi secara tiba-tiba; 'sekarang', 'baiklah', 'jadi'.","formation":"A + さて + B","formationId":"A + さて + B","examples":[{"jp":"今日の仕事が終わった。さて、これから帰るか。","romaji":"Kyou no shigoto ga owatta. Sate, kore kara kaeru ka.","en":"Today's work is done. Now then, shall we go home?","id":"Pekerjaan hari ini selesai. Kalau begitu, bisakah kita pulang?"},{"jp":"話がちょっと長くなったね。さて、もっと喜美子さんのことを教えてください。","romaji":"Hanashi ga chotto nagaku natta ne. Sate, motto Kimiko-san no koto wo oshiete kudasai.","en":"The conversation got a bit lengthy. Well, please tell me more about Kimiko.","id":"Percakapan menjadi agak panjang. Baiklah, tolong ceritakan lebih banyak tentang Kimiko."},{"jp":"映画を見て楽しかった。さて、何を食べに行こう。","romaji":"Eiga wo mite tanoshikatta. Sate, nani wo tabe ni ikou.","en":"Watching the movie was fun. So, what shall we go eat?","id":"Menonton film itu menyenangkan. Jadi, apa yang akan kita makan?"},{"jp":"マラソンが終わった！さて、少し休んでからシャワーを浴びよう。","romaji":"Marason ga owatta! Sate, sukoshi yasunde kara shawaa wo abiyou.","en":"The marathon is over! Now then, let's rest a bit and then take a shower.","id":"Maraton telah berakhir! Kalau begitu, ayo istirahat sebentar lalu mandi."}]},{"pattern":"A。しかも B。(A. Shikamo B.)","meaning":"Expressing additional information; 'moreover', 'besides', 'furthermore'.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan informasi tambahan; 'apalagi', 'selain', 'selanjutnya'.","formation":"Statement A + 。しかも + Statement B。","formationId":"Pernyataan A + 。しかも + Pernyataan B。","examples":[{"jp":"この料理は美味しいです。しかも、安いです。","romaji":"Kono ryouri wa oishii desu. Shikamo, yasui desu.","en":"This dish is delicious. Moreover, it is cheap.","id":"Hidangan ini enak. Apalagi harganya murah."},{"jp":"彼は優秀な学生です。しかも、スポーツが得意です。","romaji":"Kare wa yuushuu na gakusei desu. Shikamo, supootsu ga tokui desu.","en":"He is an excellent student. Besides, he is good at sports.","id":"Dia adalah murid yang luar biasa. Selain itu, dia pandai olahraga."},{"jp":"彼女は歌が上手です。しかも、ダンスも上手です。","romaji":"Kanojo wa uta ga jouzu desu. Shikamo, dansu mo jouzu desu.","en":"She is good at singing. Furthermore, she is also good at dancing.","id":"Dia pandai menyanyi. Selain itu, dia juga pandai menari."},{"jp":"このカフェは雰囲気がいいです。しかも、コーヒーも美味しいです。","romaji":"Kono kafe wa fun'iki ga ii desu. Shikamo, koohii mo oishii desu.","en":"This cafe has a nice atmosphere. Moreover, the coffee is also delicious.","id":"Kafe ini memiliki suasana yang menyenangkan. Apalagi kopinya juga enak."}]},{"pattern":"A。したがって B。(A. Shitagatte B.)","meaning":"Express a cause-and-effect relationship; 'therefore', 'consequently', 'so'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan hubungan sebab-akibat; 'oleh karena itu', 'akibatnya', 'jadi'.","formation":"A + したがって + B","formationId":"A + したがって + B","examples":[{"jp":"今日は雨が降っています。したがって、傘を持って行きましょう。","romaji":"Kyou wa ame ga futteimasu. Shitagatte, kasa wo motte ikimashou.","en":"It is raining today. Therefore, let's bring an umbrella.","id":"Hari ini hujan. Oleh karena itu, yuk bawa payung."},{"jp":"彼は忙しいです。したがって、彼に連絡するのはやめましょう。","romaji":"Kare wa isogashii desu. Shitagatte, kare ni renraku suru no wa yamemashou.","en":"He is busy. Consequently, let's not contact him.","id":"Dia sedang sibuk. Oleh karena itu, jangan menghubunginya."},{"jp":"そのレストランは人気があります。したがって、予約しないと席がないかもしれません。","romaji":"Sono resutoran wa ninki ga arimasu. Shitagatte, yoyaku shinai to seki ga nai kamoshiremasen.","en":"That restaurant is popular. Therefore, there might be no seats if you don't make a reservation.","id":"Restoran itu populer. Oleh karena itu, mungkin tidak ada kursi jika Anda tidak melakukan reservasi."},{"jp":"試験が近いです。したがって、勉強に集中しましょう。","romaji":"Shiken ga chikai desu. Shitagatte, benkyou ni shuuchuu shimashou.","en":"The exam is coming up soon. Consequently, let's focus on studying.","id":"Ujian akan segera tiba. Oleh karena itu, mari kita fokus belajar."}]},{"pattern":"A すなわち B。","meaning":"Express that A is equivalent to B; 'in other words', 'namely', 'that is to say'.","meaningId":"Nyatakan bahwa A setara dengan B; 'dengan kata lain', 'yaitu', 'artinya'.","formation":"Phrase A + すなわち + Phrase B","formationId":"Frase A + すなわち + Frase B","examples":[{"jp":"私は立派な成果を出したい、すなわち、成功したいのです。","romaji":"Watashi wa rippana seika wo dashitai, sunawachi, seikou shitai no desu.","en":"I want to achieve great results, in other words, I want to succeed.","id":"Saya ingin mencapai hasil yang luar biasa, dengan kata lain saya ingin sukses."},{"jp":"彼は言葉に詰まった、すなわち、何も言えなかった。","romaji":"Kare wa kotoba ni tsumatta, sunawachi, nani mo ienakatta.","en":"He was at a loss for words, that is to say, he couldn't say anything.","id":"Dia kehilangan kata-kata, artinya dia tidak bisa berkata apa-apa."},{"jp":"彼女は自分の目標に向かって努力し続けている、すなわち、彼女は非常に頑張っている。","romaji":"Kanojo wa jibun no mokuhyou ni mukatte doryoku shi tsudzukete iru, sunawachi, kanojo wa hijou ni ganbatte iru.","en":"She keeps working hard towards her goals, namely, she is trying very hard.","id":"Dia terus bekerja keras untuk mencapai tujuannya, yaitu dia berusaha sangat keras."},{"jp":"この店はお客様の満足を一番大事にしています、すなわち、サービスが良いということです。","romaji":"Kono mise wa okyakusama no manzoku o ichiban daiji ni shiteimasu, sunawachi, saabisu ga yoi to iu koto desu.","en":"This store values customer satisfaction above all else, in other words, it has good service.","id":"Toko ini mengutamakan kepuasan pelanggan di atas segalanya, dengan kata lain memiliki pelayanan yang baik."}]},{"pattern":"A。すると B。","meaning":"Indicates that when action A is done, action or event B follows; 'then', 'when', 'if'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan bahwa ketika tindakan A dilakukan, tindakan atau peristiwa B menyusul; 'lalu', 'kapan', 'jika'.","formation":"A (Sentence) + すると + B (Sentence)","formationId":"A (Kalimat) + すると + B (Kalimat)","examples":[{"jp":"電話をかけると、彼女が出ました。","romaji":"Denwa wo kakeru to, kanojo ga demashita.","en":"When I made the phone call, she answered.","id":"Ketika saya menelepon, dia menjawab."},{"jp":"このボタンを押すと、ドアが開きます。","romaji":"Kono botan wo osu to, doa ga hirakimasu.","en":"If you press this button, the door will open.","id":"Jika Anda menekan tombol ini, pintu akan terbuka."},{"jp":"コンビニに行くと、たまたま友達に会いました。","romaji":"Konbini ni iku to, tamatama tomodachi ni aimashita.","en":"When I went to the convenience store, I happened to meet my friend.","id":"Ketika saya pergi ke toko serba ada, saya kebetulan bertemu dengan teman saya."},{"jp":"彼が家を出ると、すぐに雨が降り始めました。","romaji":"Kare ga ie wo deru to, sugu ni ame ga furihajimemashita.","en":"As soon as he left the house, it started to rain.","id":"Begitu dia meninggalkan rumah, hujan mulai turun."}]},{"pattern":"A。そういえば B。","meaning":"Recalling something related to A; 'speaking of which', 'by the way', 'now that you mention it'.","meaningId":"Mengingat sesuatu yang berhubungan dengan A; 'ngomong-ngomong', 'ngomong-ngomong', 'sekarang kamu menyebutkannya'.","formation":"A + そういえば + B","formationId":"A + そういえば + B","examples":[{"jp":"映画。そういえば、彼は映画館で働いているんだ。","romaji":"Eiga. Souieba, kare wa eigakan de hataraite irun da.","en":"Movies. Speaking of which, he works at a movie theater.","id":"Film. Omong-omong, dia bekerja di bioskop."},{"jp":"山田さん。そういえば、彼女は今週末旅行しています。","romaji":"Yamada-san. Souieba, kanojo wa konshuumatsu ryokou shite imasu.","en":"Ms. Yamada. By the way, she is traveling this weekend.","id":"Nona Yamada. Ngomong-ngomong, dia bepergian akhir pekan ini."},{"jp":"そのレストラン。そういえば、次の週末そこでパーティーがあるんだ。","romaji":"Sono resutoran. Souieba, tsugi no shuumatsu soko de paatii ga arun da.","en":"That restaurant. Now that you mention it, there's a party there next weekend.","id":"Restoran itu. Sekarang setelah Anda menyebutkannya, ada pesta di sana akhir pekan depan."},{"jp":"寒い。そういえば、明日雪が降るらしいよ。","romaji":"Samui. Souieba, ashita yuki ga furu rashii yo.","en":"It's cold. Speaking of which, it seems like it will snow tomorrow.","id":"Ini dingin. Omong-omong, sepertinya besok akan turun salju."}]},{"pattern":"A。そこで B。","meaning":"Expresses 'therefore' or 'because of that'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan 'karena itu' atau 'karena itu'.","formation":"A + そこで + B","formationId":"A + そこで + B","examples":[{"jp":"明日は試験があります。そこで今晩勉強しようと思います。","romaji":"Ashita wa shiken ga arimasu. Soko de konban benkyou shiyou to omoimasu.","en":"There is an exam tomorrow. Therefore, I plan to study tonight.","id":"Besok ada ujian. Oleh karena itu, saya berencana untuk belajar malam ini."},{"jp":"このレストランは混んでいます。そこで別の場所でランチを食べましょう。","romaji":"Kono resutoran wa kondeimasu. Soko de betsu no basho de ranchi wo tabemashou.","en":"This restaurant is crowded. Therefore, let's eat lunch at a different place.","id":"Restoran ini ramai. Oleh karena itu, ayo makan siang di tempat yang berbeda."},{"jp":"彼女はアレルギーがある。そこで彼女のために別の料理を作ります。","romaji":"Kanojo wa arerugii ga aru. Soko de kanojo no tame ni betsu no ryouri wo tsukurimasu.","en":"She has an allergy. Therefore, I'll cook a different dish for her.","id":"Dia memiliki alergi. Oleh karena itu, saya akan memasak hidangan berbeda untuknya."},{"jp":"傘を持っていない。そこで雨が止むまで待ちます。","romaji":"Kasa wo motte inai. Soko de ame ga yamu made machimasu.","en":"I don't have an umbrella. Therefore, I'll wait until the rain stops.","id":"Saya tidak punya payung. Oleh karena itu, saya akan menunggu sampai hujan berhenti."}]},{"pattern":"A。それがB。","meaning":"Expressing 'that's exactly what A is; in other words, B'.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan 'itulah tepatnya A; dengan kata lain, B'.","formation":"A (Statement)。それが B (Restatement or explanation of A)。","formationId":"A (Pernyataan)。それが B (Pernyataan kembali atau penjelasan A)。","examples":[{"jp":"彼は勉強ができる。それが天才というものだ。","romaji":"Kare wa benkyou ga dekiru. Sore ga tensai to iu mono da.","en":"He can study well. That's what you call a genius.","id":"Dia bisa belajar dengan baik. Itulah yang disebut jenius."},{"jp":"美味しい料理を作る。それが私の趣味なんです。","romaji":"Oishii ryouri wo tsukuru. Sore ga watashi no shumi nan desu.","en":"I make delicious food. That's my hobby.","id":"Saya membuat makanan lezat. Itu hobiku."},{"jp":"彼女は私を助けてくれる。それが友達というものだ。","romaji":"Kanojo wa watashi wo tasukete kureru. Sore ga tomodachi to iu mono da.","en":"She helps me. That's what a friend is.","id":"Dia membantuku. Itulah arti seorang teman."},{"jp":"一人で長い旅をする。それが自由というものだ。","romaji":"Hitori de nagai tabi wo suru. Sore ga jiyuu to iu mono da.","en":"Traveling alone for a long time. That's what freedom is.","id":"Bepergian sendirian untuk waktu yang lama. Itulah kebebasan."}]},{"pattern":"A。それで B。","meaning":"Express a sequence of events or cause-and-effect; 'and then', 'so', 'because of that'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan rangkaian peristiwa atau sebab-akibat; 'dan kemudian', 'jadi', 'karena itu'.","formation":"Sentence A +。それで+ Sentence B。","formationId":"Kalimat A + 。それで+ Kalimat B。","examples":[{"jp":"昨日は雨が降っていた。それで公園に行かなかった。","romaji":"Kinou wa ame ga futte ita. Sore de kouen ni ikanakatta.","en":"It was raining yesterday. So, I didn't go to the park.","id":"Kemarin hujan. Jadi, aku tidak pergi ke taman."},{"jp":"試験に落ちた。それで再試験を受けなければならない。","romaji":"Shiken ni ochita. Sore de sai shiken wo ukenakereba naranai.","en":"I failed the exam. So, I have to take a re-exam.","id":"Saya gagal dalam ujian. Jadi, saya harus mengikuti ujian ulang."},{"jp":"部屋が寒かった。それで暖房をつけた。","romaji":"Heya ga samukatta. Sore de danbou wo tsuketa.","en":"The room was cold. So, I turned on the heater.","id":"Ruangan itu dingin. Jadi, saya menyalakan pemanasnya."},{"jp":"今日は休みだ。それで映画を見に行く。","romaji":"Kyou wa yasumi da. Sore de eiga wo mi ni iku.","en":"Today is a holiday. So, I'm going to watch a movie.","id":"Hari ini adalah hari libur. Jadi, aku akan menonton film."}]},{"pattern":"A。それでも B。","meaning":"Expresses 'even so', 'nevertheless', 'still', or 'but'; used to contrast two statements.","meaningId":"Menyatakan 'meski begitu', 'meskipun demikian', 'masih', atau 'tetapi'; digunakan untuk membedakan dua pernyataan.","formation":"A (situation) + 。それでも + B (action or thought)","formationId":"A (situasi) + 。それでも + B (tindakan atau pikiran)","examples":[{"jp":"今日は日曜日です。それでも、仕事に行かなければなりません。","romaji":"Kyou wa nichiyoubi desu. Sore demo, shigoto ni ikanakereba narimasen.","en":"Today is Sunday. Nevertheless, I have to go to work.","id":"Hari ini Minggu. Meski begitu, aku harus berangkat kerja."},{"jp":"彼は若いです。それでも、経験が豊富です。","romaji":"Kare wa wakai desu. Sore demo, keiken ga houfu desu.","en":"He is young. Even so, he has a lot of experience.","id":"Dia masih muda. Meski begitu, dia punya banyak pengalaman."},{"jp":"雨が降っています。それでも、散歩に行きたいです。","romaji":"Ame ga futteimasu. Sore demo, sanpo ni ikitai desu.","en":"It's raining. Still, I want to go for a walk.","id":"Sedang hujan. Tetap saja, aku ingin jalan-jalan."},{"jp":"試験の結果が悪かったです。それでも、諦めません。","romaji":"Shiken no kekka ga warukatta desu. Sore demo, akiramenai.","en":"The exam results were bad. But I won't give up.","id":"Hasil ujiannya buruk. Tapi saya tidak akan menyerah."}]},{"pattern":"A。それなのに B。","meaning":"Express contrast or a contradiction between two situations or facts; 'even though', 'despite', 'but still'.","meaningId":"Mengungkapkan kontras atau kontradiksi antara dua situasi atau fakta; 'walaupun', 'walaupun', 'tapi tetap saja'.","formation":"A。それなのに B。","formationId":"A。それなのに B。","examples":[{"jp":"彼は頭がいい。それなのに、試験に落ちた。","romaji":"Kare wa atama ga ii. Sore nanoni, shiken ni ochita.","en":"He is smart. Despite that, he failed the exam.","id":"Dia pintar. Meski begitu, dia gagal dalam ujian."},{"jp":"私は早く起きた。それなのに、バスに遅れた。","romaji":"Watashi wa hayaku okita. Sore nanoni, basu ni okureta.","en":"I woke up early. Even so, I was late for the bus.","id":"Saya bangun pagi-pagi. Meski begitu, aku terlambat ke bus."},{"jp":"昨日は晴れていた。それなのに、彼は傘を持っていた。","romaji":"Kinou wa harete ita. Sore nanoni, kare wa kasa wo motte ita.","en":"It was sunny yesterday. Despite that, he had an umbrella.","id":"Kemarin cerah. Meski begitu, dia punya payung."},{"jp":"彼女は運動が苦手だ。それなのに、マラソンを走ることにした。","romaji":"Kanojo wa undou ga nigate da. Sore nanoni, marason wo hashiru koto ni shita.","en":"She is not good at sports. Nevertheless, she decided to run a marathon.","id":"Dia tidak pandai olahraga. Meski begitu, dia memutuskan untuk lari maraton."}]},{"pattern":"A。それなら B。(A. Sore nara B.)","meaning":"Express 'if that's the case, then'; used to show a logical consequence or decision based on a given situation.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan 'jika itu masalahnya, maka'; digunakan untuk menunjukkan konsekuensi atau keputusan logis berdasarkan situasi tertentu.","formation":"Situation A (sentence) + 。それなら + Situation B (sentence)","formationId":"Situasi A (kalimat) + 。それなら + Situasi B (kalimat)","examples":[{"jp":"試験が近い。それなら、もっと勉強しなければならない。","romaji":"Shiken ga chikai. Sore nara, motto benkyou shinakereba naranai.","en":"The exam is coming soon. If that's the case, I must study more.","id":"Ujian akan segera datang. Jika itu masalahnya, saya harus belajar lebih banyak."},{"jp":"明日は雨が降るだろう。それなら、傘を持って行こう。","romaji":"Ashita wa ame ga furudarou. Sore nara, kasa wo motte ikou.","en":"It will probably rain tomorrow. In that case, let's bring an umbrella.","id":"Mungkin besok akan turun hujan. Kalau begitu, ayo bawa payung."},{"jp":"彼らはもう帰った。それなら、私も帰ろう。","romaji":"Karera wa mou kaetta. Sore nara, watashi mo kaerou.","en":"They have already left. If that's the case, I'll go home too.","id":"Mereka sudah pergi. Jika itu masalahnya, aku akan pulang juga."},{"jp":"あのレストランは予約がいっぱいだ。それなら、別の場所を探そう。","romaji":"Ano resutoran wa yoyaku ga ippai da. Sore nara, betsu no basho wo sagasou.","en":"Reservations at that restaurant are full. In that case, let's find another place.","id":"Reservasi di restoran itu sudah penuh. Kalau begitu, ayo cari tempat lain."}]},{"pattern":"A それはそうと B。","meaning":"Changing the topic; 'by the way', 'speaking of which'.","meaningId":"Mengubah topik; 'Ngomong-ngomong', 'ngomong-ngomong'.","formation":"Sentence A + それはそうと + Sentence B","formationId":"Kalimat A + それはそうと + Kalimat B","examples":[{"jp":"それはそうと、今日の天気はいいですね。","romaji":"Sore wa sou to, kyou no tenki wa ii desu ne.","en":"By the way, the weather is nice today, isn't it?","id":"Ngomong-ngomong, cuacanya bagus hari ini, bukan?"},{"jp":"映画は面白かったです。それはそうと、この店のラーメンはおいしいですよ。","romaji":"Eiga wa omoshirokatta desu. Sore wa sou to, kono mise no raamen wa oishii desu yo.","en":"The movie was interesting. Speaking of which, this restaurant's ramen is delicious.","id":"Filmnya menarik. Ngomong-ngomong, ramen di restoran ini enak."},{"jp":"明日から夏休みですね。それはそうと、新しいカフェがオープンしたみたいです。","romaji":"Ashita kara natsu yasumi desu ne. Sore wa sou to, atarashii kafe ga oopun shita mitai desu.","en":"Summer vacation starts tomorrow, huh? By the way, it seems a new cafe has opened.","id":"Liburan musim panas dimulai besok, ya? Ngomong-ngomong, sepertinya kafe baru sudah dibuka."},{"jp":"昨日の試験は難しかった。それはそうと、週末にパーティーがあるのを知ってますか？","romaji":"Kinou no shiken wa muzukashikatta. Sore wa sou to, shuumatsu ni paatii ga aru no wo shitte masu ka?","en":"Yesterday's exam was difficult. Speaking of which, do you know there's a party this weekend?","id":"Ujian kemarin sulit. Ngomong-ngomong, tahukah kamu ada pesta akhir pekan ini?"}]},{"pattern":"A。だが B。","meaning":"Expresses contrasting ideas or statements; 'but', 'however'.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan ide atau pernyataan yang kontras; 'tapi', 'namun'.","formation":"Sentence A + だが + Sentence B","formationId":"Kalimat A + だが + Kalimat B","examples":[{"jp":"このレストランは値段が高い。だが、味はとてもいい。","romaji":"Kono resutoran wa nedan ga takai. Daga, aji wa totemo ii.","en":"This restaurant is expensive. But, the taste is very good.","id":"Restoran ini mahal. Tapi, rasanya sangat enak."},{"jp":"彼は疲れている。だが、仕事を終わらせるまで休まない。","romaji":"Kare wa tsukarete iru. Daga, shigoto o owaraseru made yasumanai.","en":"He is tired. However, he will not rest until he finishes work.","id":"Dia lelah. Namun, dia tidak akan beristirahat sampai pekerjaannya selesai."},{"jp":"昨日は寒かった。だが、今日は暖かい。","romaji":"Kinou wa samukatta. Daga, kyou wa atatakai.","en":"Yesterday was cold. But, today is warm.","id":"Kemarin dingin. Tapi, hari ini hangat."},{"jp":"彼女は外見は地味だ。だが、性格が素晴らしい。","romaji":"Kanojo wa gaiken wa jimi da. Daga, seikaku ga subarashii.","en":"Her appearance is plain. However, she has a wonderful personality.","id":"Penampilannya polos. Namun, dia memiliki kepribadian yang luar biasa."}]},{"pattern":"A。ただB。","meaning":"Express contrast between two situations; 'although', 'but', 'however'.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan kontras antara dua situasi; 'walaupun', 'tetapi', 'namun'.","formation":"Sentence A + ただ + Sentence B","formationId":"Kalimat A + ただ + Kalimat B","examples":[{"jp":"彼は頭がいい。ただ、努力はあまりしない。","romaji":"Kare wa atama ga ii. Tada, doryoku wa amari shinai.","en":"He is smart; however, he doesn't make much effort.","id":"Dia pintar; Namun, dia tidak berusaha banyak."},{"jp":"外は雨が降っている。ただ、家にいると暇だ。","romaji":"Soto wa ame ga futte iru. Tada, ie ni iru to hima da.","en":"It's raining outside, but I'm bored at home.","id":"Di luar hujan, tapi aku bosan di rumah."},{"jp":"そのレストランは値段が高い。ただ、サービスが良い。","romaji":"Sono resutoran wa nedan ga takai. Tada, saabisu ga yoi.","en":"That restaurant is expensive; however, the service is good.","id":"Restoran itu mahal; namun, layanannya bagus."},{"jp":"テストの結果は良くなかった。ただ、やり直すチャンスがある。","romaji":"Tesuto no kekka wa yokunakatta. Tada, yarinaosu chansu ga aru.","en":"The test results were not good, but there's a chance to retake it.","id":"Hasil tesnya kurang bagus, tapi ada peluang untuk mengulangnya."}]},{"pattern":"A。ただしB。 (A. Tadashi B)","meaning":"Adding a condition or exception to a statement; 'however', 'provided that', 'but only if'.","meaningId":"Menambahkan kondisi atau pengecualian pada pernyataan; 'namun', 'asalkan', 'tetapi hanya jika'.","formation":"Statement A + ただし + Condition B","formationId":"Pernyataan A + ただし + Kondisi B","examples":[{"jp":"この部屋を使ってもいいです。ただし、使った後で掃除してください。","romaji":"Kono heya wo tsukatte mo ii desu. Tadashi, tsukatta ato de souji shite kudasai.","en":"You can use this room. However, please clean up after you use it.","id":"Anda dapat menggunakan ruangan ini. Namun, harap bersihkan setelah Anda menggunakannya."},{"jp":"明日から出張で不在になります。ただし、緊急の場合は携帯に連絡してください。","romaji":"Ashita kara shucchou de fuzai ni narimasu. Tadashi, kinkyuu no baai wa keitai ni renraku shite kudasai.","en":"I'll be away on a business trip starting tomorrow. However, in case of emergency, please contact me on my cell phone.","id":"Saya akan pergi dalam perjalanan bisnis mulai besok. Namun, jika terjadi keadaan darurat, harap hubungi saya melalui ponsel saya."},{"jp":"食事代は全額会社が負担します。ただし、アルコールのみ自己負担となります。","romaji":"Shokuji dai wa zengaku kaisha ga futan shimasu. Tadashi, arukooru nomi jiko futan to narimasu.","en":"The company will cover the entire meal cost. However, alcohol expenses will be borne by the individual.","id":"Perusahaan akan menanggung seluruh biaya makan. Namun, biaya alkohol akan ditanggung oleh individu."},{"jp":"図書館で本を借りることができます。ただし、期限内に返さなければなりません。","romaji":"Toshokan de hon wo kariru koto ga dekimasu. Tadashi, kigen nai ni kaesanakereba narimasen.","en":"You can borrow books from the library. However, you must return them within the deadline.","id":"Anda dapat meminjam buku dari perpustakaan. Namun, Anda harus mengembalikannya dalam batas waktu yang ditentukan."}]},{"pattern":"A。だって B。","meaning":"Used to give a reason, express cause or bring up a topic; 'because', 'since', 'it's just that'.","meaningId":"Digunakan untuk memberi alasan, mengungkapkan penyebab atau mengangkat suatu topik; 'karena', 'sejak', 'hanya saja'.","formation":"Verb-casual + だって、い-Adjective + だって、な-Adjective + だって、Noun + だって","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + だって、い-Kata Sifat + だって、な-Kata Sifat + だって、Kata Benda + だって","examples":[{"jp":"暇だって、映画を見に行こうよ。","romaji":"Hima datte, eiga wo mi ni ikou yo.","en":"Since we are free, let's go watch a movie.","id":"Karena kita punya waktu luang, ayo kita menonton film."},{"jp":"寒いだって、コートを着てください。","romaji":"Samui datte, ko-to wo kite kudasai.","en":"Because it's cold, please wear a coat.","id":"Karena dingin, mohon pakai mantel."},{"jp":"疲れているだって、休んだほうがいい。","romaji":"Tsukarete iru datte, yasunda hou ga ii.","en":"Since you're tired, it's better to rest.","id":"Karena kamu lelah, lebih baik istirahat."},{"jp":"彼女が料理上手だって、みんな彼女の作った料理を楽しみにしています。","romaji":"Kanojo ga ryouri jouzu datte, minna kanojo no tsukutta ryouri wo tanoshimi ni shiteimasu.","en":"Because she is good at cooking, everyone is looking forward to her dishes.","id":"Karena dia pandai memasak, semua orang menantikan masakannya."}]},{"pattern":"A。ちなみに B。(A. Chinamini B.)","meaning":"Used to give additional information about the topic; 'by the way', 'incidentally'.","meaningId":"Digunakan untuk memberikan informasi tambahan tentang topik; 'ngomong-ngomong', 'kebetulan'.","formation":"A。ちなみに B。","formationId":"A。ちなみに B。","examples":[{"jp":"今日は授業がありません。ちなみに、明日も休みです。","romaji":"Kyou wa jugyou ga arimasen. Chinamini, asu mo yasumi desu.","en":"There's no class today. By the way, tomorrow is also a day off.","id":"Tidak ada kelas hari ini. Ngomong-ngomong, besok juga merupakan hari libur."},{"jp":"この店のラーメンは美味しいです。ちなみに、餃子もおすすめです。","romaji":"Kono mise no ramen wa oishii desu. Chinamini, gyoza mo osusume desu.","en":"The ramen at this shop is delicious. By the way, their gyoza is also recommended.","id":"Ramen di toko ini enak. Ngomong-ngomong, gyoza mereka juga direkomendasikan."},{"jp":"彼は今日は遅刻しました。ちなみに、昨日は欠席しました。","romaji":"Kare wa kyou wa chikoku shimashita. Chinamini, kinou wa kesseki shimashita.","en":"He was late today. By the way, he was absent yesterday.","id":"Dia terlambat hari ini. Ngomong-ngomong, dia absen kemarin."},{"jp":"映画は面白かったです。ちなみに、原作の方がもっといいですよ。","romaji":"Eiga wa omoshirokatta desu. Chinamini, gensaku no hou ga motto ii desu yo.","en":"The movie was interesting. By the way, the original work is even better.","id":"Filmnya menarik. Ngomong-ngomong, karya aslinya bahkan lebih bagus."}]},{"pattern":"A。ということは B。 (A. To iu koto wa B.)","meaning":"Expresses the meaning 'if A, that means B' or 'A implies B'.","meaningId":"Mengungkapkan arti 'jika A, itu berarti B' atau 'A menyiratkan B'.","formation":"A + ということは + B","formationId":"A + ということは + B","examples":[{"jp":"彼女が泣いている。ということは何か悲しいことがあったに違いない。","romaji":"Kanojo ga naite iru. To iu koto wa nanika kanashii koto ga atta ni chigainai.","en":"She is crying. That means something sad must have happened.","id":"Dia menangis. Itu berarti sesuatu yang menyedihkan pasti telah terjadi."},{"jp":"このケーキが残っている。ということは、みんなお腹がいっぱいだったのかな。","romaji":"Kono keeki ga nokotte iru. To iu koto wa, minna onaka ga ippai datta no ka na.","en":"This cake is left over. That means everyone must have been full, I guess.","id":"Kue ini tersisa. Itu artinya semua orang pasti sudah kenyang, kurasa."},{"jp":"道が渋滞している。ということは、事故があったのかもしれない。","romaji":"Michi ga juutai shite iru. To iu koto wa, jiko ga atta no kamoshirenai.","en":"The road is congested. That means there might have been an accident.","id":"Jalanan macet. Artinya mungkin saja terjadi kecelakaan."},{"jp":"彼が試験に受かった。ということは、勉強がたくさん頑張ったんだね。","romaji":"Kare ga shiken ni ukatta. To iu koto wa, benkyou ga takusan ganbattan da ne.","en":"He passed the exam. That means he must have studied really hard.","id":"Dia lulus ujian. Itu artinya dia pasti belajar dengan giat."}]},{"pattern":"A。というのは B。","meaning":"Used to give an explanation or provide additional information for A; 'that is to say', 'in other words'.","meaningId":"Digunakan untuk memberikan penjelasan atau memberikan informasi tambahan bagi A; 'artinya', 'dengan kata lain'.","formation":"[Statement A]。というのは、[Statement B]。","formationId":"[Pernyataan A]。というのは、[Pernyataan B]。","examples":[{"jp":"彼は非常に疲れています。というのは、昨夜、車で遠くまで行ってきたためです。","romaji":"Kare wa hijou ni tsukareteimasu. To iu no wa, sakuya, kuruma de tooku made itte kita tame desu.","en":"He is very tired. That is to say, because he went far by car last night.","id":"Dia sangat lelah. Artinya, karena dia pergi jauh dengan mobil tadi malam."},{"jp":"このレストランはおすすめです。というのは、料理が美味しいし、雰囲気もいいからです。","romaji":"Kono resutoran wa osusume desu. To iu no wa, ryouri ga oishii shi, fun'iki mo ii kara desu.","en":"I recommend this restaurant. That is to say, because the food is delicious and the atmosphere is nice.","id":"Saya merekomendasikan restoran ini. Artinya, karena makanannya enak dan suasananya menyenangkan."},{"jp":"試験に落ちた。というのは、十分に勉強しなかったからです。","romaji":"Shiken ni ochita. To iu no wa, juubun ni benkyou shinakatta kara desu.","en":"I failed the exam. In other words, because I didn't study enough.","id":"Saya gagal dalam ujian. Dengan kata lain, karena saya kurang belajar."},{"jp":"彼女は独特な趣味がある。というのは、昆虫収集だ。","romaji":"Kanojo wa dokutoku na shumi ga aru. To iu no wa, konchuu shuushuu da.","en":"She has a unique hobby. Namely, insect collecting.","id":"Dia memiliki hobi yang unik. Yakni pengumpulan serangga."}]},{"pattern":"A。なおB。(A. Nao B.)","meaning":"Provides additional information; 'moreover', 'besides', 'in addition'.","meaningId":"Memberikan informasi tambahan; 'selain itu', 'di samping', 'di samping itu'.","formation":"A (sentence) + なお + B (sentence)","formationId":"A (kalimat) + なお + B (kalimat)","examples":[{"jp":"明日は休みです。なお、月曜日も休みです。","romaji":"Ashita wa yasumi desu. Nao, getsuyoubi mo yasumi desu.","en":"Tomorrow is a holiday. Moreover, Monday is also a holiday.","id":"Besok adalah hari libur. Apalagi hari Senin juga merupakan hari libur."},{"jp":"彼は頭が良いです。なお、スポーツも得意です。","romaji":"Kare wa atama ga yoi desu. Nao, supootsu mo tokui desu.","en":"He is smart. Besides, he is also good at sports.","id":"Dia pintar. Selain itu, dia juga pandai dalam olahraga."},{"jp":"この本は面白いです。なお、安いです。","romaji":"Kono hon wa omoshiroi desu. Nao, yasui desu.","en":"This book is interesting. In addition, it is cheap.","id":"Buku ini menarik. Selain itu, harganya murah."},{"jp":"私は日本語を勉強しています。なお、韓国語も勉強しています。","romaji":"Watashi wa nihongo wo benkyou shiteimasu. Nao, kankokugo mo benkyou shiteimasu.","en":"I am studying Japanese. Moreover, I am also studying Korean.","id":"Saya sedang belajar bahasa Jepang. Selain itu, saya juga belajar bahasa Korea."}]},{"pattern":"A。もっとも B。","meaning":"Express contrasting opinions or facts; 'although', 'but', 'however'.","meaningId":"Mengungkapkan pendapat atau fakta yang kontras; 'walaupun', 'tetapi', 'namun'.","formation":"Clause A + もっとも + Clause B","formationId":"Klausul A + もっとも + Klausul B","examples":[{"jp":"彼は頭がいい。もっとも、勉強も大切だ。","romaji":"Kare wa atama ga ii. Mottomo, benkyou mo taisetsu da.","en":"He is smart. However, studying is also important.","id":"Dia pintar. Namun, belajar juga penting."},{"jp":"このレストランは美味しい。もっとも、値段が高い。","romaji":"Kono resutoran wa oishii. Mottomo, nedan ga takai.","en":"This restaurant is delicious. But, the prices are high.","id":"Restoran ini enak. Tapi, harganya tinggi."},{"jp":"彼女は綺麗だ。もっとも、性格が悪い。","romaji":"Kanojo wa kirei da. Mottomo, seikaku ga warui.","en":"She is beautiful. Although, her personality is bad.","id":"Dia cantik. Meski begitu, kepribadiannya buruk."},{"jp":"日本は面白い国だ。もっとも、住むのが大変そうだ。","romaji":"Nihon wa omoshiroi kuni da. Mottomo, sumu no ga taihen sou da.","en":"Japan is an interesting country. But, it seems difficult to live in.","id":"Jepang adalah negara yang menarik. Namun, tampaknya sulit untuk hidup di dalamnya."}]},{"pattern":"A。要するに B。(A. Yousuru ni B.)","meaning":"Expressing 'in short', 'in a nutshell', or 'to sum up' when restating or summarizing A as B.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan 'singkatnya', 'singkatnya', atau 'ringkasannya' ketika menyatakan kembali atau meringkas A sebagai B.","formation":"A。要するに B。","formationId":"A。要するに B。","examples":[{"jp":"このプロジェクトは成功しました。要するに、私たちのチームは素晴らしい仕事をしました。","romaji":"Kono purojekuto wa seikou shimashita. Yousuru ni, watashitachi no chiimu wa subarashii shigoto o shimashita.","en":"This project was successful. In short, our team did a great job.","id":"Proyek ini berhasil. Singkatnya, tim kami melakukan pekerjaan dengan baik."},{"jp":"彼は料理が上手です。要するに、彼は優れたシェフです。","romaji":"Kare wa ryouri ga jouzu desu. Yousuru ni, kare wa sugureta shefu desu.","en":"He is good at cooking. In a nutshell, he is an excellent chef.","id":"Dia pandai memasak. Singkatnya, dia adalah koki yang hebat."},{"jp":"昨日はとても忙しかった。要するに、一日中働いていました。","romaji":"Kinou wa totemo isogashikatta. Yousuru ni, ichinichijuu hataraite imashita.","en":"Yesterday was very busy. To sum up, I was working all day.","id":"Kemarin sangat sibuk. Singkatnya, saya bekerja sepanjang hari."},{"jp":"彼女は新しい仕事が好きです。要するに、彼女は満足しています。","romaji":"Kanojo wa atarashii shigoto ga suki desu. Yousuru ni, kanojo wa manzoku shiteimasu.","en":"She likes her new job. In short, she is satisfied.","id":"Dia menyukai pekerjaan barunya. Singkatnya, dia puas."}]},{"pattern":"Noun につき (〜ni tsuki)","meaning":"Indicates the reason, cause, or condition for something; 'due to', 'regarding', 'per'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan alasan, sebab, atau kondisi sesuatu; 'karena', 'mengenai', 'per'.","formation":"Noun + につき","formationId":"Kata benda + につき","examples":[{"jp":"試験につき、今日は静かにしてください。","romaji":"Shiken ni tsuki, kyou wa shizuka ni shite kudasai.","en":"Due to the exam, please be quiet today.","id":"Karena ada ujian, harap tenang hari ini."},{"jp":"このエリアは工事中につき、通行止めです。","romaji":"Kono eria wa koujichuu ni tsuki, tsuukoudome desu.","en":"The area is closed for passage due to construction.","id":"Area tersebut ditutup untuk lalu lintas karena konstruksi."},{"jp":"博物館は整備中につき、入場料が無料です。","romaji":"Hakubutsukan wa seibichuu ni tsuki, nyuujouryou ga muryou desu.","en":"Due to maintenance, admission to the museum is free.","id":"Karena pemeliharaan, tiket masuk ke museum ini gratis."},{"jp":"商品お一つにつき、1000円の割引があります。","romaji":"Shouhin o hitotsu ni tsuki, sen'en no waribiki ga arimasu.","en":"There is a 1,000 yen discount per item.","id":"Ada diskon 1.000 yen per item."}]},{"pattern":"Noun にて","meaning":"Expresses location or means; 'at', 'in', 'by', 'with'.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan lokasi atau sarana; 'di', 'di', 'oleh', 'dengan'.","formation":"Noun + にて","formationId":"Kata benda + にて","examples":[{"jp":"駅前広場にてイベントが開催されます。","romaji":"Ekimae hiroba nite ibento ga kaisai saremasu.","en":"An event will be held at the station square.","id":"Sebuah acara akan diadakan di alun-alun stasiun."},{"jp":"ホテルにて会議が行われます。","romaji":"Hoteru nite kaigi ga okonawaremasu.","en":"The meeting will take place at the hotel.","id":"Pertemuan akan berlangsung di hotel."},{"jp":"郵便局にて荷物を受け取りました。","romaji":"Yubinkyoku nite nimotsu wo uketorimashita.","en":"I received the package at the post office.","id":"Saya menerima paketnya di kantor pos."},{"jp":"インターネットにて調べたら、答えが見つかりました。","romaji":"Intaanetto nite shirabetara, kotae ga mitsukarimashita.","en":"I searched online and found the answer.","id":"Saya mencari online dan menemukan jawabannya."}]},{"pattern":"Noun の ことだから","meaning":"Used to provide a reason or explanation based on one's knowledge about the noun; 'since', 'because', 'knowing'.","meaningId":"Digunakan untuk memberikan alasan atau penjelasan berdasarkan pengetahuan seseorang tentang kata benda; 'sejak', 'karena', 'mengetahui'.","formation":"Noun + のことだから","formationId":"Kata benda + のことだから","examples":[{"jp":"料理が得意な彼のことだから、美味しい料理を作ってくれるでしょう。","romaji":"Ryouri ga tokui na kare no koto dakara, oishii ryouri wo tsukutte kureru deshou.","en":"Since he’s good at cooking, he’ll probably make delicious food.","id":"Karena dia pandai memasak, dia mungkin akan membuat makanan enak."},{"jp":"いつも遅刻する彼女のことだから、今日も遅れるかもしれない。","romaji":"Itsumo chikoku suru kanojo no koto dakara, kyou mo okureru kamoshirenai.","en":"Because she’s always late, she might be late again today.","id":"Karena dia selalu terlambat, dia mungkin akan terlambat lagi hari ini."},{"jp":"安い店のことだから、たくさん売れるはずだ。","romaji":"Yasui mise no koto dakara, takusan ureru hazu da.","en":"Since it’s a cheap store, it should sell a lot.","id":"Karena ini toko yang murah, seharusnya terjual banyak."},{"jp":"ドラマ好きな彼のことだから、最新のドラマについて話すといいでしょう。","romaji":"Dorama suki na kare no koto dakara, saishin no dorama ni tsuite hanasu to ii deshou.","en":"Knowing he likes dramas, it’d be good to talk about the latest shows.","id":"Mengetahui dia menyukai drama, ada baiknya membicarakan acara terbaru."}]},{"pattern":"Noun を はじめ","meaning":"Meaning 'starting with', 'including', 'not only... but also'.","meaningId":"Artinya 'dimulai dengan', 'termasuk', 'tidak hanya... tetapi juga'.","formation":"Noun + をはじめ","formationId":"Kata benda + をはじめ","examples":[{"jp":"日本料理をはじめ、さまざまな料理がこのレストランで楽しめます。","romaji":"Nihon ryouri wo hajime, samazama na ryouri ga kono resutoran de tanoshimemasu.","en":"You can enjoy various dishes in this restaurant, starting with Japanese cuisine.","id":"Beragam hidangan bisa Anda nikmati di restoran ini, mulai dari masakan Jepang."},{"jp":"彼は絵画をはじめ、彫刻や写真もコレクションしている。","romaji":"Kare wa kaiga wo hajime, choukoku ya shashin mo korekushon shite iru.","en":"He collects not only paintings but also sculptures and photographs.","id":"Ia tidak hanya mengoleksi lukisan, tetapi juga patung dan foto."},{"jp":"京都をはじめ、日本のいくつかの都市で伝統的な祭りが行われている。","romaji":"Kyouto wo hajime, Nihon no ikutsu ka no toshi de dentouteki na matsuri ga okonawarete iru.","en":"Traditional festivals are held in several cities in Japan, including Kyoto.","id":"Festival tradisional diadakan di beberapa kota di Jepang, termasuk Kyoto."},{"jp":"太陽をはじめ、地球や火星などの惑星も太陽系に含まれている。","romaji":"Taiyou wo hajime, chikyuu ya kasei nado no wakusei mo taiyoukei ni fukumarete iru.","en":"Not only the Sun, but also planets such as Earth and Mars are included in the solar system.","id":"Tidak hanya Matahari, planet seperti Bumi dan Mars juga termasuk dalam tata surya."}]},{"pattern":"Noun を はじめとして","meaning":"Expresses 'starting with', 'beginning with', or 'including'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan 'dimulai dengan', 'dimulai dengan', atau 'termasuk'.","formation":"Noun + をはじめとして","formationId":"Kata benda + をはじめとして","examples":[{"jp":"東京をはじめとして、日本にはたくさんの観光スポットがあります。","romaji":"Tōkyō o hajime to shite, Nihon ni wa takusan no kankō supotto ga arimasu.","en":"There are many tourist spots in Japan, starting with Tokyo.","id":"Ada banyak sekali tempat wisata di Jepang, salah satunya Tokyo."},{"jp":"彼は、ピアノをはじめとして、たくさんの楽器を演奏できます。","romaji":"Kare wa, piano o hajime to shite, takusan no gakki o ensō dekimasu.","en":"He can play many instruments, starting with piano.","id":"Dia bisa memainkan banyak alat musik, dimulai dengan piano."},{"jp":"この本は手作りのガーゼマスクをはじめとして、便利な生活アイディアが満載です。","romaji":"Kono hon wa tezukuri no gāze masuku o hajime to shite, benrina seikatsu aidea ga mansai desu.","en":"This book is packed with useful life hacks, including how to make a handmade gauze mask.","id":"Buku ini penuh dengan kiat-kiat bermanfaat, termasuk cara membuat masker kain kasa buatan tangan."},{"jp":"そのショッピングモールには、ZARAをはじめとして、多くのブランドが集まっています。","romaji":"Sono shoppingu mōru ni wa, ZARA o hajime to shite, ōku no burando ga atsumatte imasu.","en":"Many brands, including ZARA, gather in that shopping mall.","id":"Banyak brand, termasuk ZARA, berkumpul di pusat perbelanjaan itu."}]},{"pattern":"Noun を はじめとする Noun","meaning":"Indicates a representative example of a group; 'starting with', 'including', 'such as'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan contoh perwakilan suatu kelompok; 'dimulai dengan', 'termasuk', 'seperti'.","formation":"Noun1 を はじめとする Noun2","formationId":"Kata Benda1 を はじめとする Kata Benda2","examples":[{"jp":"彼はフランス語をはじめとする外国語が話せる。","romaji":"Kare wa furansugo o hajime to suru gaikokugo ga hanaseru.","en":"He can speak foreign languages, starting with French.","id":"Dia bisa berbicara bahasa asing, dimulai dengan bahasa Prancis."},{"jp":"このコンサートには、BTSをはじめとする人気アーティストが出演する予定です。","romaji":"Kono konsāto ni wa, BTS o hajime to suru ninki ātisuto ga shutsuen suru yotei desu.","en":"This concert is scheduled to feature popular artists, including BTS.","id":"Konser ini rencananya akan menampilkan artis-artis populer, termasuk BTS."},{"jp":"彼女は魚をはじめとする海の幸が大好きだ。","romaji":"Kanojo wa sakana o hajime to suru umi no sachi ga daisuki da.","en":"She loves seafood, starting with fish.","id":"Dia menyukai makanan laut, dimulai dengan ikan."},{"jp":"この図書館には、子供向けの本をはじめとするさまざまなジャンルの本があります。","romaji":"Kono toshokan ni wa, kodomomuke no hon o hajime to suru samazama na janru no hon ga arimasu.","en":"This library has various genres of books, including children's books.","id":"Perpustakaan ini memiliki berbagai genre buku, termasuk buku anak-anak."}]},{"pattern":"Noun を めぐって","meaning":"Concerning; with regard to; about","meaningId":"Tentang; dengan memperhatikan; tentang","formation":"Noun + を + めぐって","formationId":"Kata Benda + を + めぐって","examples":[{"jp":"環境問題をめぐって、多くの議論が行われています。","romaji":"Kankyō mondai o megutte, ōku no giron ga okonawarete imasu.","en":"Many discussions are held concerning environmental issues.","id":"Banyak diskusi yang diadakan terkait isu lingkungan hidup."},{"jp":"彼の死をめぐって、いくつかの陰謀説が浮かび上がっている。","romaji":"Kare no shi o megutte, ikutsuka no inbōsetsu ga ukabiagatte iru.","en":"Several conspiracy theories have emerged regarding his death.","id":"Beberapa teori konspirasi bermunculan terkait kematiannya."},{"jp":"昇給をめぐって会社と労働組合が話し合いをしています。","romaji":"Shōkyū o megutte kaisha to rōdō kumiai ga hanashiai o shite imasu.","en":"The company and the labor union are having discussions about pay raises.","id":"Perusahaan dan serikat pekerja sedang berdiskusi mengenai kenaikan gaji."},{"jp":"この映画をめぐって、賛否両論が存在している。","romaji":"Kono eiga o megutte, sanpi ryōron ga sonzai shite iru.","en":"There are both pros and cons regarding this movie.","id":"Ada pro dan kontra mengenai film ini."}]},{"pattern":"Noun を めぐる Noun","meaning":"Indicate a situation or event revolving around a particular noun; 'concerning', 'regarding', 'pertaining to'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan situasi atau peristiwa seputar kata benda tertentu; 'mengenai', 'mengenai', 'berkaitan dengan'.","formation":"Noun1 + を + めぐる + Noun2","formationId":"Kata Benda1 + を + めぐる + Kata Benda2","examples":[{"jp":"この事件をめぐる議論が続いています。","romaji":"Kono jiken o meguru giron ga tsudzuite imasu.","en":"The debate concerning this incident continues.","id":"Perdebatan mengenai kejadian ini terus berlanjut."},{"jp":"環境問題をめぐる国際会議が開かれます。","romaji":"Kankyō mondai o meguru kokusai kaigi ga hirakaremasu.","en":"An international conference regarding environmental issues will be held.","id":"Konferensi internasional mengenai isu lingkungan akan diadakan."},{"jp":"彼の突然の辞任をめぐるうわさが広がっている。","romaji":"Kare no totsuzen no jinin o meguru uwasa ga hirogatte iru.","en":"Rumors are spreading concerning his sudden resignation.","id":"Rumor menyebar mengenai pengunduran dirinya yang tiba-tiba."},{"jp":"映画祭をめぐる活動が多くなっています。","romaji":"Eigashai o meguru katsudō ga ōku natte imasu.","en":"There are increasing activities surrounding the film festival.","id":"Ada peningkatan aktivitas seputar festival film."}]},{"pattern":"Noun を もとに","meaning":"Based on; drawing from; using as a reference.","meaningId":"Berdasarkan; menggambar dari; gunakan sebagai referensi.","formation":"Noun + をもとに","formationId":"Kata benda + をもとに","examples":[{"jp":"この映画は実話をもとに作られました。","romaji":"Kono eiga wa jitsuwa o moto ni tsukuraremashita.","en":"This movie was made based on a true story.","id":"Film ini dibuat berdasarkan kisah nyata."},{"jp":"彼の経験をもとにアドバイスが必要だ。","romaji":"Kare no keiken o moto ni adobaisu ga hitsuyō da.","en":"Advice is needed based on his experience.","id":"Saran diperlukan berdasarkan pengalamannya."},{"jp":"データをもとに分析を行いました。","romaji":"Dēta o moto ni bunseki o okonaimashita.","en":"I performed an analysis based on the data.","id":"Saya melakukan analisis berdasarkan data."},{"jp":"世界中の美術館をもとにコレクションを作りました。","romaji":"Sekaijū no bijutsukan o moto ni korekushon o tsukurimashita.","en":"I created a collection based on art galleries all over the world.","id":"Saya membuat koleksi berdasarkan galeri seni di seluruh dunia."}]},{"pattern":"Noun を もとにして","meaning":"Based on; using; utilizing.","meaningId":"Berdasarkan; menggunakan; memanfaatkan.","formation":"Noun + をもとにして","formationId":"Kata Benda + をもとにして","examples":[{"jp":"彼の意見をもとにして、計画を変更しました。","romaji":"Kare no iken o moto ni shite, keikaku o henkō shimashita.","en":"Based on his opinion, we changed the plan.","id":"Berdasarkan pendapatnya, kami mengubah rencana."},{"jp":"この小説は実話をもとにして書かれています。","romaji":"Kono shōsetsu wa jitsuwa o moto ni shite kakarete imasu.","en":"This novel is written based on a true story.","id":"Novel ini ditulis berdasarkan kisah nyata."},{"jp":"資料をもとにして、レポートを作成しました。","romaji":"Shiryō o moto ni shite, repōto o sakusei shimashita.","en":"I created the report based on the materials.","id":"Saya membuat laporan berdasarkan materi."},{"jp":"過去の成功例をもとにして、新しいプロジェクトを進める予定です。","romaji":"Kako no seikōrei o moto ni shite, atarashii purojekuto o susumeru yotei desu.","en":"We plan to proceed with the new project based on past successful examples.","id":"Kami berencana untuk melanjutkan proyek baru berdasarkan contoh sukses di masa lalu."}]},{"pattern":"Verb ことなく","meaning":"Means 'without doing', 'not doing', or 'without happening'.","meaningId":"Berarti 'tanpa melakukan', 'tidak melakukan', atau 'tanpa terjadi'.","formation":"Verb-stem + ことなく","formationId":"Batang kata kerja + ことなく","examples":[{"jp":"彼女は泣くことなく帰ってしまいました。","romaji":"Kanojo wa naku koto naku kaette shimaimashita.","en":"She went home without crying.","id":"Dia pulang ke rumah tanpa menangis."},{"jp":"彼は注意することなく突然出かけた。","romaji":"Kare wa chūi suru koto naku totsuzen dekaketa.","en":"He suddenly left without giving any warning.","id":"Dia tiba-tiba pergi tanpa memberikan peringatan apapun."},{"jp":"山田さんは誰にも話すことなく会社を辞めました。","romaji":"Yamada-san wa dare ni mo hanasu koto naku kaisha o yamemashita.","en":"Mr. Yamada quit the company without talking to anyone.","id":"Tuan Yamada keluar dari perusahaan tanpa berbicara dengan siapa pun."},{"jp":"２０年間、病気になることなく働いています。","romaji":"Nijūnenkan, byōki ni naru koto naku hataraite imasu.","en":"I have been working for 20 years without getting sick.","id":"Saya telah bekerja selama 20 tahun tanpa sakit."}]},{"pattern":"Verb ないことには Verb ない","meaning":"Express that something cannot be done without meeting a certain condition.","meaningId":"Nyatakan bahwa sesuatu tidak dapat dilakukan tanpa memenuhi syarat tertentu.","formation":"Verb-ない + ことには + Verb-ない","formationId":"Kata Kerja-ない + ことには + Kata Kerja-ない","examples":[{"jp":"薬を飲まないことには、病気が治らない。","romaji":"Kusuri o nomanai koto ni wa, byōki ga naoranai.","en":"Unless you take the medicine, the illness won't get better.","id":"Kecuali Anda meminum obatnya, penyakitnya tidak akan membaik."},{"jp":"この問題によく考えないことには、解決できない。","romaji":"Kono mondai ni yoku kangaenai koto ni wa, kaiketsu dekinai.","en":"Unless you think carefully about this problem, you can't solve it.","id":"Kecuali Anda memikirkan masalah ini dengan hati-hati, Anda tidak dapat menyelesaikannya."},{"jp":"練習をしないことには、スキルが上達しない。","romaji":"Renshū o shinai koto ni wa, sukiru ga jōtatsu shinai.","en":"Unless you practice, your skills won't improve.","id":"Kecuali Anda berlatih, keterampilan Anda tidak akan meningkat."},{"jp":"手続きをしないことには、新しいパスポートがもらえない。","romaji":"Tetsuzuki o shinai koto ni wa, atarashii pasupōto ga moraenai.","en":"Unless you go through the procedures, you can't get a new passport.","id":"Kecuali Anda melalui prosedurnya, Anda tidak bisa mendapatkan paspor baru."}]},{"pattern":"～あげく","meaning":"Expresses the outcome of a series of actions or events; 'in the end', 'finally', 'after'.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan hasil dari serangkaian tindakan atau peristiwa; 'pada akhirnya', 'akhirnya', 'setelah'.","formation":"Verb-た + あげく / Noun + の + あげく","formationId":"Kata Kerja-た + あげく / Kata Benda + の + あげく","examples":[{"jp":"長い時間待ったあげく、電車が来なかった。","romaji":"Nagai jikan matta ageku, densha ga konakatta.","en":"After waiting a long time, in the end, the train didn't come.","id":"Setelah menunggu lama, akhirnya kereta tidak kunjung datang."},{"jp":"いろいろな方法を試したあげく、成功した。","romaji":"Iroiro na hōhō o tameshita ageku, seikō shita.","en":"After trying various methods, I finally succeeded.","id":"Setelah mencoba berbagai cara, akhirnya saya berhasil."},{"jp":"彼は失敗のあげく、会社を辞める決心をした。","romaji":"Kare wa shippai no ageku, kaisha o yameru kesshin o shita.","en":"In the end, after his failures, he decided to quit the company.","id":"Pada akhirnya, setelah kegagalannya, dia memutuskan untuk keluar dari perusahaan."},{"jp":"彼女は長い間悩んだあげく、その仕事を断った。","romaji":"Kanojo wa nagai aida nayanda ageku, sono shigoto o kotowatta.","en":"After worrying for a long time, she finally turned down the job.","id":"Setelah lama khawatir, dia akhirnya menolak pekerjaan itu."}]},{"pattern":"～あまり (〜amari)","meaning":"Expresses the result of doing something excessively or beyond a certain point.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan akibat melakukan sesuatu secara berlebihan atau melampaui titik tertentu.","formation":"Verb-ます stem + あまり, い-Adjective + あまり, な-Adjective + のあまり, Noun + のあまり","formationId":"Kata Kerja-ます batang + あまり, い-Kata Sifat + あまり, な-Kata Sifat + のあまり, Kata Benda + のあまり","examples":[{"jp":"昨日は疲れすぎたあまり、朝まで眠り続けました。","romaji":"Kinō wa tsukare-sugita amari, asa made nemuri tsuzukemashita.","en":"Yesterday, I was so tired that I slept until morning.","id":"Kemarin, saya sangat lelah sehingga saya tidur sampai pagi."},{"jp":"彼女はうれしいあまり、泣き出してしまった。","romaji":"Kanojo wa ureshii amari, nakidashite shimatta.","en":"She was so happy that she ended up crying.","id":"Dia sangat senang sampai akhirnya menangis."},{"jp":"彼は安全を確認するあまり、何回もドアをチェックしている。","romaji":"Kare wa anzen o kakunin suru amari, nankai mo doa o chekku shite iru.","en":"He is so concerned about safety that he checks the door many times.","id":"Dia sangat memperhatikan keselamatan sehingga dia memeriksa pintu berkali-kali."},{"jp":"寒さのあまり、彼は震えが止まらなかった。","romaji":"Samusa no amari, kare wa furue ga tomaranakatta.","en":"It was so cold that he couldn't stop shivering.","id":"Itu sangat dingin sehingga dia tidak bisa berhenti menggigil."}]},{"pattern":"～うちに (〜uchi ni)","meaning":"Expresses doing something while a certain condition still holds; 'while', 'before', 'as long as'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan melakukan sesuatu selagi kondisi tertentu masih berlaku; 'sementara', 'sebelum', 'selama'.","formation":"Verb-casual + うちに, い-Adjective + うちに, な-Adjective + なうちに, Noun + のうちに","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + うちに, い-Kata Sifat + うちに, な-Kata Sifat + なうちに, Kata Benda + のうちに","examples":[{"jp":"元気なうちに、旅行を楽しんでください。","romaji":"Genki na uchi ni, ryokō o tanoshinde kudasai.","en":"Enjoy traveling while you are healthy.","id":"Nikmati perjalanan selagi Anda sehat."},{"jp":"若いうちに、いろいろなことを学ぶべきだ。","romaji":"Wakai uchi ni, iroiro na koto o manabu beki da.","en":"One should learn various things while they are young.","id":"Seseorang harus mempelajari berbagai hal ketika mereka masih muda."},{"jp":"子供が寝ているうちに、夕食の準備をしましょう。","romaji":"Kodomo ga nete iru uchi ni, yūshoku no junbi o shimashō.","en":"Let's prepare dinner while the kids are sleeping.","id":"Ayo siapkan makan malam selagi anak-anak tidur."},{"jp":"雨が降らないうちに、家に帰りましょう。","romaji":"Ame ga furanai uchi ni, ie ni kaerimashō.","en":"Let's go home before it starts raining.","id":"Ayo pulang sebelum hujan mulai turun."}]},{"pattern":"～がい (〜gai)","meaning":"Expresses 'worth doing' for verbs.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan 'layak dilakukan' untuk kata kerja.","formation":"Verb-stem + がい","formationId":"Batang kata kerja + がい","examples":[{"jp":"この本は読みがいがあります。","romaji":"Kono hon wa yomi-gai ga arimasu.","en":"This book is worth reading.","id":"Buku ini layak dibaca."},{"jp":"早起きしがいがあると思いますよ。","romaji":"Hayaoki shigai ga aru to omoimasu yo.","en":"I think it's worth waking up early.","id":"Saya pikir ada baiknya bangun pagi."},{"jp":"長い時間をかけがいのある仕事だ。","romaji":"Nagai jikan o kake-gai no aru shigoto da.","en":"It's a job worth spending a long time on.","id":"Ini adalah pekerjaan yang layak untuk dilakukan dalam waktu lama."},{"jp":"彼とは話しがいがあるでしょう。","romaji":"Kare to wa hanashi-gai ga aru deshō.","en":"It's worth talking to him.","id":"Ada baiknya berbicara dengannya."}]},{"pattern":"～かいがあって (〜kaiga atte)","meaning":"Used to express that an effort is worth it or has value; 'to be worth the effort' or 'to pay off'.","meaningId":"Digunakan untuk menyatakan bahwa suatu upaya sepadan atau mempunyai nilai; 'sepadan dengan usaha' atau 'membayar'.","formation":"Verb-past + かいがあって / Noun + の + かいがあって","formationId":"Kata kerja lampau + かいがあって / Kata benda + の + かいがあって","examples":[{"jp":"毎日勉強したかいがあって、テストに合格しました。","romaji":"Mainichi benkyō shita kai ga atte, tesuto ni gōkaku shimashita.","en":"Studying every day paid off—I passed the test.","id":"Belajar setiap hari membuahkan hasil—saya lulus ujian."},{"jp":"練習のかいがあって、試合に勝つことができた。","romaji":"Renshū no kai ga atte, shiai ni katsu koto ga dekita.","en":"The practice paid off, and we were able to win the match.","id":"Latihan ini membuahkan hasil, dan kami mampu memenangkan pertandingan."},{"jp":"雨の中を走ってきたかいがあって、電車に間に合った。","romaji":"Ame no naka o hashitte kita kai ga atte, densha ni maniatta.","en":"Running in the rain was worth it, as I made it to the train on time.","id":"Berlari di tengah hujan tidak ada gunanya, karena saya tiba di kereta tepat waktu."},{"jp":"早起きして掃除をしたかいがあって、部屋がきれいになった。","romaji":"Hayaoki shite sōji o shita kai ga atte, heya ga kirei ni natta.","en":"Waking up early to clean paid off; the room is now spotless.","id":"Bangun pagi untuk bersih-bersih membuahkan hasil; ruangan itu sekarang bersih."}]},{"pattern":"～かいもなく (〜kai mo naku)","meaning":"Expresses the meaning of 'without worth', 'in vain', 'fruitless'.","meaningId":"Mengungkapkan arti 'tanpa nilai', 'sia-sia', 'tidak membuahkan hasil'.","formation":"Verb-た + かいもなく / Noun + の + かいもなく","formationId":"Kata Kerja-た + かいもなく / Kata Benda + の + かいもなく","examples":[{"jp":"長い間苦労したかいもなく、失敗してしまった。","romaji":"Nagai aida kurō shita kai mo naku, shippai shite shimatta.","en":"I struggled for a long time, but in the end, it was all in vain and I failed.","id":"Lama sekali aku berjuang, namun pada akhirnya semuanya sia-sia dan aku gagal."},{"jp":"このプロジェクトにたくさん時間をかけたかいもなく、うまくいかなかった。","romaji":"Kono purojekuto ni takusan jikan o kaketa kai mo naku, umaku ikanakatta.","en":"I spent a lot of time on this project, but it ended fruitlessly.","id":"Saya menghabiskan banyak waktu untuk proyek ini, tetapi berakhir sia-sia."},{"jp":"助けを求めたかいもなく、誰も来なかった。","romaji":"Tasuke o motometa kai mo naku, dare mo konakatta.","en":"He asked for help, but it was in vain as no one came.","id":"Ia meminta bantuan, namun sia-sia karena tidak ada yang datang."},{"jp":"色々な方法でダイエットを試みたかいもなく、全然痩せなかった。","romaji":"Iroirona hōhō de daietto o kokoromita kai mo naku, zenzen yasenakatta.","en":"I tried various diet methods, but it was all for nothing—I didn't lose any weight.","id":"Saya mencoba berbagai metode diet, tetapi semuanya sia-sia—berat badan saya tidak turun."}]},{"pattern":"～かける (〜kakeru)","meaning":"Indicates a process or action is 'in progress' or 'halfway'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan proses atau tindakan sedang 'sedang berlangsung' atau 'setengah jalan'.","formation":"Verb-stem + かける","formationId":"Batang kata kerja + かける","examples":[{"jp":"彼女は食べかけのリンゴを置いて出かけた。","romaji":"Kanojo wa tabe-kake no ringo o oite dekaketa.","en":"She left a partially eaten apple and went out.","id":"Dia meninggalkan apel yang sudah dimakan sebagian dan keluar."},{"jp":"子供たちはやりかけの宿題を机の上に残した。","romaji":"Kodomotachi wa yari-kake no shukudai o tsukue no ue ni nokoshita.","en":"The children left their half-finished homework on the desk.","id":"Anak-anak meninggalkan pekerjaan rumah mereka yang setengah selesai di meja."},{"jp":"読みかけの本を夜になると探す。","romaji":"Yomi-kake no hon o yoru ni naru to sagasu.","en":"I look for the book I started reading once night comes.","id":"Saya mencari buku yang mulai saya baca ketika malam tiba."},{"jp":"オフィスには、作りかけの書類がたくさんある。","romaji":"Ofisu ni wa, tsukuri-kake no shorui ga takusan aru.","en":"There are a lot of documents in the process of being created in the office.","id":"Ada banyak sekali dokumen yang sedang dalam proses pembuatan di kantor."}]},{"pattern":"～がち (〜gachi)","meaning":"Expresses that something tends to occur frequently or habitually.","meaningId":"Menyatakan bahwa sesuatu cenderung sering terjadi atau menjadi kebiasaan.","formation":"Verb-ます stem + がち / い-Adjective stem + がち / な-Adjective stem + がち","formationId":"Kata kerja-ます batang + がち / い-Batang kata sifat + がち / な-Batang kata sifat + がち","examples":[{"jp":"彼は風邪を引きがちです。","romaji":"Kare wa kaze o hiki-gachi desu.","en":"He tends to catch colds easily.","id":"Ia cenderung mudah masuk angin."},{"jp":"この地域は雨が降りがちです。","romaji":"Kono chiiki wa ame ga furi-gachi desu.","en":"This area tends to get a lot of rain.","id":"Daerah ini cenderung banyak diguyur hujan."},{"jp":"彼女は忘れ物をしがちです。","romaji":"Kanojo wa wasuremono o shi-gachi desu.","en":"She tends to forget things.","id":"Dia cenderung melupakan banyak hal."},{"jp":"私は遅刻しがちなので、もっと早く起きないといけません。","romaji":"Watashi wa chikoku shi-gachi na no de, motto hayaku okinai to ikemasen.","en":"I tend to be late, so I need to wake up earlier.","id":"Saya cenderung terlambat, jadi saya harus bangun lebih awal."}]},{"pattern":"～か～ないかのうちに (〜ka〜naika no uchi ni)","meaning":"Expresses an action that occurs immediately after another action; 'as soon as', 'no sooner than', 'the moment'.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan suatu tindakan yang terjadi segera setelah tindakan lainnya; 'segera', 'tidak lebih cepat dari', 'saat ini'.","formation":"Verb-casual + か + Verb-negative form + かのうちに","formationId":"Kata kerja-kasual + か + Bentuk kata kerja-negatif + かのうちに","examples":[{"jp":"駅に着くか着かないかのうちに、雨が降り出した。","romaji":"Eki ni tsuku ka tsukanai ka no uchi ni, ame ga furidashita.","en":"No sooner had I arrived at the station than it started raining.","id":"Tidak lama setelah saya tiba di stasiun, hujan mulai turun."},{"jp":"ケータイを買うか買わないかのうちに、新しいモデルが発売された。","romaji":"Keitai o kau ka kawanai ka no uchi ni, atarashii moderu ga hatsubai sareta.","en":"As soon as I decided to buy the cell phone, a new model was released.","id":"Segera setelah saya memutuskan untuk membeli ponsel, model baru dirilis."},{"jp":"彼が家を出るか出ないかのうちに、電話が鳴った。","romaji":"Kare ga ie o deru ka denai ka no uchi ni, denwa ga natta.","en":"The moment he left the house, the phone rang.","id":"Saat dia meninggalkan rumah, telepon berdering."},{"jp":"パーティーが始まるか始まらないかのうちに、彼女が泣き出した。","romaji":"Pātī ga hajimaru ka hajimaranai ka no uchi ni, kanojo ga nakidashita.","en":"As soon as the party began, she started crying.","id":"Begitu pesta dimulai, dia mulai menangis."}]},{"pattern":"～かねない (〜kane nai)","meaning":"Express the likelihood of a negative outcome or consequence.","meaningId":"Nyatakan kemungkinan hasil atau konsekuensi negatif.","formation":"Verb-stem + かねない","formationId":"Kata kerja dasar + かねない","examples":[{"jp":"彼はあまりにも無責任で、約束を破りかねない。","romaji":"Kare wa amarini mo musekinin de, yakusoku o yaburi-kane nai.","en":"He is so irresponsible that he might break his promise.","id":"Dia sangat tidak bertanggung jawab sehingga dia mungkin mengingkari janjinya."},{"jp":"注意しないと、事故を起こしかねない。","romaji":"Chūi shinai to, jiko o okoshi-kane nai.","en":"If you don't pay attention, you might cause an accident.","id":"Jika tidak hati-hati, bisa saja terjadi kecelakaan."},{"jp":"このアプリはバグが多いので、クラッシュしかねない。","romaji":"Kono apuri wa bagu ga ōi no de, kurasshu shi-kane nai.","en":"Since this app has many bugs, it might crash.","id":"Karena aplikasi ini memiliki banyak bug, aplikasi ini mungkin macet."},{"jp":"彼女は緊張しているので、失敗しかねない。","romaji":"Kanojo wa kinchō shite iru no de, shippai shi-kane nai.","en":"She's so nervous that she might fail.","id":"Dia sangat gugup sehingga dia mungkin gagal."}]},{"pattern":"～かねる (〜kaneru)","meaning":"Express inability or impossibility of doing an action (often as a polite refusal).","meaningId":"Menyatakan ketidakmampuan atau ketidakmungkinan melakukan suatu tindakan (seringkali dalam bentuk penolakan yang sopan).","formation":"Verb-ます stem + かねる","formationId":"Kata kerja-ます batang + かねる","examples":[{"jp":"その問題は難しいので、私には解決しかねます。","romaji":"Sono mondai wa muzukashii no de, watashi ni wa kaiketsu shi-kanemasu.","en":"Since that problem is difficult, I cannot solve it.","id":"Karena soal itu sulit, saya tidak bisa menyelesaikannya."},{"jp":"彼の言っていることが真実かどうか判断しかねます。","romaji":"Kare no itte iru koto ga shinjitsu ka dō ka handan shi-kanemasu.","en":"I cannot judge whether what he is saying is true or not.","id":"Saya tidak bisa menilai apakah yang dia katakan itu benar atau tidak."},{"jp":"彼女が来るかどうか今すぐには分かりかねます。","romaji":"Kanojo ga kuru ka dō ka ima sugu ni wa wakari-kanemasu.","en":"I cannot immediately know whether she will come or not.","id":"Saya tidak bisa langsung mengetahui apakah dia akan datang atau tidak."},{"jp":"詳しい内容については説明しかねます。","romaji":"Kuwashii naiyō ni tsuite wa setsumei shi-kanemasu.","en":"I cannot explain the details.","id":"Saya tidak bisa menjelaskan detailnya."}]},{"pattern":"～かのようだ (〜ka no you da)","meaning":"Express a similarity or comparison; 'as if', 'like', 'as though'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan persamaan atau perbandingan; 'seolah-olah', 'seperti', 'seolah-olah'.","formation":"Verb-casual + かのようだ, い-Adjective + かのようだ, な-Adjective + であるかのようだ, Noun + であるかのようだ","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + かのようだ, い-Kata Sifat + かのようだ, な-Kata Sifat + であるかのようだ, Kata Benda + であるかのようだ","examples":[{"jp":"彼は犬が怖いかのようだ。","romaji":"Kare wa inu ga kowai ka no you da.","en":"He seems as if he is scared of dogs.","id":"Sepertinya dia takut pada anjing."},{"jp":"この部屋は寒いかのようだ。","romaji":"Kono heya wa samui ka no you da.","en":"This room feels as if it's cold.","id":"Ruangan ini terasa dingin."},{"jp":"彼女は有名人であるかのようだ。","romaji":"Kanojo wa yuumeijin de aru ka no you da.","en":"She acts as though she is a celebrity.","id":"Dia bertindak seolah-olah dia adalah seorang selebriti."},{"jp":"彼は子供であるかのようだ。","romaji":"Kare wa kodomo de aru ka no you da.","en":"He acts as if he's a child.","id":"Dia bertindak seolah-olah dia masih anak-anak."}]},{"pattern":"～か～まいか (〜ka 〜maika)","meaning":"Used to express a dilemma or indecision between two options or actions.","meaningId":"Digunakan untuk menyatakan dilema atau keragu-raguan antara dua pilihan atau tindakan.","formation":"Verb-volitional + か + Verb-volitional + まいか, い-Adjective + であるか + い-Adjective + であるまいか, な-Adjective + であるか + な-Adjective + であるまいか, Noun + であるか + Noun + であるまいか","formationId":"Kata kerja-kehendak + か + Kata kerja-kehendak + まいか, い-Kata Sifat + であるか + い-Kata Sifat + であるまいか, な-Kata Sifat + であるか + な-Kata Sifat +であるまいか, Kata Benda + であるか + Kata Benda + であるまいか","examples":[{"jp":"このプロジェクトを引き受けようか引き受けまいか、まだ決めていない。","romaji":"Kono purojekuto o hikiukeyou ka hikiukemai ka, mada kimete inai.","en":"I haven't decided whether to take on this project or not.","id":"Saya belum memutuskan apakah akan mengambil proyek ini atau tidak."},{"jp":"彼が成功しようか成功するまいか、今は予測できない。","romaji":"Kare ga seikou shiyou ka seikou suru maika, ima wa yosoku dekinai.","en":"Whether he will succeed or not is unpredictable at the moment.","id":"Apakah dia akan berhasil atau tidak, tidak dapat diprediksi saat ini."},{"jp":"この問題は簡単であるか難しいであるまいか、意見が分かれている。","romaji":"Kono mondai wa kantan de aru ka muzukashii de aru maika, iken ga wakarete iru.","en":"Opinions are divided on whether this problem is simple or difficult.","id":"Pendapat terbagi mengenai apakah masalah ini sederhana atau sulit."},{"jp":"彼はリーダーであるかフォロワーであるまいか、自分で選ぶべきだ。","romaji":"Kare wa riidā de aru ka forowā de aru maika, jibun de erabu beki da.","en":"He should choose for himself whether he is a leader or a follower.","id":"Dia harus memilih sendiri apakah dia seorang pemimpin atau pengikut."}]},{"pattern":"～からこそ (〜kara koso)","meaning":"Express the emphasis on the reason; 'precisely because', 'it is precisely because'.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan penekanan pada alasannya; 'tepatnya karena', 'tepatnya karena'.","formation":"Verb-casual + からこそ, い-Adjective + からこそ, な-Adjective + だからこそ, Noun + だからこそ","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + からこそ, い-Kata Sifat + からこそ, な-Kata Sifat + だからこそ, Kata Benda + だからこそ","examples":[{"jp":"失敗したからこそ、成功の意味がわかる。","romaji":"Shippai shita kara koso, seikou no imi ga wakaru.","en":"It is precisely because I failed that I understand the meaning of success.","id":"Justru karena saya gagal maka saya memahami arti sukses."},{"jp":"苦しかったからこそ、今日の私がある。","romaji":"Kurushikatta kara koso, kyou no watashi ga aru.","en":"It is precisely because I went through hardships that I am who I am today.","id":"Justru karena saya mengalami kesulitan maka saya menjadi seperti sekarang ini."},{"jp":"彼は親切だからこそ、人気がある。","romaji":"Kare wa shinsetsu da kara koso, ninki ga aru.","en":"He is popular precisely because he is kind.","id":"Dia populer justru karena dia baik hati."},{"jp":"昔の経験があるからこそ、その問題がよく理解できる。","romaji":"Mukashi no keiken ga aru kara koso, sono mondai ga yoku rikai dekiru.","en":"I can understand that problem well precisely because I have past experience.","id":"Saya dapat memahami masalah itu dengan baik karena saya memiliki pengalaman masa lalu."}]},{"pattern":"〜からして (〜kara shite)","meaning":"Expresses that something is exceptional, unusual, or negative based on a particular aspect or point.","meaningId":"Menyatakan bahwa ada sesuatu yang luar biasa, tidak biasa, atau negatif berdasarkan aspek atau poin tertentu.","formation":"Noun + からして","formationId":"Kata benda + からして","examples":[{"jp":"彼の顔つきからして、何か悪いことがあったのだろう。","romaji":"Kare no kaotsuki kara shite, nanika warui koto ga atta no darou.","en":"From his facial expression, something bad must have happened.","id":"Dari ekspresi wajahnya, sesuatu yang buruk pasti telah terjadi."},{"jp":"この料理の見た目からして、おいしくなさそうだ。","romaji":"Kono ryouri no mitame kara shite, oishikunasa sou da.","en":"Judging from the appearance of this dish, it doesn't look delicious.","id":"Dilihat dari tampilannya masakan ini sepertinya kurang enak."},{"jp":"彼女の試験成績からして、合格するのは難しいでしょう。","romaji":"Kanojo no shiken seiseki kara shite, goukaku suru no wa muzukashii deshou.","en":"Considering her test scores, it will be difficult for her to pass.","id":"Mengingat nilai ujiannya, akan sulit baginya untuk lulus."},{"jp":"その映画のタイトルからして、面白くないと思う。","romaji":"Sono eiga no taitoru kara shite, omoshirokunai to omou.","en":"Judging from the title of the movie, I think it's not interesting.","id":"Kalau dilihat dari judul filmnya, menurutku kurang menarik."}]},{"pattern":"～からすると (〜kara suru to)","meaning":"Expresses a judgment or evaluation based on a certain standard; 'from this perspective', 'considering', 'judging from'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan penilaian atau evaluasi berdasarkan standar tertentu; 'dari perspektif ini', 'mempertimbangkan', 'menilai dari'.","formation":"Noun + からすると","formationId":"Kata benda + からすると","examples":[{"jp":"経験からすると、この仕事は難しいでしょう。","romaji":"Keiken kara suru to, kono shigoto wa muzukashii deshou.","en":"Considering their experience, this job might be difficult.","id":"Mengingat pengalaman mereka, pekerjaan ini mungkin sulit."},{"jp":"評判からすると、あのレストランはとても美味しいです。","romaji":"Hyouban kara suru to, ano resutoran wa totemo oishii desu.","en":"Judging from the reputation, that restaurant is very delicious.","id":"Dilihat dari reputasinya, restoran itu enak sekali."},{"jp":"価格からすると、この商品は高品質のものと思われます。","romaji":"Kakaku kara suru to, kono shouhin wa kouhinshitsu no mono to omowaremasu.","en":"Considering the price, this product seems to be of high quality.","id":"Dilihat dari harganya, produk ini sepertinya berkualitas tinggi."},{"jp":"このエリアですが、交通の便からすると、便利です。","romaji":"Kono eria desu ga, koutsuu no ben kara suru to, benri desu.","en":"As for this area, considering the transportation convenience, it's convenient.","id":"Sedangkan untuk kawasan ini, mengingat kemudahan transportasinya, maka nyaman."}]},{"pattern":"～からといって (〜kara to itte)","meaning":"Expresses 'just because...doesn't mean' or 'even though...not necessarily'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan 'hanya karena...tidak berarti' atau 'walaupun...belum tentu'.","formation":"Verb-casual + からといって, い-Adjective + からといって, な-Adjective + だからといって, Noun + だからといって","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + からといって, い-Kata Sifat + からといって, な-Kata Sifat + だからといって, Kata Benda + だからといって","examples":[{"jp":"雨が降ったからといって、試合が中止になるわけではありません。","romaji":"Ame ga futta kara to itte, shiai ga chuushi ni naru wake de wa arimasen.","en":"Just because it rained doesn't mean the game will be canceled.","id":"Hanya karena hujan bukan berarti pertandingan dibatalkan."},{"jp":"彼が有名だからといって、彼の意見がいつも正しいわけではない。","romaji":"Kare ga yuumei da kara to itte, kare no iken ga itsumo tadashii wake de wa nai.","en":"Just because he is famous doesn't mean his opinions are always correct.","id":"Hanya karena dia terkenal bukan berarti pendapatnya selalu benar."},{"jp":"このスープが辛いからといって、全ての人が辛いと感じるわけではない。","romaji":"Kono suupu ga karai kara to itte, subete no hito ga karai to kanjiru wake de wa nai.","en":"Just because this soup is spicy doesn't mean everyone will find it spicy.","id":"Hanya karena sup ini pedas bukan berarti semua orang akan menganggapnya pedas."},{"jp":"彼女が泣いているからといって、悲しいわけではないかもしれない。","romaji":"Kanojo ga naiteiru kara to itte, kanashii wake de wa nai kamoshirenai.","en":"Just because she is crying doesn't necessarily mean she's sad.","id":"Hanya karena dia menangis bukan berarti dia sedih."}]},{"pattern":"～から～にかけて (〜kara 〜ni kakete)","meaning":"Expresses a range of time, space, or quantities; 'from...to', 'between...and', 'over'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan rentang waktu, ruang, atau kuantitas; 'dari...ke', 'antara...dan', 'selesai'.","formation":"Noun 1 + から + Noun 2 + にかけて","formationId":"Kata Benda 1 + から + Kata Benda 2 + にかけて","examples":[{"jp":"午前９時から午後５時にかけて、仕事をしています。","romaji":"Gozen ku-ji kara gogo go-ji ni kakete, shigoto wo shite imasu.","en":"I work from 9 in the morning to 5 in the evening.","id":"Saya bekerja dari jam 9 pagi sampai jam 5 sore."},{"jp":"東京から大阪にかけて、新幹線が走っています。","romaji":"Toukyou kara Oosaka ni kakete, shinkansen ga hashitte imasu.","en":"The bullet train runs from Tokyo to Osaka.","id":"Kereta peluru berangkat dari Tokyo ke Osaka."},{"jp":"春から夏にかけて、花がたくさん咲いています。","romaji":"Haru kara natsu ni kakete, hana ga takusan saite imasu.","en":"Many flowers bloom between spring and summer.","id":"Banyak bunga mekar antara musim semi dan musim panas."},{"jp":"２０歳から３０歳にかけて、多くの人が大学を卒業し、仕事に就くことが一般的です。","romaji":"Hatachi kara sanjuu-sai ni kakete, ooku no hito ga daigaku wo sotsugyou shi, shigoto ni tsuku koto ga ippan-teki desu.","en":"It is common for many people to graduate from university and start working between the ages of 20 and 30.","id":"Banyak orang yang lulus dari universitas dan mulai bekerja pada usia 20 hingga 30 tahun adalah hal yang lumrah."}]},{"pattern":"～からには (〜kara niwa)","meaning":"Express a sense of responsibility or determination; 'since', 'now that', 'if'.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan rasa tanggung jawab atau tekad; 'sejak', 'sekarang', 'jika'.","formation":"Noun + だ + からには, な-Adjective + だ + からには, い-Adjective + からには, Verb-casual + からには","formationId":"Kata Benda + だ + からには, な-Kata Sifat + だ + からには, い-Kata Sifat + からには, Kata Kerja-kasual + からには","examples":[{"jp":"試験に合格したからには、一所懸命働かなければならない。","romaji":"Shiken ni goukaku shita kara niwa, isshokenmei hatarakanakereba naranai.","en":"Since I passed the exam, I have to work hard.","id":"Sejak saya lulus ujian, saya harus bekerja keras."},{"jp":"約束したからには、守らなければなりません。","romaji":"Yakusoku shita kara niwa, mamoranakereba narimasen.","en":"Since I made a promise, I must keep it.","id":"Karena aku sudah berjanji, aku harus menepatinya."},{"jp":"この映画が面白いからには、友達にも見せたい。","romaji":"Kono eiga ga omoshiroi kara niwa, tomodachi ni mo misetai.","en":"Since this movie is interesting, I want to show it to my friends too.","id":"Karena film ini menarik, saya ingin menunjukkannya kepada teman-teman saya juga."},{"jp":"彼女が助けを求めたからには、手伝わなければならない。","romaji":"Kanojo ga tasuke wo motometa kara niwa, tetsudawanakereba naranai.","en":"Since she asked for help, I must help her.","id":"Karena dia meminta bantuan, saya harus membantunya."}]},{"pattern":"～から見ると (〜kara miru to)","meaning":"Express a perspective or point of view; 'from the standpoint of', 'in terms of', 'from the perspective of'.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan perspektif atau sudut pandang; 'dari sudut pandang', 'dalam hal', 'dari sudut pandang'.","formation":"Noun + から見ると","formationId":"Kata benda + から見ると","examples":[{"jp":"費用から見ると、このプランはお得です。","romaji":"Hiyou kara miru to, kono puran wa otoku desu.","en":"In terms of cost, this plan is a good deal.","id":"Dari segi biaya, rencana ini bagus."},{"jp":"彼女の意見から見ると、社長の決定は理解できる。","romaji":"Kanojo no iken kara miru to, shachou no kettei wa rikai dekiru.","en":"From her perspective, the president's decision is understandable.","id":"Dari sudut pandangnya, keputusan presiden bisa dimengerti."},{"jp":"実力から見ると、彼はチームで最も優れている。","romaji":"Jitsuryoku kara miru to, kare wa chiimu de mottomo sugurete iru.","en":"In terms of ability, he is the best in the team.","id":"Dari segi kemampuan, dia adalah yang terbaik di tim."},{"jp":"健康面から見ると、この食品は良くない。","romaji":"Kenkoumen kara miru to, kono shokuhin wa yokunai.","en":"From the standpoint of health, this food is not good.","id":"Dari segi kesehatan, makanan ini kurang baik."}]},{"pattern":"～から言うと (〜kara iuto)","meaning":"Express a judgment or opinion based on a specific criterion; 'speaking from', 'in terms of', 'from the viewpoint of'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan penilaian atau pendapat berdasarkan kriteria tertentu; 'berbicara dari', 'dalam istilah', 'dari sudut pandang'.","formation":"Noun + から言うと (common), [Verb-casual / Adjective + から言って] (less common)","formationId":"Kata Benda + から言うと (umum), [Kata kerja kasual / Kata Sifat + から言って] (kurang umum)","examples":[{"jp":"値段から言うと、この商品が最もお得です。","romaji":"Nedan kara iuto, kono shouhin ga mottomo otoku desu.","en":"Speaking from the viewpoint of price, this product is the best deal.","id":"Dari segi harga, produk ini adalah yang terbaik."},{"jp":"味から言って、このレストランはおいしいと思います。","romaji":"Aji kara itte, kono resutoran wa oishii to omoimasu.","en":"In terms of taste, I think this restaurant is delicious.","id":"Dari segi rasa, menurut saya restoran ini enak."},{"jp":"便利さから言って、このアパートは最適な場所にあります。","romaji":"Benrisa kara itte, kono apaato wa saiteki na basho ni arimasu.","en":"Speaking from the perspective of convenience, this apartment is in the best location.","id":"Dari segi kenyamanan, apartemen ini berada di lokasi terbaik."},{"jp":"健康から言うと、毎日運動することが大切です。","romaji":"Kenkou kara iuto, mainichi undou suru koto ga taisetsu desu.","en":"From the viewpoint of health, it is important to exercise every day.","id":"Dari sudut pandang kesehatan, penting untuk berolahraga setiap hari."}]},{"pattern":"～くせに (〜kuse ni)","meaning":"Used to criticize someone for doing something contrary to what one would expect from their nature or situation.","meaningId":"Digunakan untuk mengkritik seseorang karena melakukan sesuatu yang bertentangan dengan apa yang diharapkan dari sifat atau situasinya.","formation":"Verb (casual) + くせに / い-Adjective + くせに / な-Adjective + な(or の) + くせに / Noun + の + くせに","formationId":"Kata Kerja (kasual) + くせに / い-Kata Sifat + くせに / な-Kata Sifat + な(atau の) + くせに / Kata Benda + の + くせに","examples":[{"jp":"彼はいつも遅刻してくるくせに、自分が待たされるのが嫌いだ。","romaji":"Kare wa itsumo chikoku shite kuru kuse ni, jibun ga matasareru no ga kirai da.","en":"He’s always late, yet he hates being kept waiting.","id":"Dia selalu terlambat, namun dia benci terus menunggu."},{"jp":"悪いなと言ってるくせに、また同じことを繰り返している。","romaji":"Warui na to itteru kuse ni, mata onaji koto o kurikaeshite iru.","en":"He says he's sorry, yet he keeps doing the same thing.","id":"Dia bilang dia minta maaf, namun dia terus melakukan hal yang sama."},{"jp":"彼は背が高いくせに、バスケが下手だ。","romaji":"Kare wa se ga takai kuse ni, basuke ga heta da.","en":"Despite being tall, he's bad at basketball.","id":"Meskipun tinggi, dia buruk dalam bola basket."},{"jp":"この店は有名なのくせに、サービスが悪い。","romaji":"Kono mise wa yuumei na no kuse ni, saabisu ga warui.","en":"Despite being famous, this store has poor service.","id":"Meski terkenal, toko ini memiliki pelayanan yang buruk."}]},{"pattern":"～ことから (〜koto kara)","meaning":"Indicates the reason or basis for something; 'because', 'since', 'due to'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan alasan atau dasar sesuatu; 'karena', 'sejak', 'karena'.","formation":"Verb-casual + ことから / い-Adjective + ことから / な-Adjective + なことから / Noun + のことから","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + ことから / い-Kata Sifat + ことから / な-Kata Sifat + なことから / Kata Benda + のことから","examples":[{"jp":"彼は毎日運動することから、体が丈夫です。","romaji":"Kare wa mainichi undou suru koto kara, karada ga joubu desu.","en":"Because he exercises every day, he is physically strong.","id":"Karena dia berolahraga setiap hari, fisiknya kuat."},{"jp":"この店のサービスがいいことから、いつも混んでいます。","romaji":"Kono mise no saabisu ga ii koto kara, itsumo konde imasu.","en":"This store is always crowded because of its good service.","id":"Toko ini selalu ramai karena pelayanannya yang baik."},{"jp":"彼女は親切なことから、みんなに好かれています。","romaji":"Kanojo wa shinsetsu na koto kara, minna ni sukarete imasu.","en":"She’s well-liked by everyone due to her kindness.","id":"Dia sangat disukai oleh semua orang karena kebaikannya."},{"jp":"その会社の評判が良いことから、就職先として人気があります。","romaji":"Sono kaisha no hyouban ga yoi koto kara, shuushoku-saki toshite ninki ga arimasu.","en":"Because that company’s reputation is good, it’s popular as a place to work.","id":"Karena reputasi perusahaan itu bagus, maka populer sebagai tempat bekerja."}]},{"pattern":"～ことに (〜koto ni)","meaning":"Used to express feelings or emotions about a situation, action, or outcome.","meaningId":"Digunakan untuk mengungkapkan perasaan atau emosi tentang situasi, tindakan, atau hasil.","formation":"Verb-casual + ことに / い-Adjective + ことに / な-Adjective + なことに / Noun + のことに","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + ことに / い-Kata Sifat + ことに / な-Kata Sifat + なことに / Kata Benda + のことに","examples":[{"jp":"彼が急に帰国することに驚いた。","romaji":"Kare ga kyuu ni kikoku suru koto ni odoroita.","en":"I was surprised that he suddenly returned to his home country.","id":"Saya terkejut dia tiba-tiba kembali ke negara asalnya."},{"jp":"彼女が優勝したことに感動した。","romaji":"Kanojo ga yuushou shita koto ni kandou shita.","en":"I was moved by the fact that she won the championship.","id":"Saya tersentuh oleh kenyataan bahwa dia memenangkan kejuaraan."},{"jp":"彼がいつも遅刻することに腹が立つ。","romaji":"Kare ga itsumo chikoku suru koto ni hara ga tatsu.","en":"I get angry that he is always late.","id":"Aku marah karena dia selalu terlambat."},{"jp":"彼女がこんなに美しいことに気がつかなかった。","romaji":"Kanojo ga konna ni utsukushii koto ni ki ga tsukanakatta.","en":"I hadn’t realized how beautiful she was.","id":"Saya tidak menyadari betapa cantiknya dia."}]},{"pattern":"～ことになっている (〜koto ni natte iru)","meaning":"Expresses that something is supposed to be or has been decided (rule, plan, custom).","meaningId":"Menyatakan bahwa sesuatu seharusnya atau telah diputuskan (aturan, rencana, adat istiadat).","formation":"Verb-plain form + ことになっている / い-Adjective + ことになっている / な-Adjective + だ + ことになっている / Noun + だ + ことになっている","formationId":"Kata kerja-bentuk biasa + ことになっている / い-Kata Sifat + ことになっている / な-Kata Sifat + だ + ことになっている / Kata Benda + だ +ことになっている","examples":[{"jp":"日本では、左側を運転することになっています。","romaji":"Nihon de wa, hidarigawa o unten suru koto ni natte imasu.","en":"In Japan, it is decided that people drive on the left side.","id":"Di Jepang, diputuskan bahwa orang mengemudi di sisi kiri."},{"jp":"会社の規則では、制服を着ることになっている。","romaji":"Kaisha no kisoku de wa, seifuku o kiru koto ni natte iru.","en":"According to the company rules, we are supposed to wear uniforms.","id":"Menurut peraturan perusahaan, kami diharuskan mengenakan seragam."},{"jp":"彼女は明日結婚することになっています。","romaji":"Kanojo wa ashita kekkon suru koto ni natte imasu.","en":"She is supposed to get married tomorrow.","id":"Dia seharusnya menikah besok."},{"jp":"この商品は高品質だということになっています。","romaji":"Kono shouhin wa kouhinshitsu da to iu koto ni natte imasu.","en":"It is said (or generally accepted) that this product is of high quality.","id":"Dikatakan (atau diterima secara umum) bahwa produk ini berkualitas tinggi."}]},{"pattern":"～さえ～ば (〜sae ~ba)","meaning":"Expresses that, as long as a certain condition is met, something else will follow; 'if only', 'provided that'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan bahwa, selama suatu kondisi tertentu terpenuhi, maka kondisi lain akan mengikuti; 'kalau saja', 'asalkan'.","formation":"Noun + さえ + Verb-conditional / Verb-ますstem + さえすれば / etc. (varies by part of speech)","formationId":"Kata benda + さえ + Verb-conditional / Verb-ますstem + さえすれば / dll. (bervariasi berdasarkan bagian ucapan)","examples":[{"jp":"お金さえあれば、幸せです。","romaji":"Okane sae areba, shiawase desu.","en":"As long as I have money, I’m happy.","id":"Selama saya punya uang, saya bahagia."},{"jp":"試験に合格しさえすれば、卒業できます。","romaji":"Shiken ni goukaku shi sae sureba, sotsugyou dekimasu.","en":"If only I pass the exam, I can graduate.","id":"Kalau saja aku lulus ujian, aku bisa lulus."},{"jp":"野菜さえたくさん食べれば、母は喜びます。","romaji":"Yasai sae takusan tabereba, haha wa yorokobimasu.","en":"As long as I eat plenty of vegetables, my mother will be happy.","id":"Selama saya makan banyak sayur, ibu saya akan senang."},{"jp":"交通費さえ支払ってもらえれば、どこへでも行きます。","romaji":"Koutsuuhi sae shiharatte moraereba, doko e demo ikimasu.","en":"As long as my transportation costs are covered, I’ll go anywhere.","id":"Selama biaya transportasi saya tanggung, saya akan pergi kemana saja."}]},{"pattern":"～ざるを得ない (〜zaru wo enai)","meaning":"Have no choice but to; cannot help but.","meaningId":"Tidak punya pilihan selain; tidak bisa membantu tetapi.","formation":"Verb-ない form (drop ない) + ざるを得ない","formationId":"Bentuk kata kerja-ない (jatuhkan ない) + ざるを得ない","examples":[{"jp":"この仕事は締め切りが近いので、残業せざるを得ない。","romaji":"Kono shigoto wa shimekiri ga chikai no de, zangyou sezaru wo enai.","en":"Since the deadline is near, I have no choice but to work overtime.","id":"Karena tenggat waktu sudah dekat, saya tidak punya pilihan selain bekerja lembur."},{"jp":"電車が遅れたため、タクシーに乗るざるを得なかった。","romaji":"Densha ga okureta tame, takushii ni noru zaru wo enakatta.","en":"Because the train was delayed, I had no choice but to take a taxi.","id":"Karena keretanya tertunda, saya tidak punya pilihan selain naik taksi."},{"jp":"彼女の説明が納得できなかったが、とりあえず信じざるを得ない。","romaji":"Kanojo no setsumei ga nattoku dekinakatta ga, toriaezu shinjizaru wo enai.","en":"I couldn’t really accept her explanation, but for now I have no choice but to believe her.","id":"Aku tidak bisa menerima penjelasannya, tapi untuk saat ini aku tidak punya pilihan selain mempercayainya."},{"jp":"この状況では、新しい計画を立て直さざるを得ない。","romaji":"Kono joukyou de wa, atarashii keikaku wo tatenaosazaru wo enai.","en":"In this situation, we have no choice but to revise the new plan.","id":"Dalam situasi ini, kami tidak punya pilihan selain merevisi rencana baru."}]},{"pattern":"～ずにはいられない (〜zu ni wa irarenai)","meaning":"Cannot help but; cannot resist doing; an irresistible urge.","meaningId":"Mau tidak mau; tidak bisa menolak melakukan; sebuah dorongan yang tidak bisa ditolak.","formation":"Verb-ない form (drop ない) + ずにはいられない","formationId":"Bentuk kata kerja-ない (jatuhkan ない) + ずにはいられない","examples":[{"jp":"この曲を聞くと、歌わずにはいられない。","romaji":"Kono kyoku o kiku to, utawazu ni wa irarenai.","en":"When I hear this song, I can’t help but sing.","id":"Ketika saya mendengar lagu ini, saya tidak bisa menahan diri untuk tidak bernyanyi."},{"jp":"彼女が泣いているのを見ると、慰めずにはいられない。","romaji":"Kanojo ga naite iru no o miru to, nagusamezu ni wa irarenai.","en":"When I see her crying, I can’t resist comforting her.","id":"Ketika saya melihatnya menangis, saya tidak dapat menahan diri untuk tidak menghiburnya."},{"jp":"この小説は面白いので、読まずにはいられない。","romaji":"Kono shousetsu wa omoshiroi no de, yomazu ni wa irarenai.","en":"This novel is so interesting that I can’t help but read it.","id":"Novel ini sangat menarik sehingga saya tidak bisa tidak membacanya."},{"jp":"彼はおいしい料理を前にすると、食べずにはいられない。","romaji":"Kare wa oishii ryouri o mae ni suru to, tabezu ni wa irarenai.","en":"When he’s faced with delicious food, he can’t help but eat it.","id":"Saat dia dihadapkan pada makanan lezat, dia mau tidak mau memakannya."}]},{"pattern":"～そうにない (〜sou ni nai)","meaning":"Express the unlikelihood of something happening; 'not likely', 'doesn't seem'.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan kemungkinan terjadinya sesuatu; 'tidak mungkin', 'sepertinya tidak'.","formation":"Verb-stem + そうにない / い-Adjective (drop い) + そうにない / な-Adjective + そうにない","formationId":"Kata kerja-batang + そうにない / い-Kata Sifat (jatuhkan い) + そうにない / な-Kata Sifat + そうにない","examples":[{"jp":"この雨は止みそうにない。","romaji":"Kono ame wa yami sou ni nai.","en":"It doesn't seem like this rain will stop.","id":"Sepertinya hujan ini tidak akan berhenti."},{"jp":"彼が試験に合格しそうにない。","romaji":"Kare ga shiken ni goukaku shi sou ni nai.","en":"It doesn't look like he'll pass the exam.","id":"Sepertinya dia tidak akan lulus ujian."},{"jp":"この料理がおいしそうにない。","romaji":"Kono ryouri ga oishisou ni nai.","en":"This dish doesn't look like it will be tasty.","id":"Hidangan ini sepertinya tidak enak."},{"jp":"この部屋はきれいそうにない。","romaji":"Kono heya wa kirei sou ni nai.","en":"This room doesn't seem likely to be clean.","id":"Ruangan ini sepertinya tidak bersih."}]},{"pattern":"～たかと思ったら (〜ta ka to omottara)","meaning":"Express a sequence of events happening in quick succession; 'as soon as', 'no sooner than'.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan rangkaian peristiwa yang terjadi secara berurutan; 'segera', 'tidak lebih cepat dari'.","formation":"Verb-た form + かと思ったら","formationId":"Bentuk kata kerja-た + かと思ったら","examples":[{"jp":"電話をかけたかと思ったら、すぐに彼女が出た。","romaji":"Denwa o kaketa ka to omottara, sugu ni kanojo ga deta.","en":"No sooner had I called than she picked up.","id":"Tidak lama setelah saya menelepon, dia mengangkatnya."},{"jp":"離陸したかと思ったら、飛行機が揺れ始めた。","romaji":"Ririku shita ka to omottara, hikouki ga yure hajimeta.","en":"As soon as we took off, the plane started shaking.","id":"Begitu kami lepas landas, pesawat mulai bergetar."},{"jp":"買い物に行ったかと思ったら、雨が降ってきた。","romaji":"Kaimono ni itta ka to omottara, ame ga futte kita.","en":"No sooner had I gone shopping than it began to rain.","id":"Tidak lama setelah saya pergi berbelanja, hujan mulai turun."},{"jp":"仕事を終わったかと思ったら、上司が追加の仕事を持ってきた。","romaji":"Shigoto o owatta ka to omottara, joushi ga tsuika no shigoto o motte kita.","en":"As soon as I finished work, my boss brought more tasks.","id":"Segera setelah saya selesai bekerja, atasan saya membawa lebih banyak tugas."}]},{"pattern":"～たきり (〜takiri)","meaning":"Express 'since then' or 'after'; used to indicate that an action occurred once and has not been repeated or that a state has continued since a certain event or time.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan 'sejak itu' atau 'setelah'; digunakan untuk menunjukkan bahwa suatu tindakan terjadi satu kali dan belum terulang atau bahwa suatu keadaan terus berlanjut sejak peristiwa atau waktu tertentu.","formation":"Verb-past + きり","formationId":"Kata kerja-masa lalu + きり","examples":[{"jp":"彼は会社を辞めたきり、連絡がない。","romaji":"Kare wa kaisha o yameta kiri, renraku ga nai.","en":"Ever since he quit the company, there's been no contact.","id":"Sejak dia keluar dari perusahaan, tidak ada kontak."},{"jp":"昨日の朝、メールを送ったきり、返事がない。","romaji":"Kinō no asa, mēru o okutta kiri, henji ga nai.","en":"I sent an email yesterday morning, and there's been no reply since then.","id":"Saya mengirim email kemarin pagi, dan tidak ada balasan sejak itu."},{"jp":"子供のころ海に行ったきりで、もう20年になる。","romaji":"Kodomo no koro umi ni itta kiri de, mō nijūnen ni naru.","en":"It's been 20 years since I last went to the sea as a child.","id":"Sudah 20 tahun sejak terakhir kali saya pergi ke laut sebagai seorang anak."},{"jp":"彼女と別れたきり、彼女のことを考えなくなった。","romaji":"Kanojo to wakareta kiri, kanojo no koto o kangaenaku natta.","en":"Ever since I broke up with her, I stopped thinking about her.","id":"Sejak aku putus dengannya, aku berhenti memikirkannya."}]},{"pattern":"～だけあって (〜dake atte)","meaning":"Expresses that something is as expected or deserves its reputation.","meaningId":"Menyatakan bahwa sesuatu sesuai dengan yang diharapkan atau pantas mendapatkan reputasinya.","formation":"Verb-casual + だけあって, い-Adjective + だけあって, な-Adjective + なだけあって, Noun + だけあって","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + だけあって, い-Kata Sifat + だけあって, な-Kata Sifat + なだけあって, Kata Benda + だけあって","examples":[{"jp":"彼は日本語が上手だけあって、日本人のように話すことができる。","romaji":"Kare wa nihongo ga jōzu dake atte, nihonjin no yō ni hanasu koto ga dekiru.","en":"As expected from his good Japanese skills, he can speak like a native.","id":"Seperti yang diharapkan dari kemampuan bahasa Jepangnya yang bagus, dia bisa berbicara seperti penduduk asli."},{"jp":"このレストランは有名だけあって、料理がとても美味しい。","romaji":"Kono resutoran wa yūmei dake atte, ryōri ga totemo oishii.","en":"No wonder this restaurant is famous; the food is very delicious.","id":"Tidak heran restoran ini terkenal; makanannya sangat lezat."},{"jp":"彼女は経験豊富なだけあって、その問題を簡単に解決できた。","romaji":"Kanojo wa keiken hōfu na dake atte, sono mondai o kantan ni kaiketsu dekita.","en":"It's natural that she's experienced; she solved the problem easily.","id":"Wajar jika dia berpengalaman; dia memecahkan masalahnya dengan mudah."},{"jp":"彼は優秀な学生だけあって、いつもテストの点数が高い。","romaji":"Kare wa yūshū na gakusei dake atte, itsumo tesuto no tensū ga takai.","en":"As expected of an excellent student, he always scores high on tests.","id":"Seperti yang diharapkan dari seorang siswa yang berprestasi, dia selalu mendapat nilai tinggi dalam ujian."}]},{"pattern":"～だけましだ (〜dake mashi da)","meaning":"Expresses that although the situation isn’t ideal, it could be worse; 'it’s not great, but at least...'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan bahwa walaupun situasinya tidak ideal, keadaannya bisa saja menjadi lebih buruk; 'itu tidak bagus, tapi setidaknya...'.","formation":"Verb-casual + だけましだ, い-Adjective + だけましだ, な-Adjective + だけましだ, Noun + だけましだ","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + だけましだ, い-Kata Sifat + だけましだ, な-Kata Sifat + だけましだ, Kata Benda + だけましだ","examples":[{"jp":"失敗するだけましだ。もっと大変なことにならなくてよかった。","romaji":"Shippai suru dake mashi da. Motto taihen na koto ni naranakute yokatta.","en":"At least we only failed—it could’ve been much worse.","id":"Setidaknya kami hanya gagal—bisa jadi lebih buruk lagi."},{"jp":"遅れるだけましだ。来られないよりはいい。","romaji":"Okureru dake mashi da. Korarenai yori wa ii.","en":"At least I’m only late. It’s better than not being able to come at all.","id":"Setidaknya aku hanya terlambat. Itu lebih baik daripada tidak bisa datang sama sekali."},{"jp":"小さな部屋だけましだ。全く部屋がないよりはいい。","romaji":"Chīsana heya dake mashi da. Mattaku heya ga nai yori wa ii.","en":"At least we have a small room; it’s better than having no room at all.","id":"Setidaknya kita memiliki ruangan kecil; itu lebih baik daripada tidak punya ruang sama sekali."},{"jp":"彼が結婚しないだけましだ。大変なことになるところだったよ。","romaji":"Kare ga kekkon shinai dake mashi da. Taihen na koto ni naru tokoro datta yo.","en":"At least he’s not getting married—things could have gotten complicated.","id":"Setidaknya dia tidak akan menikah—segalanya bisa menjadi rumit."}]},{"pattern":"～たところ (〜ta tokoro)","meaning":"Used to describe an action that has just been completed, often followed by a result or observation.","meaningId":"Digunakan untuk menggambarkan suatu tindakan yang baru saja selesai, sering kali diikuti dengan hasil atau observasi.","formation":"Verb-past + ところ","formationId":"Kata kerja-masa lalu + ところ","examples":[{"jp":"掃除したところ、部屋がずっとキレイになりました。","romaji":"Sōji shita tokoro, heya ga zutto kirei ni narimashita.","en":"I just finished cleaning, and the room is so much cleaner now.","id":"Saya baru saja selesai membersihkan, dan ruangannya jauh lebih bersih sekarang."},{"jp":"彼に聞いたところ、その質問の答えは分からないみたいです。","romaji":"Kare ni kiita tokoro, sono shitsumon no kotae wa wakaranai mitai desu.","en":"I just asked him, and it seems he doesn't know the answer.","id":"Saya baru saja bertanya kepadanya, dan sepertinya dia tidak tahu jawabannya."},{"jp":"宿題を出したところ、先生が間違いを見つけました。","romaji":"Shukudai o dashita tokoro, sensei ga machigai o mitsukemashita.","en":"As soon as I turned in my homework, the teacher found a mistake.","id":"Segera setelah saya menyerahkan pekerjaan rumah saya, guru menemukan kesalahan."},{"jp":"昼ごはんを食べたところ、気分が良くなりました。","romaji":"Hirugohan o tabeta tokoro, kibun ga yoku narimashita.","en":"Right after eating lunch, I started feeling better.","id":"Tepat setelah makan siang, saya mulai merasa lebih baik."}]},{"pattern":"～たとたん (〜ta totan)","meaning":"Express the moment something happens; 'as soon as', 'just when'.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan saat sesuatu terjadi; 'segera', 'saat'.","formation":"Verb-past + たとたん","formationId":"Kata kerja-masa lalu + たとたん","examples":[{"jp":"ドアを開けたとたん、雨が降り始めた。","romaji":"Doa o aketa totan, ame ga furi-hajimeta.","en":"As soon as I opened the door, it started raining.","id":"Segera setelah saya membuka pintu, hujan mulai turun."},{"jp":"電話をかけたとたん、バッテリーが切れた。","romaji":"Denwa o kaketa totan, batterī ga kireta.","en":"Just when I made the phone call, the battery died.","id":"Tepat saat saya menelepon, baterainya mati."},{"jp":"彼女に会ったとたん、思い出の歌が流れた。","romaji":"Kanojo ni atta totan, omoide no uta ga nagareta.","en":"No sooner had I met her than a nostalgic song started playing.","id":"Tidak lama setelah saya bertemu dengannya, sebuah lagu nostalgia mulai diputar."},{"jp":"テストが終わったとたん、リラックスできた。","romaji":"Tesuto ga owatta totan, rirakkusu dekita.","en":"The moment the test ended, I was able to relax.","id":"Saat ujian berakhir, saya bisa bersantai."}]},{"pattern":"～だらけ (〜darake)","meaning":"Indicates that something is full of or covered with a certain (usually negative) characteristic.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan bahwa sesuatu penuh atau ditutupi dengan karakteristik tertentu (biasanya negatif).","formation":"Noun + だらけ","formationId":"Kata benda + だらけ","examples":[{"jp":"彼の部屋はゴミだらけだ。","romaji":"Kare no heya wa gomi darake da.","en":"His room is full of trash.","id":"Kamarnya penuh dengan sampah."},{"jp":"このビーチは岩だらけで泳ぎにくい。","romaji":"Kono bīchi wa iwa darake de oyogi nikui.","en":"This beach is full of rocks and is difficult to swim at.","id":"Pantai ini penuh dengan bebatuan dan sulit untuk berenang."},{"jp":"彼の顔はしわだらけだ。","romaji":"Kare no kao wa shiwa darake da.","en":"His face is covered with wrinkles.","id":"Wajahnya dipenuhi kerutan."},{"jp":"このリンゴは虫食いだらけだ。","romaji":"Kono ringo wa mushikui darake da.","en":"This apple is riddled with wormholes.","id":"Apel ini penuh dengan lubang cacing."}]},{"pattern":"～っこない (〜kkonai)","meaning":"Expresses the impossibility or very low probability of something happening; 'no way', 'impossible'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan ketidakmungkinan atau sangat kecil kemungkinan terjadinya sesuatu; 'tidak mungkin', 'tidak mungkin'.","formation":"Verb-negative stem + っこない","formationId":"Batang kata kerja negatif + っこない","examples":[{"jp":"こんなに雪が降っているんだから、学校に間に合いっこない。","romaji":"Konna ni yuki ga futteirun dakara, gakkō ni maniai kkonai.","en":"With snow falling this heavily, there's no way we'll make it to school on time.","id":"Dengan turunnya salju sederas ini, mustahil kami bisa tiba di sekolah tepat waktu."},{"jp":"彼は泳げないので、プールの向こう側に泳いで行きっこない。","romaji":"Kare wa oyogenai node, pūru no mukōgawa ni oyoide ikkonai.","en":"Since he can’t swim, there’s no way he’ll make it to the other side of the pool.","id":"Karena dia tidak bisa berenang, tidak mungkin dia bisa sampai ke seberang kolam."},{"jp":"彼女はとても怖がりなので、一人で夜の公園に行きっこない。","romaji":"Kanojo wa totemo kowagari na node, hitori de yoru no kōen ni ikkonai.","en":"She’s so timid, there’s no chance she’d go to the park alone at night.","id":"Dia sangat pemalu, tidak mungkin dia pergi ke taman sendirian di malam hari."},{"jp":"この短い時間で、その本を全部読むことはできっこない。","romaji":"Kono mijikai jikan de, sono hon o zenbu yomu koto wa dekikkonai.","en":"It's impossible to read the entire book in such a short time.","id":"Tidak mungkin membaca keseluruhan buku dalam waktu sesingkat itu."}]},{"pattern":"～つつ (〜tsutsu)","meaning":"Shows two actions happening simultaneously or a contrast; 'while', 'although'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan dua tindakan yang terjadi secara bersamaan atau berlawanan; 'sementara', 'meskipun'.","formation":"Verb-stem + つつ","formationId":"Batang kata kerja + つつ","examples":[{"jp":"彼はテレビを見つつ、宿題をしていました。","romaji":"Kare wa terebi o mitsutsu, shukudai o shite imashita.","en":"He was doing his homework while watching TV.","id":"Dia mengerjakan pekerjaan rumahnya sambil menonton TV."},{"jp":"最近忙しいと思いつつ、毎日運動を続けています。","romaji":"Saikin isogashii to omoi tsutsu, mainichi undō o tsuzukete imasu.","en":"Although I feel busy these days, I still exercise every day.","id":"Meskipun saya merasa sibuk akhir-akhir ini, saya tetap berolahraga setiap hari."},{"jp":"彼女は泣きつつ、笑顔で別れを告げた。","romaji":"Kanojo wa naki tsutsu, egao de wakare o tsugeta.","en":"She was crying, yet she said goodbye with a smile on her face.","id":"Dia menangis, namun dia mengucapkan selamat tinggal dengan senyuman di wajahnya."},{"jp":"雨に濡れつつ、彼は歩き続けました。","romaji":"Ame ni nure tsutsu, kare wa aruki tsuzukemashita.","en":"He continued walking even though he was getting soaked by the rain.","id":"Ia terus berjalan meski basah kuyup oleh hujan."}]},{"pattern":"～つつある (〜tsutsu aru)","meaning":"Expresses an ongoing process or gradual change.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan proses yang sedang berlangsung atau perubahan bertahap.","formation":"Verb-stem + つつある","formationId":"Batang kata kerja + つつある","examples":[{"jp":"地球温暖化は進行しつつある。","romaji":"Chikyū ondanka wa shinkō shitsutsu aru.","en":"Global warming is in progress.","id":"Pemanasan global sedang berlangsung."},{"jp":"この町は急速に発展しつつある。","romaji":"Kono machi wa kyūsoku ni hatten shitsutsu aru.","en":"This town is rapidly developing.","id":"Kota ini berkembang pesat."},{"jp":"子供たちは成長しつつある。","romaji":"Kodomo-tachi wa seichō shitsutsu aru.","en":"The children are growing up.","id":"Anak-anak sedang tumbuh dewasa."},{"jp":"景気が回復しつつある。","romaji":"Keiki ga kaifuku shitsutsu aru.","en":"The economy is recovering.","id":"Perekonomian mulai pulih."}]},{"pattern":"～っぱなし (〜ppanashi)","meaning":"Express a continuous action or state; 'left as is', 'non-stop'.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan tindakan atau keadaan yang berkelanjutan; 'dibiarkan apa adanya', 'tanpa henti'.","formation":"Verb-ます stem + っぱなし","formationId":"Kata kerja-ます batang + っぱなし","examples":[{"jp":"窓を開けっぱなしにして、部屋が寒くなってしまった。","romaji":"Mado o akeppanashi ni shite, heya ga samuku natte shimatta.","en":"I left the window open, and the room got cold.","id":"Saya membiarkan jendela terbuka, dan ruangan menjadi dingin."},{"jp":"彼は音楽を聴くのが好きで、いつもイヤホンをつけっぱなしです。","romaji":"Kare wa ongaku o kiku no ga suki de, itsumo iyahon o tsukeppanashi desu.","en":"He loves listening to music and always has his earphones on.","id":"Dia suka mendengarkan musik dan selalu memakai earphone."},{"jp":"子供はおもちゃを床に置きっぱなしで、片付けなかった。","romaji":"Kodomo wa omocha o yuka ni okippanashi de, katazukenakatta.","en":"The child left the toys on the floor and didn’t put them away.","id":"Anak itu meninggalkan mainannya di lantai dan tidak menyimpannya."},{"jp":"昨夜は忙しかったので、テレビをつけっぱなしにして寝てしまった。","romaji":"Sakuya wa isogashikatta node, terebi o tsukeppanashi ni shite nete shimatta.","en":"I was busy last night, so I left the TV on and fell asleep.","id":"Saya sibuk tadi malam, jadi saya membiarkan TV menyala dan tertidur."}]},{"pattern":"～っぽい (〜ppoi)","meaning":"Indicates that something has the appearance, characteristics, or behavior of something else.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan bahwa sesuatu memiliki penampilan, karakteristik, atau perilaku sesuatu yang lain.","formation":"Noun + っぽい, Verb-casual + っぽい, い-Adjective + っぽい, な-Adjective + っぽい","formationId":"Kata benda + っぽい, Kata Kerja-kasual + っぽい, い-Kata Sifat + っぽい, な-Kata Sifat + っぽい","examples":[{"jp":"彼女は大人っぽい服を着ている。","romaji":"Kanojo wa otonappoi fuku o kite iru.","en":"She’s wearing clothes that look mature.","id":"Dia mengenakan pakaian yang terlihat dewasa."},{"jp":"この説明は分かりにくっぽい。","romaji":"Kono setsumei wa wakari nikuppoi.","en":"This explanation seems hard to understand.","id":"Penjelasan ini sepertinya sulit untuk dipahami."},{"jp":"彼は疲れたっぽい顔をしている。","romaji":"Kare wa tsukareta ppoi kao o shite iru.","en":"He has a face that looks tired.","id":"Dia memiliki wajah yang terlihat lelah."},{"jp":"この部屋は寒っぽい感じがする。","romaji":"Kono heya wa samuppoi kanji ga suru.","en":"This room feels kind of chilly.","id":"Ruangan ini terasa agak dingin."}]},{"pattern":"～ていられない (〜te irarenai)","meaning":"Expresses that one cannot afford to do something; 'can't keep on', 'unable to continue'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan bahwa seseorang tidak mampu melakukan sesuatu; 'tidak dapat melanjutkan', 'tidak dapat melanjutkan'.","formation":"Verb-て form + いられない","formationId":"Bentuk kata kerja-て + いられない","examples":[{"jp":"こんなに忙しいのに、無理に遊んでいられない。","romaji":"Konna ni isogashii noni, muri ni asonde irarenai.","en":"I'm so busy that I can't afford to just play around.","id":"Saya sangat sibuk sehingga saya tidak mampu untuk hanya bermain-main."},{"jp":"寒すぎて、外で待っていられない。","romaji":"Samusugite, soto de matte irarenai.","en":"It's too cold; I can't keep waiting outside.","id":"Ini terlalu dingin; Aku tidak bisa terus menunggu di luar."},{"jp":"この問題は重要だから、放っておいていられない。","romaji":"Kono mondai wa jūyō dakara, houtte oite irarenai.","en":"This issue is too important to ignore.","id":"Masalah ini terlalu penting untuk diabaikan."},{"jp":"彼女の態度が我慢できず、黙っていられない。","romaji":"Kanojo no taido ga gaman dekizu, damatte irarenai.","en":"I can't stand her attitude, so I can't stay silent.","id":"Aku tidak tahan dengan sikapnya, jadi aku tidak bisa tinggal diam."}]},{"pattern":"～てかなわない (〜te kanawanai)","meaning":"Expresses that something cannot be endured, tolerated, or is unbearable.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan bahwa sesuatu tidak dapat ditanggung, ditoleransi, atau tidak tertahankan.","formation":"Adjective (〜く / 〜で) + て + かなわない / Verb phrase (reworded to an adjective/negative) + て + かなわない","formationId":"Kata sifat (〜く / 〜で) + て + かなわない / Frasa kata kerja (diubah menjadi kata sifat/negatif) + て + かなわない","examples":[{"jp":"こんなに暑くてかなわない。","romaji":"Konnani atsukute kanawanai.","en":"I can’t stand this heat.","id":"Aku tidak tahan dengan panas ini."},{"jp":"彼の話は失礼すぎてかなわない。","romaji":"Kare no hanashi wa shitsurei sugite kanawanai.","en":"His remarks are so rude I can’t put up with them.","id":"Ucapannya sangat kasar sehingga saya tidak tahan dengan ucapannya."},{"jp":"映画があまりに感動的で、忘れられなくてかなわない。","romaji":"Eiga ga amari ni kandō-teki de, wasurerarenakute kanawanai.","en":"The movie was so moving that I can’t stand how it stays on my mind.","id":"Film itu begitu mengharukan sehingga saya tidak tahan membayangkannya."},{"jp":"彼女の笑顔がまぶしくてかなわない。","romaji":"Kanojo no egao ga mabushikute kanawanai.","en":"Her smile is so dazzling that it’s overwhelming.","id":"Senyumannya begitu mempesona hingga membuat kewalahan."}]},{"pattern":"～てからでないと (〜te kara denai to)","meaning":"Indicates that something cannot be done before a certain action is completed; 'not until', 'only after'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan bahwa sesuatu tidak dapat dilakukan sebelum tindakan tertentu selesai; 'tidak sampai', 'hanya setelah'.","formation":"Verb-て + からでないと","formationId":"Kata Kerja-て + からでないと","examples":[{"jp":"宿題をしてからでないと、遊びに行けません。","romaji":"Shukudai o shite kara denai to, asobi ni ikemasen.","en":"You cannot go play until you’ve finished your homework.","id":"Anda tidak bisa bermain sampai Anda menyelesaikan pekerjaan rumah Anda."},{"jp":"食事をしてからでないと、デザートを食べられません。","romaji":"Shokuji o shite kara denai to, dezāto o taberaremasen.","en":"You cannot eat dessert until after having a meal.","id":"Anda tidak bisa makan makanan penutup sampai setelah makan."},{"jp":"チケットを買ってからでないと、映画を見られません。","romaji":"Chiketto o katte kara denai to, eiga o miraremasen.","en":"You can’t watch the movie until after you buy a ticket.","id":"Anda tidak dapat menonton filmnya sampai Anda membeli tiketnya."},{"jp":"試験が終わってからでないと、休みを取れません。","romaji":"Shiken ga owatte kara denai to, yasumi o toremasen.","en":"You can’t take time off until the exam is over.","id":"Anda tidak dapat mengambil cuti sampai ujian selesai."}]},{"pattern":"～てこそ (〜te koso)","meaning":"Emphasizes the condition; 'only when', 'precisely because'.","meaningId":"Menekankan kondisi; 'hanya ketika', 'tepatnya karena'.","formation":"Verb-て form + こそ / い-Adjective + くてこそ / な-Adjective + でこそ / Noun + でこそ","formationId":"Bentuk kata kerja-て + こそ / い-Kata Sifat + くてこそ / な-Kata Sifat + でこそ / Kata Benda + でこそ","examples":[{"jp":"勉強してこそ、テストに合格できる。","romaji":"Benkyō shite koso, tesuto ni gōkaku dekiru.","en":"Only when you study can you pass the test.","id":"Hanya ketika Anda belajar Anda dapat lulus ujian."},{"jp":"素直になってこそ、相手の気持ちが分かります。","romaji":"Sunao ni natte koso, aite no kimochi ga wakarimasu.","en":"Only when you’re honest can you understand the other person’s feelings.","id":"Hanya jika Anda jujur, Anda dapat memahami perasaan orang lain."},{"jp":"静かでこそ、心が落ち着く。","romaji":"Shizuka de koso, kokoro ga ochitsuku.","en":"Only in silence can one’s mind be at peace.","id":"Hanya dalam keheningan pikiran seseorang bisa tenang."},{"jp":"友達でこそ、お互いに助け合うのは当然だ。","romaji":"Tomodachi de koso, otagai ni tasukeau no wa tōzen da.","en":"Precisely because we’re friends, it’s natural to help each other.","id":"Justru karena kita berteman, wajar saja jika kita saling membantu."}]},{"pattern":"～でしょうがない (〜deshou ga nai)","meaning":"Expresses an intense emotional or physical state; 'extremely', 'can’t help but'.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan keadaan emosional atau fisik yang intens; 'sangat', 'tidak bisa tidak'.","formation":"い-Adjective(く) + てしょうがない / な-Adjective + で(は)しょうがない / Verb-て form + しょうがない","formationId":"い-Kata Sifat(く) + てしょうがない / な-Kata Sifat + で(は)しょうがない / Bentuk Kata Kerja-て + しょうがない","examples":[{"jp":"今日は暇で(は)しょうがない。","romaji":"Kyō wa hima de shō ga nai.","en":"I’m extremely bored today.","id":"Saya sangat bosan hari ini."},{"jp":"試験が近いから不安でしょうがない。","romaji":"Shiken ga chikai kara fuan deshō ga nai.","en":"I’m so anxious because the exam is coming up.","id":"Saya sangat cemas karena ujian akan segera tiba."},{"jp":"頭が痛くてしょうがないから、早退したい。","romaji":"Atama ga itakute shō ga nai kara, sōtai shitai.","en":"My head hurts so much I can’t stand it—I want to leave early.","id":"Kepalaku sangat sakit hingga aku tidak tahan lagi—aku ingin pulang lebih awal."},{"jp":"新しいゲームが気になってしょうがない。","romaji":"Atarashii gēmu ga ki ni natte shō ga nai.","en":"I can’t help but keep thinking about the new game.","id":"Mau tak mau aku terus memikirkan game baru ini."}]},{"pattern":"～でたまらない (〜de tamaranai)","meaning":"Express extremely strong feelings or sensations; 'can't stand', 'unbearably'.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan perasaan atau sensasi yang sangat kuat; 'tidak tahan', 'tak tertahankan'.","formation":"い-Adjective (く) + てたまらない / な-Adjective + でたまらない / Verb-て form + たまらない","formationId":"い-Kata Sifat (く) + てたまらない / な-Kata Sifat + でたまらない / Bentuk Kata Kerja-て + たまらない","examples":[{"jp":"この暑さは本当に暑くてたまらない。","romaji":"Kono atsusa wa hontō ni atsukute tamaranai.","en":"This heat is absolutely unbearable.","id":"Panas ini sungguh tak tertahankan."},{"jp":"彼女のことが好きでたまらない。","romaji":"Kanojo no koto ga suki de tamaranai.","en":"I like her so much I can hardly stand it.","id":"Aku sangat menyukainya sehingga aku hampir tidak tahan."},{"jp":"この部屋は寒くてたまらない。","romaji":"Kono heya wa samukute tamaranai.","en":"This room is unbearably cold.","id":"Ruangan ini sangat dingin."},{"jp":"彼の態度を見ていると、腹が立ってたまらない。","romaji":"Kare no taido o mite iru to, hara ga tatte tamaranai.","en":"Seeing his attitude makes me extremely angry.","id":"Melihat sikapnya membuatku sangat marah."}]},{"pattern":"～でならない (〜de naranai)","meaning":"Indicates an uncontrollable emotion or feeling; 'can’t help but', 'overwhelmingly'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan emosi atau perasaan yang tidak terkendali; 'tidak bisa membantu tetapi', 'sangat banyak'.","formation":"な-Adjective + でならない / い-Adjective (く) + てならない / Verb-て + ならない","formationId":"な-Kata Sifat + でならない / い-Kata Sifat (く) + てならない / Kata Kerja-て + ならない","examples":[{"jp":"彼の演技が素晴らしくてならない。","romaji":"Kare no engi ga subarashikute naranai.","en":"I can’t help but be amazed at his wonderful performance.","id":"Saya sangat kagum dengan penampilannya yang luar biasa."},{"jp":"合格発表が気になってならない。","romaji":"Gōkaku happyō ga ki ni natte naranai.","en":"I can’t stop worrying about the exam results.","id":"Saya tidak bisa berhenti mengkhawatirkan hasil ujian."},{"jp":"友達が引っ越してしまって、寂しくてならない。","romaji":"Tomodachi ga hikkoshite shimatte, sabishikute naranai.","en":"My friend moved away, and I feel unbearably lonely.","id":"Teman saya pindah, dan saya merasa sangat kesepian."},{"jp":"初めての海外旅行で、不安でならない。","romaji":"Hajimete no kaigai ryokō de, fuan de naranai.","en":"It’s my first trip abroad, and I’m extremely anxious.","id":"Ini adalah perjalanan pertamaku ke luar negeri, dan aku sangat cemas."}]},{"pattern":"～でばかりはいられない (〜de bakari wa irarenai)","meaning":"Cannot afford to only do something; cannot always rely on it.","meaningId":"Tidak mampu hanya melakukan sesuatu; tidak selalu bisa mengandalkannya.","formation":"Verb-て form + ばかりはいられない / Noun + ばかりはいられない (with appropriate particles)","formationId":"Bentuk kata kerja-て + ばかりはいられない / Kata Benda + ばかりはいられない (dengan partikel yang sesuai)","examples":[{"jp":"いつも助けてもらってばかりはいられない。","romaji":"Itsumo tasukete moratte bakari wa irarenai.","en":"I can’t just keep letting people help me all the time.","id":"Saya tidak bisa membiarkan orang lain membantu saya sepanjang waktu."},{"jp":"好きな仕事ばかりしてはいられない。","romaji":"Suki na shigoto bakari shite wa irarenai.","en":"I can’t afford to only do the work I love.","id":"Saya tidak mampu hanya melakukan pekerjaan yang saya sukai."},{"jp":"親に頼ってばかりはいられない。","romaji":"Oya ni tayotte bakari wa irarenai.","en":"I can’t keep depending on my parents forever.","id":"Saya tidak bisa terus bergantung pada orang tua saya selamanya."},{"jp":"休んでばかりはいられない。仕事もしなくちゃ。","romaji":"Yasunde bakari wa irarenai. Shigoto mo shinakucha.","en":"I can’t just keep taking breaks; I have work to do as well.","id":"Saya tidak bisa terus-menerus beristirahat; Aku juga punya pekerjaan yang harus diselesaikan."}]},{"pattern":"～ではないか (〜de wa nai ka)","meaning":"Used to show a strong assertion or emphasis on one’s opinion; 'isn't it?', 'aren't you?', 'right?'.","meaningId":"Digunakan untuk menunjukkan penegasan atau penekanan yang kuat pada pendapat seseorang; 'bukankah?', 'bukankah?', 'kan?'.","formation":"Noun + ではないか / い-Adjective + ではないか / な-Adjective + ではないか / Verb-casual + ではないか","formationId":"Kata Benda + ではないか / い-Kata Sifat + ではないか / な-Kata Sifat + ではないか / Kata Kerja-kasual + ではないか","examples":[{"jp":"彼は優秀な学生ではないか。","romaji":"Kare wa yūshū na gakusei de wa nai ka.","en":"Isn’t he an excellent student?","id":"Bukankah dia murid yang berprestasi?"},{"jp":"この料理は美味しいではないか。","romaji":"Kono ryōri wa oishii de wa nai ka.","en":"Isn’t this dish delicious?","id":"Bukankah hidangan ini enak?"},{"jp":"あなたは彼女の友達ではないか。","romaji":"Anata wa kanojo no tomodachi de wa nai ka.","en":"Aren’t you her friend?","id":"Bukankah kamu temannya?"},{"jp":"明日は休みではないか。","romaji":"Ashita wa yasumi de wa nai ka.","en":"Tomorrow’s a day off, right?","id":"Besok hari libur, kan?"}]},{"pattern":"～てはならない (〜te wa naranai)","meaning":"Express prohibition; 'must not', 'cannot', 'should not'.","meaningId":"Larangan tegas; 'tidak boleh', 'tidak bisa', 'tidak boleh'.","formation":"Verb-て form + はならない","formationId":"Bentuk kata kerja-て + はならない","examples":[{"jp":"ここでタバコを吸ってはならない。","romaji":"Koko de tabako o sutte wa naranai.","en":"You must not smoke here.","id":"Anda tidak boleh merokok di sini."},{"jp":"秘密を他人に話してはならない。","romaji":"Himitsu o tanin ni hanashite wa naranai.","en":"You cannot reveal this secret to others.","id":"Anda tidak dapat mengungkapkan rahasia ini kepada orang lain."},{"jp":"この部屋に入ってはならない。","romaji":"Kono heya ni haitte wa naranai.","en":"You must not enter this room.","id":"Anda tidak boleh memasuki ruangan ini."},{"jp":"飲酒運転をしてはならない。","romaji":"Inshu unten o shite wa naranai.","en":"You must not drink and drive.","id":"Anda tidak boleh minum dan mengemudi."}]},{"pattern":"～てまで (〜te made)","meaning":"Express the extent someone goes in order to achieve something; 'to the point of', 'even', 'so far as to'.","meaningId":"Mengungkapkan sejauh mana seseorang berusaha mencapai sesuatu; 'sampai', 'genap', 'sejauh'.","formation":"Verb-て form + まで","formationId":"Bentuk kata kerja-て + まで","examples":[{"jp":"彼は試験に合格するために、徹夜してまで勉強しました。","romaji":"Kare wa shiken ni gōkaku suru tame ni, tetsuya shite made benkyō shimashita.","en":"He studied to the point of staying up all night in order to pass the exam.","id":"Ia belajar sampai begadang semalaman agar bisa lulus ujian."},{"jp":"この商品がほしかったので、朝早く起きてまで並んで買いました。","romaji":"Kono shōhin ga hoshikatta node, asa hayaku okite made narande kaimashita.","en":"I wanted this product so much that I went so far as to get up early and wait in line to buy it.","id":"Saya sangat menginginkan produk ini sehingga saya bangun pagi-pagi dan mengantri untuk membelinya."},{"jp":"彼女は彼を助けるために、お金を借りてまで手術代を払いました。","romaji":"Kanojo wa kare o tasukeru tame ni, okane o karite made shujutsudai o haraimashita.","en":"In order to help him, she even borrowed money to pay for the surgery.","id":"Untuk membantunya, dia bahkan meminjam uang untuk membayar operasinya."},{"jp":"部長はそのプロジェクトを成功させるために、休日も働いてまで取り組んでいます。","romaji":"Buchō wa sono purojekuto o seikō saseru tame ni, kyūjitsu mo hataraite made torikunde imasu.","en":"The manager is even working on holidays to make the project a success.","id":"Manajer bahkan bekerja pada hari libur untuk menyukseskan proyek tersebut."}]},{"pattern":"～て当然だ (〜te tōzen da)","meaning":"Expresses that something is natural or expected.","meaningId":"Menyatakan bahwa sesuatu itu wajar atau diharapkan.","formation":"Verb-て form + 当然だ","formationId":"Bentuk kata kerja-て + 当然だ","examples":[{"jp":"彼は毎日勉強しているから、試験に合格して当然だ。","romaji":"Kare wa mainichi benkyō shite iru kara, shiken ni gōkaku shite tōzen da.","en":"Since he studies every day, it's only natural that he passes the exam.","id":"Karena dia belajar setiap hari, wajar saja jika dia lulus ujian."},{"jp":"そのレストランは料理が美味しいので、予約がいっぱいになって当然だ。","romaji":"Sono resutoran wa ryōri ga oishii node, yoyaku ga ippai ni natte tōzen da.","en":"Because that restaurant’s food is delicious, no wonder its reservations are always full.","id":"Karena makanan di restoran itu enak, tak heran jika reservasinya selalu penuh."},{"jp":"彼女は毎晩練習しているので、上手になって当然だ。","romaji":"Kanojo wa maiban renshū shite iru node, jōzu ni natte tōzen da.","en":"She practices every night, so it's natural that she becomes skilled.","id":"Dia berlatih setiap malam, jadi wajar jika dia menjadi terampil."},{"jp":"彼は仕事で成功していて、お金持ちになって当然だ。","romaji":"Kare wa shigoto de seikō shite ite, okanemochi ni natte tōzen da.","en":"He has succeeded at his job, so it's only natural that he's become wealthy.","id":"Dia telah berhasil dalam pekerjaannya, jadi wajar saja jika dia menjadi kaya raya."}]},{"pattern":"～というものだ (〜to iu mono da)","meaning":"Expressing a general rule or common sense.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan aturan umum atau akal sehat.","formation":"Sentence + というものだ","formationId":"Kalimat + というものだ","examples":[{"jp":"若者の熱情は尊敬に値するというものだ。","romaji":"Wakamono no netsujō wa sonkei ni ataisuru to iu mono da.","en":"The passion of young people is something that deserves respect.","id":"Semangat generasi muda merupakan sesuatu yang patut dihormati."},{"jp":"勉強は一日でもサボれば遅れるというものだ。","romaji":"Benkyō wa ichinichi demo saboreba okureru to iu mono da.","en":"If you skip even a day of studying, you'll fall behind—that's just how it is.","id":"Jika Anda melewatkan satu hari pun untuk belajar, Anda akan tertinggal—begitulah yang terjadi."},{"jp":"成功するためには困難に立ち向かうというものだ。","romaji":"Seikō suru tame ni wa konnan ni tachimukau to iu mono da.","en":"To succeed, one must face difficulties—that's just the way it is.","id":"Untuk berhasil, seseorang harus menghadapi kesulitan—begitulah adanya."},{"jp":"友情はお金で買えないというものだ。","romaji":"Yūjō wa okane de kaenai to iu mono da.","en":"It is said that friendship cannot be bought with money.","id":"Ada pepatah yang mengatakan persahabatan tidak bisa dibeli dengan uang."}]},{"pattern":"どうにか～ないものか (dō ni ka ~ nai mono ka)","meaning":"Express a strong desire or wish for something to be possible.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan keinginan atau harapan yang kuat agar sesuatu menjadi mungkin.","formation":"どうにか + Verb-negative form + ないものか","formationId":"どうにか + Bentuk kata kerja negatif + ないものか","examples":[{"jp":"どうにかこの仕事を終わらせないものか。","romaji":"Dō ni ka kono shigoto o owarasenai mono ka.","en":"Isn't there some way to finish this job?","id":"Apakah tidak ada cara untuk menyelesaikan pekerjaan ini?"},{"jp":"どうにか次の試験で合格しないものか。","romaji":"Dō ni ka tsugi no shiken de gōkaku shinai mono ka.","en":"Can't we somehow pass the next exam?","id":"Tidak bisakah kita lulus ujian berikutnya?"},{"jp":"どうにか込んでいる電車に乗れないものか。","romaji":"Dō ni ka konde iru densha ni norenai mono ka.","en":"Is there no way to get on the crowded train somehow?","id":"Apakah tidak ada cara untuk naik kereta yang penuh sesak itu?"},{"jp":"どうにか彼女と仲直りしないものか。","romaji":"Dō ni ka kanojo to nakanaori shinai mono ka.","en":"Isn't there some way to make up with her?","id":"Apakah tidak ada cara untuk berbaikan dengannya?"}]},{"pattern":"～とおり (〜toori)","meaning":"Express doing something as instructed or describing how something matches a rule or guideline; 'as', 'according to'.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan melakukan sesuatu seperti yang diinstruksikan atau menggambarkan bagaimana sesuatu sesuai dengan aturan atau pedoman; 'sebagai', 'menurut'.","formation":"Verb-casual + とおり, い-Adjective + とおり, な-Adjective + だとおり, Noun + だとおり","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + とおり, い-Kata Sifat + とおり, な-Kata Sifat + だとおり, Kata Benda + だとおり","examples":[{"jp":"先生が言ったとおりに宿題をしました。","romaji":"Sensei ga itta tōri ni shukudai o shimashita.","en":"I did my homework exactly as the teacher said.","id":"Saya mengerjakan pekerjaan rumah saya persis seperti yang diperintahkan guru."},{"jp":"この地図のとおりに歩いてください。","romaji":"Kono chizu no tōri ni aruite kudasai.","en":"Please walk according to this map.","id":"Silakan berjalan sesuai peta ini."},{"jp":"彼はいつもルールどおりに遊びます。","romaji":"Kare wa itsumo rūru-dōri ni asobimasu.","en":"He always plays by the rules.","id":"Dia selalu bermain sesuai aturan."},{"jp":"その道路は昼間と同じくらい夜も賑やかだというとおりでした。","romaji":"Sono dōro wa hiruma to onaji kurai yoru mo nigiyaka da to iu tōri deshita.","en":"As I heard, that street was just as lively at night as it is in the daytime.","id":"Seperti yang saya dengar, jalan itu sama ramainya di malam hari dan di siang hari."}]},{"pattern":"～とか (〜to ka)","meaning":"Used to list examples or express uncertainty; 'such as', 'like', 'or something like that'.","meaningId":"Digunakan untuk membuat daftar contoh atau menyatakan ketidakpastian; 'seperti', 'seperti', 'atau sesuatu seperti itu'.","formation":"Verb-casual + とか, い-Adjective + とか, な-Adjective + だとか, Noun + だとか","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + とか, い-Kata Sifat + とか, な-Kata Sifat + だとか, Kata Benda + だとか","examples":[{"jp":"休日は映画を見るとか、買い物に行くとかして過ごします。","romaji":"Kyūjitsu wa eiga o miru to ka, kaimono ni iku to ka shite sugoshimasu.","en":"On my days off, I do things like watch movies or go shopping.","id":"Pada hari libur, saya melakukan hal-hal seperti menonton film atau berbelanja."},{"jp":"彼女はオーストラリアとかニュージーランドとかに行きたがっています。","romaji":"Kanojo wa Ōsutoraria to ka Nyūjīrando to ka ni ikitagatte imasu.","en":"She wants to go to places like Australia or New Zealand.","id":"Dia ingin pergi ke tempat-tempat seperti Australia atau Selandia Baru."},{"jp":"今日の天気は晴れたり、曇ったりとかだそうです。","romaji":"Kyō no tenki wa hare tari, kumottari to ka da sō desu.","en":"I heard today’s weather is something like sunny at times, cloudy at times.","id":"Kudengar cuaca hari ini terkadang cerah, terkadang berawan."},{"jp":"彼は野球をしたり、サッカーをしたりとかしています。","romaji":"Kare wa yakyū o shitari, sakkā o shitari to ka shite imasu.","en":"He spends his time playing baseball and soccer and such.","id":"Dia menghabiskan waktunya bermain baseball, sepak bola, dan semacamnya."}]},{"pattern":"～ところ (〜tokoro)","meaning":"Express a specific point in time or state; 'when', 'just about', or 'in the middle of'.","meaningId":"Nyatakan titik waktu atau keadaan tertentu; 'kapan', 'hampir', atau 'di tengah-tengah'.","formation":"Verb-casual + ところ, い-Adjective + ところ, な-Adjective + なところ, Noun + のところ","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + ところ, い-Kata Sifat + ところ, な-Kata Sifat + なところ, Kata Benda + のところ","examples":[{"jp":"出かけるところです。","romaji":"Dekakeru tokoro desu.","en":"I'm just about to go out.","id":"Aku baru saja akan keluar."},{"jp":"映画を見ているところです。","romaji":"Eiga o mite iru tokoro desu.","en":"I'm in the middle of watching a movie.","id":"Aku sedang menonton film."},{"jp":"おいしいところで食事をするつもりです。","romaji":"Oishii tokoro de shokuji o suru tsumori desu.","en":"I plan to have a meal at a good (tasty) place.","id":"Saya berencana untuk makan di tempat yang enak (enak)."},{"jp":"彼は忙しいところを手伝ってくれました。","romaji":"Kare wa isogashii tokoro o tetsudatte kuremashita.","en":"He helped me when he himself was busy.","id":"Dia membantu saya ketika dia sendiri sedang sibuk."}]},{"pattern":"～どころか (〜dokoro ka)","meaning":"Express 'far from', 'not just', 'not only', or 'to say nothing of'.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan 'jauh dari', 'tidak hanya', 'tidak hanya', atau 'tidak mengatakan apa-apa'.","formation":"Verb-casual + どころか, い-Adjective + どころか, な-Adjective + どころか, Noun + どころか","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + どころか, い-Kata Sifat + どころか, な-Kata Sifat + どころか, Kata Benda + どころか","examples":[{"jp":"彼は歌が上手どころか、プロの歌手みたいだ。","romaji":"Kare wa uta ga jōzu dokoro ka, puro no kashu mitai da.","en":"Far from just being good at singing, he sounds like a professional singer.","id":"Jauh dari sekadar pandai menyanyi, ia terdengar seperti penyanyi profesional."},{"jp":"この料理はおいしいどころか、最高の味だ。","romaji":"Kono ryōri wa oishii dokoro ka, saikō no aji da.","en":"This dish is not just delicious, it’s absolutely the best.","id":"Hidangan ini tidak hanya enak, tapi juga yang terbaik."},{"jp":"彼女はただの友達どころか、私の親友だ。","romaji":"Kanojo wa tada no tomodachi dokoro ka, watashi no shin’yū da.","en":"She’s far from just a friend; she’s my best friend.","id":"Dia bukan sekedar teman; dia sahabatku."},{"jp":"彼は英語ができるどころか、他の3つの言語も話せる。","romaji":"Kare wa eigo ga dekiru dokoro ka, hoka no mittsu no gengo mo hanaseru.","en":"Not only can he speak English, he also speaks three other languages.","id":"Dia tidak hanya bisa berbicara bahasa Inggris, dia juga berbicara tiga bahasa lainnya."}]},{"pattern":"～どころではない (〜dokoro de wa nai)","meaning":"Not the time/place for; far from; can't possibly.","meaningId":"Bukan waktu/tempat untuk; jauh dari; tidak mungkin.","formation":"Verb-casual + どころではない, い-Adjective + どころではない, な-Adjective + どころではない, Noun + どころではない","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + どころではない, い-Kata Sifat + どころではない, な-Kata Sifat + どころではない, Kata Benda +どころではない","examples":[{"jp":"彼の失敗を笑うどころではない。私たちも同じミスをしている。","romaji":"Kare no shippai o warau dokoro de wa nai. Watashitachi mo onaji misu o shite iru.","en":"This is not the time to laugh at his mistakes—we’re making the same ones.","id":"Ini bukan waktunya untuk menertawakan kesalahannya—kita melakukan kesalahan yang sama."},{"jp":"病気で寝ている時は、遊ぶどころではない。","romaji":"Byōki de nete iru toki wa, asobu dokoro de wa nai.","en":"When you’re sick in bed, it's far from the time to play around.","id":"Saat Anda sakit di tempat tidur, ini bukan waktunya untuk bermain-main."},{"jp":"試験が近いので、映画を見るどころではない。","romaji":"Shiken ga chikai node, eiga o miru dokoro de wa nai.","en":"Since the exam is coming up, I can’t possibly watch a movie.","id":"Karena ujian sudah dekat, saya tidak mungkin menonton film."},{"jp":"仕事が忙しすぎて、旅行なんて考えるどころではない。","romaji":"Shigoto ga isogashisugite, ryokō nante kangaeru dokoro de wa nai.","en":"I'm way too busy with work to even think about going on a trip.","id":"Saya terlalu sibuk dengan pekerjaan sehingga tidak berpikir untuk melakukan perjalanan."}]},{"pattern":"～としたら (〜to shitara)","meaning":"Express a hypothetical situation; 'if', 'suppose', 'assuming'.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan situasi hipotetis; 'jika', 'seandainya', 'dengan asumsi'.","formation":"Verb-casual + としたら, い-Adjective + としたら, な-Adjective + だとしたら, Noun + だとしたら","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + としたら, い-Kata Sifat + としたら, な-Kata Sifat + だとしたら, Kata Benda + だとしたら","examples":[{"jp":"明日雨が降るとしたら、傘を持っていきましょう。","romaji":"Ashita ame ga furu to shitara, kasa o motte ikimashō.","en":"If it rains tomorrow, let’s bring umbrellas.","id":"Kalau besok hujan, ayo bawa payung."},{"jp":"このケーキが美味しくないとしたら、誰も食べないだろう。","romaji":"Kono kēki ga oishikunai to shitara, dare mo tabenai darō.","en":"If this cake isn’t tasty, probably no one will eat it.","id":"Jika kue ini tidak enak, mungkin tidak ada yang akan memakannya."},{"jp":"彼が病気だとしたら、早めに病院へ行かないといけません。","romaji":"Kare ga byōki da to shitara, hayame ni byōin e ikanai to ikemasen.","en":"If he is sick, he needs to go to the hospital soon.","id":"Jika dia sakit, dia harus segera pergi ke rumah sakit."},{"jp":"彼女が学生だとしたら、このレストランは割引があるでしょう。","romaji":"Kanojo ga gakusei da to shitara, kono resutoran wa waribiki ga aru deshō.","en":"If she’s a student, there’s probably a discount at this restaurant.","id":"Jika dia seorang pelajar, mungkin ada diskon di restoran ini."}]},{"pattern":"～としても (〜to shite mo)","meaning":"Even if, despite, although","meaningId":"Sekalipun, meskipun demikian","formation":"Verb-casual + としても, い-Adjective + としても, な-Adjective + だとしても, Noun + だとしても","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + としても, い-Kata Sifat + としても, な-Kata Sifat + だとしても, Kata Benda + だとしても","examples":[{"jp":"雨が降るとしても、レースは中止しません。","romaji":"Ame ga furu to shite mo, rēsu wa chūshi shimasen.","en":"Even if it rains, we won't cancel the race.","id":"Meski hujan, kami tidak akan membatalkan balapan."},{"jp":"このケーキが美味しくないとしても、私は食べるつもりです。","romaji":"Kono kēki ga oishikunai to shite mo, watashi wa taberu tsumori desu.","en":"Even if this cake isn't delicious, I plan on eating it.","id":"Meskipun kue ini tidak enak, saya berencana untuk memakannya."},{"jp":"彼女が遅刻するとしても、私たちは待ち続けます。","romaji":"Kanojo ga chikoku suru to shite mo, watashitachi wa machitsuzukemasu.","en":"Even if she is late, we will keep waiting.","id":"Meski dia terlambat, kami akan tetap menunggu."},{"jp":"忙しいだとしても、友達との約束は守りたい。","romaji":"Isogashii da to shite mo, tomodachi to no yakusoku wa mamoritai.","en":"Even if I'm busy, I want to keep my promise to my friend.","id":"Walaupun aku sibuk, aku ingin menepati janjiku pada temanku."}]},{"pattern":"～と～ともに (〜to 〜tomoni)","meaning":"Expresses 'together with' or 'along with'; used to describe two events or actions happening simultaneously or in parallel.","meaningId":"Menyatakan 'bersama dengan' atau 'bersama dengan'; digunakan untuk menggambarkan dua peristiwa atau tindakan yang terjadi secara bersamaan atau paralel.","formation":"Verb-casual + とともに, い-Adjective + とともに, な-Adjective + とともに, Noun + とともに","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + とともに, い-Kata Sifat + とともに, な-Kata Sifat + とともに, Kata Benda + とともに","examples":[{"jp":"彼が来るとともに、パーティーが始まりました。","romaji":"Kare ga kuru to tomoni, paatii ga hajimarimashita.","en":"The party started as soon as he arrived.","id":"Pesta dimulai segera setelah dia tiba."},{"jp":"季節が変わるとともに、服のファッションも変わります。","romaji":"Kisetsu ga kawaru to tomoni, fuku no fasshon mo kawarimasu.","en":"As the seasons change, clothing fashion also changes.","id":"Seiring bergantinya musim, fashion pakaian pun ikut berubah."},{"jp":"成長とともに、いろいろな経験を積むことが大切です。","romaji":"Seichou to tomoni, iroirona keiken wo tsumu koto ga taisetsu desu.","en":"As you grow, it is important to gain various experiences.","id":"Saat Anda tumbuh, penting untuk mendapatkan berbagai pengalaman."},{"jp":"技術の進歩とともに、便利なアプリが増えています。","romaji":"Gijutsu no shinpo to tomoni, benrina apuri ga fueteimasu.","en":"With the advancement of technology, the number of convenient apps is increasing.","id":"Dengan kemajuan teknologi, jumlah aplikasi yang mudah digunakan semakin meningkat."}]},{"pattern":"～とは限らない (〜to wa kagiranai)","meaning":"Expresses that something is not necessarily true; 'not always', 'not necessarily'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan bahwa sesuatu belum tentu benar; 'tidak selalu', 'belum tentu'.","formation":"Verb-casual + とは限らない, い-Adjective + とは限らない, な-Adjective + だとは限らない, Noun + だとは限らない","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + とは限らない, い-Kata Sifat + とは限らない, な-Kata Sifat + だとは限らない, Kata Benda + だとは限らない","examples":[{"jp":"いつも勉強しているとは限らない。","romaji":"Itsumo benkyou shite iru to wa kagiranai.","en":"It's not always true that I'm studying.","id":"Tidak selalu benar bahwa saya sedang belajar."},{"jp":"高い商品がいいとは限らない。","romaji":"Takai shouhin ga ii to wa kagiranai.","en":"Expensive products are not necessarily good.","id":"Produk mahal belum tentu bagus."},{"jp":"彼が正しいとは限らない。","romaji":"Kare ga tadashii to wa kagiranai.","en":"It's not necessarily true that he is right.","id":"Belum tentu dia benar."},{"jp":"雨が降るとは限らない。","romaji":"Ame ga furu to wa kagiranai.","en":"It's not necessarily going to rain.","id":"Belum tentu akan turun hujan."}]},{"pattern":"～ないことはない (〜nai koto wa nai)","meaning":"Express that something is not impossible, meaning it is possible or could be done.","meaningId":"Menyatakan bahwa sesuatu itu bukan sesuatu yang mustahil, artinya mungkin atau bisa dilakukan.","formation":"Verb-ないform + ことはない","formationId":"Kata kerja-ないbentuk + ことはない","examples":[{"jp":"彼が来ないことはない。","romaji":"Kare ga konai koto wa nai.","en":"It's not that he won't come (it's possible that he will come).","id":"Bukannya dia tidak akan datang (mungkin saja dia akan datang)."},{"jp":"あの問題が解けないことはない。","romaji":"Ano mondai ga tokenai koto wa nai.","en":"It's not impossible to solve that problem (it can be solved).","id":"Bukan hal yang mustahil untuk menyelesaikan masalah itu (bisa diselesaikan)."},{"jp":"その仕事が難しくないことはない。","romaji":"Sono shigoto ga muzukashikunai koto wa nai.","en":"That job is not without difficulty (it has some difficulties).","id":"Pekerjaan itu bukannya tanpa kesulitan (memiliki beberapa kesulitan)."},{"jp":"彼女が正しくないことはない。","romaji":"Kanojo ga tadashikunai koto wa nai.","en":"It's not impossible that she is right (she could be right).","id":"Bukan tidak mungkin dia benar (dia bisa saja benar)."}]},{"pattern":"～ないこともない (〜nai koto mo nai)","meaning":"Used to express an action or state is 'not impossible', but emphasizes reluctance or doubt.","meaningId":"Digunakan untuk menyatakan suatu tindakan atau keadaan 'bukanlah mustahil', namun menekankan keengganan atau keraguan.","formation":"Verb-ないForm + こともない, い-adjective + こともない","formationId":"Kata kerja-ないBentuk + こともない, い-kata sifat + こともない","examples":[{"jp":"この問題は解けないこともないけど、難しいです。","romaji":"Kono mondai wa tokenai koto mo nai kedo, muzukashii desu.","en":"It's not that I can't solve this problem, but it's difficult.","id":"Bukannya saya tidak bisa menyelesaikan masalah ini, tapi sulit."},{"jp":"彼に会わないこともないが、あまり話す時間がない。","romaji":"Kare ni awanai koto mo nai ga, amari hanasu jikan ga nai.","en":"It's not that I can't meet him, but there's not much time to talk.","id":"Bukannya aku tidak bisa bertemu dengannya, tapi tidak banyak waktu untuk ngobrol."},{"jp":"お金がないこともないけれど、節約した方がいい。","romaji":"O-kane ga nai koto mo nai keredo, setsuyaku shita hou ga ii.","en":"It's not that I don't have money, but it's better to save.","id":"Bukannya saya tidak punya uang, tapi lebih baik menabung."},{"jp":"このゲームが面白くないこともないが、他のゲームの方が楽しい。","romaji":"Kono geemu ga omoshirokunai koto mo nai ga, hoka no geemu no hou ga tanoshii.","en":"It's not that this game isn't interesting, but other games are more fun.","id":"Bukan berarti game ini tidak menarik, tapi game lain lebih seru."}]},{"pattern":"～ないではいられない (〜nai de wa irarenai)","meaning":"Cannot help but; cannot avoid; unable to refrain from.","meaningId":"Mau tidak mau; tidak bisa menghindari; tidak bisa menahan diri.","formation":"Verb-ない form + ではいられない or じゃいられない","formationId":"Bentuk kata kerja-ない + ではいられない atau じゃいられない","examples":[{"jp":"この映画はとても感動的で、泣かないではいられなかった。","romaji":"Kono eiga wa totemo kandouteki de, nakanai de wa irarenakatta.","en":"This movie was so touching, I couldn't help but cry.","id":"Film ini sangat menyentuh, saya tidak bisa menahan tangis."},{"jp":"彼女の笑顔を見ると、笑わないではいられない。","romaji":"Kanojo no egao wo miru to, warawanai de wa irarenai.","en":"When I see her smile, I can't help but laugh.","id":"Saat aku melihatnya tersenyum, aku tidak bisa menahan tawa."},{"jp":"この部屋はとても寒いので、震えないではいられない。","romaji":"Kono heya wa totemo samui node, furuenai de wa irarenai.","en":"This room is so cold, I can't help but shiver.","id":"Ruangan ini sangat dingin, aku menggigil."},{"jp":"彼の話はつまらないが、聞かないではいられない。","romaji":"Kare no hanashi wa tsumaranai ga, kikanai de wa irarenai.","en":"His story is boring, but I can't help but listen.","id":"Ceritanya membosankan, tapi mau tak mau aku mendengarkannya."}]},{"pattern":"～ながら (〜nagara)","meaning":"Express doing two things simultaneously or at the same time.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan melakukan dua hal secara bersamaan atau bersamaan.","formation":"Verb-stem + ながら","formationId":"Batang kata kerja + ながら","examples":[{"jp":"テレビを見ながら宿題をしています。","romaji":"Terebi wo minagara shukudai wo shiteimasu.","en":"I am doing my homework while watching TV.","id":"Saya mengerjakan pekerjaan rumah saya sambil menonton TV."},{"jp":"彼女は歌いながら料理を作っていました。","romaji":"Kanojo wa utainagara ryouri wo tsukutte imashita.","en":"She was cooking while singing.","id":"Dia sedang memasak sambil bernyanyi."},{"jp":"電車の中で立ちながら本を読んでいる人が多いです。","romaji":"Densha no naka de tachinagara hon wo yonde iru hito ga ooi desu.","en":"There are many people who read books while standing on the train.","id":"Banyak orang yang membaca buku sambil berdiri di dalam kereta."},{"jp":"僕は歩きながらスマホを使っています。","romaji":"Boku wa arukinagara sumaho wo tsukatteimasu.","en":"I am using my smartphone while walking.","id":"Saya menggunakan ponsel cerdas saya sambil berjalan."}]},{"pattern":"～にあたり (〜ni atari)","meaning":"Expresses the meaning of 'at the time of', 'in', 'on', or 'upon'.","meaningId":"Mengungkapkan arti 'pada saat', 'dalam', 'pada', atau 'pada'.","formation":"Noun + にあたり","formationId":"Kata benda + にあたり","examples":[{"jp":"入学にあたり、必要な書類を準備してください。","romaji":"Nyuugaku ni atari, hitsuyou na shorui wo junbi shite kudasai.","en":"Please prepare the necessary documents upon entering the school.","id":"Harap siapkan dokumen yang diperlukan saat memasuki sekolah."},{"jp":"新年にあたり、抱負を立てる人が多いです。","romaji":"Shinnen ni atari, houfu wo tateru hito ga ooi desu.","en":"Many people set goals at the time of the new year.","id":"Banyak orang menetapkan tujuan pada saat tahun baru."},{"jp":"結婚にあたり、両家は大切な儀式を行います。","romaji":"Kekkon ni atari, ryouke wa taisetsu na gishiki wo okonaimasu.","en":"Upon getting married, both families conduct an important ceremony.","id":"Setelah menikah, kedua keluarga mengadakan upacara penting."},{"jp":"新しい仕事を始めるにあたり、準備が必要です。","romaji":"Atarashii shigoto wo hajimeru ni atari, junbi ga hitsuyou desu.","en":"In starting a new job, preparation is necessary.","id":"Dalam memulai pekerjaan baru, diperlukan persiapan."}]},{"pattern":"～において (〜ni oite)","meaning":"Indicates the place, time, or context where an action or event occurs; 'in', 'at', 'on', 'regarding'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan tempat, waktu, atau konteks terjadinya suatu tindakan atau peristiwa; 'dalam', 'pada', 'pada', 'mengenai'.","formation":"Noun + において","formationId":"Kata benda + において","examples":[{"jp":"この大学において、英語のクラスが一番人気があります。","romaji":"Kono daigaku ni oite, eigo no kurasu ga ichiban ninki ga arimasu.","en":"In this university, English classes are the most popular.","id":"Di universitas ini, kelas bahasa Inggris adalah yang paling populer."},{"jp":"彼の研究において新しい発見がありました。","romaji":"Kare no kenkyuu ni oite atarashii hakken ga arimashita.","en":"In his research, there were new discoveries.","id":"Dalam penelitiannya, ada penemuan baru."},{"jp":"運動会において、彼は大活躍しました。","romaji":"Undoukai ni oite, kare wa daikatsuyaku shimashita.","en":"At the sports festival, he performed exceptionally well.","id":"Di festival olahraga, dia tampil sangat baik."},{"jp":"環境問題においては、みんなが責任を持って行動すべきです。","romaji":"Kankyou mondai ni oite wa, minna ga sekinin wo motte koudou subeki desu.","en":"Regarding environmental issues, everyone should take responsibility and act accordingly.","id":"Mengenai masalah lingkungan hidup, setiap orang harus mengambil tanggung jawab dan bertindak sesuai dengan hal tersebut."}]},{"pattern":"～にかかわらず (〜ni kakawarazu)","meaning":"Regardless of; irrespective of; (often used as) 'whether or not'.","meaningId":"Terlepas dari; terlepas dari; (sering digunakan sebagai) 'apakah atau tidak'.","formation":"Verb-dictionary form + にかかわらず, い-Adjective + にかかわらず, な-Adjective + にかかわらず, Noun + にかかわらず","formationId":"Bentuk kamus kata kerja + にかかわらず, い-Kata Sifat + にかかわらず, な-Kata Sifat + にかかわらず, Kata Benda + にかかわらず","examples":[{"jp":"天気にかかわらず、今日の試合は行われます。","romaji":"Tenki ni kakawarazu, kyou no shiai wa okonawaremasu.","en":"The game today will be held, regardless of the weather.","id":"Pertandingan hari ini akan digelar, apapun cuacanya."},{"jp":"彼は年齢にかかわらず、新しいことを学び続けています。","romaji":"Kare wa nenrei ni kakawarazu, atarashii koto wo manabi tsuzukete imasu.","en":"He continues to learn new things, regardless of his age.","id":"Dia terus belajar hal-hal baru, berapa pun usianya."},{"jp":"その仕事が難しいかどうかにかかわらず、彼女は努力し続けた。","romaji":"Sono shigoto ga muzukashii ka dou ka ni kakawarazu, kanojo wa doryoku shi tsuzuketa.","en":"Regardless of whether the job is difficult or not, she continued to make an effort.","id":"Terlepas sulit atau tidaknya pekerjaan itu, ia terus berupaya."},{"jp":"経験の有無にかかわらず、このプログラムは誰でも利用できます。","romaji":"Keiken no umu ni kakawarazu, kono puroguramu wa daredemo riyou dekimasu.","en":"Regardless of experience, this program can be used by anyone.","id":"Terlepas dari pengalamannya, program ini dapat digunakan oleh siapa saja."}]},{"pattern":"～にかけては (〜ni kakete wa)","meaning":"Indicates a specific area or aspect in which someone or something excels.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan bidang atau aspek tertentu di mana seseorang atau sesuatu unggul.","formation":"Noun + にかけては","formationId":"Kata benda + にかけては","examples":[{"jp":"料理の腕前にかけては、彼女は誰にも負けません。","romaji":"Ryouri no udemae ni kakete wa, kanojo wa dare ni mo makemasen.","en":"When it comes to cooking skills, she is second to none.","id":"Dalam hal keterampilan memasak, dia tidak ada duanya."},{"jp":"この町にかけては、彼の店が一番おいしいラーメンを売っています。","romaji":"Kono machi ni kakete wa, kare no mise ga ichiban oishii raamen wo utteimasu.","en":"As far as this town is concerned, his store sells the most delicious ramen.","id":"Sejauh menyangkut kota ini, tokonya menjual ramen paling enak."},{"jp":"音楽の知識にかけては、彼は私たちの中で一番詳しいです。","romaji":"Ongaku no chishiki ni kakete wa, kare wa watashitachi no naka de ichiban kuwashii desu.","en":"When it comes to music knowledge, he is the most knowledgeable among us.","id":"Kalau soal ilmu musik, dialah yang paling berpengetahuan di antara kami."},{"jp":"スポーツにかけては、彼はどんな競技も得意です。","romaji":"Supootsu ni kakete wa, kare wa donna kyogi mo tokui desu.","en":"When it comes to sports, he excels in any competition.","id":"Dalam bidang olahraga, dia unggul dalam kompetisi apa pun."}]},{"pattern":"～にしたがって (〜ni shitagatte)","meaning":"Expresses a natural consequence or a change that occurs according to something else; 'as', 'with', 'in accordance with'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan akibat alami atau perubahan yang terjadi karena sesuatu yang lain; 'sebagai', 'dengan', 'sesuai dengan'.","formation":"Noun + にしたがって","formationId":"Kata benda + にしたがって","examples":[{"jp":"成長にしたがって、この植物の葉が大きくなります。","romaji":"Seichou ni shitagatte, kono shokubutsu no ha ga ookiku narimasu.","en":"As it grows, the leaves of this plant become larger.","id":"Seiring pertumbuhannya, daun tanaman ini semakin besar."},{"jp":"説明書にしたがって、家具を組み立ててください。","romaji":"Setsumeisho ni shitagatte, kagu wo kumitatete kudasai.","en":"Please assemble the furniture according to the instructions.","id":"Silakan merakit furnitur sesuai dengan instruksi."},{"jp":"年齢にしたがって、人の体力は低下します。","romaji":"Nenrei ni shitagatte, hito no tairyoku wa teika shimasu.","en":"As people age, their physical strength declines.","id":"Seiring bertambahnya usia, kekuatan fisik mereka menurun."},{"jp":"運動にしたがって、心拍数が増加することが一般的です。","romaji":"Undou ni shitagatte, shinpakusuu ga zouka suru koto ga ippan teki desu.","en":"It is common for the heart rate to increase with exercise.","id":"Denyut jantung meningkat saat berolahraga adalah hal yang biasa."}]},{"pattern":"～にしたら (〜ni shitara)","meaning":"Express a point of view; 'from the perspective of', 'if I were'.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan sudut pandang; 'dari sudut pandang', 'seandainya aku'.","formation":"Noun + にしたら, Pronoun + にしたら","formationId":"Kata benda + にしたら, Kata ganti + にしたら","examples":[{"jp":"彼にしたら、早く帰りたいだろう。","romaji":"Kare ni shitara, hayaku kaeritai darou.","en":"From his perspective, he probably wants to go home early.","id":"Dari sudut pandangnya, dia mungkin ingin pulang lebih awal."},{"jp":"子供たちにしたら、この話はつまらないかもしれない。","romaji":"Kodomo-tachi ni shitara, kono hanashi wa tsumaranai kamoshirenai.","en":"If I were the children, this story might be boring.","id":"Jika saya masih anak-anak, cerita ini mungkin membosankan."},{"jp":"私にしたら、そのプレゼントは素晴らしいと思います。","romaji":"Watashi ni shitara, sono purezento wa subarashii to omoimasu.","en":"From my perspective, I think that present is wonderful.","id":"Dari sudut pandangku, menurutku hadiah itu luar biasa."},{"jp":"彼女にしたら、この映画が好きではないでしょう。","romaji":"Kanojo ni shitara, kono eiga ga suki dewa nai deshou.","en":"If I were her, I would not like this movie.","id":"Jika saya jadi dia, saya tidak akan menyukai film ini."}]},{"pattern":"～にしろ～にしろ (〜ni shiro 〜ni shiro)","meaning":"Expresses 'either way', 'in any case', 'be it...', used when presenting two alternatives.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan 'bagaimanapun juga', 'dalam hal apapun', 'baiklah...', digunakan ketika menghadirkan dua alternatif.","formation":"Verb (dictionary form or negative form) + にしろ, い-Adjective + にしろ, な-Adjective + にしろ, Noun + にしろ","formationId":"Kata Kerja (bentuk kamus atau bentuk negatif) + にしろ, い-Kata Sifat + にしろ, な-Kata Sifat + にしろ, Kata Benda + にしろ","examples":[{"jp":"行くにしろ行かないにしろ、早く決めてください。","romaji":"Iku ni shiro ikanai ni shiro, hayaku kimete kudasai.","en":"Either way, whether you go or not, please decide quickly.","id":"Apa pun pilihannya, apakah Anda pergi atau tidak, harap putuskan dengan cepat."},{"jp":"彼が来るにしろ来ないにしろ、パーティーは始めましょう。","romaji":"Kare ga kuru ni shiro konai ni shiro, paatii wa hajimemashou.","en":"Be it if he comes or not, let's start the party either way.","id":"Baik dia datang atau tidak, ayo kita mulai pestanya."},{"jp":"雨が降るにしろ降らないにしろ、傘を持って行ったほうがいいです。","romaji":"Ame ga furu ni shiro furanai ni shiro, kasa wo motte itta hou ga ii desu.","en":"Either way, whether it rains or not, it's better to bring an umbrella.","id":"Apapun itu, hujan atau tidak, lebih baik membawa payung."},{"jp":"このレストランが高いにしろ安いにしろ、料理は美味しいです。","romaji":"Kono resutoran ga takai ni shiro yasui ni shiro, ryouri wa oishii desu.","en":"In any case, whether this restaurant is expensive or cheap, the food is delicious.","id":"Bagaimanapun, restoran ini mahal atau murah, makanannya enak."}]},{"pattern":"～につけ～につけ (〜ni tsuke 〜ni tsuke)","meaning":"Expresses 'whenever', 'each time', 'whether...or'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan 'kapanpun', 'setiap waktu', 'apakah...atau'.","formation":"Verb-casual + につけ, い-Adjective + につけ, な-Adjective + につけ, Noun + につけ","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + につけ, い-Kata Sifat + につけ, な-Kata Sifat + につけ, Kata Benda + につけ","examples":[{"jp":"外国へ行くにつけ、勉強するにつけ、言葉の壁にぶつかる。","romaji":"Gaikoku e iku ni tsuke, benkyou suru ni tsuke, kotoba no kabe ni butsukaru.","en":"Whether I go abroad or study, I always encounter language barriers.","id":"Baik saya pergi ke luar negeri atau belajar, saya selalu menemui kendala bahasa."},{"jp":"彼と話すにつけ、彼が考えるにつけ、彼の知識に驚かされる。","romaji":"Kare to hanasu ni tsuke, kare ga kangaeru ni tsuke, kare no chishiki ni odorokasareru.","en":"Whenever I talk to him or hear his thoughts, I'm always amazed by his knowledge.","id":"Setiap kali saya berbicara dengannya atau mendengar pemikirannya, saya selalu kagum dengan pengetahuannya."},{"jp":"この公園で遊ぶにつけ、散歩するにつけ、子供時代を思い出す。","romaji":"Kono kouen de asobu ni tsuke, sanpo suru ni tsuke, kodomo jidai wo omoidasu.","en":"Each time I play or take a walk in this park, it reminds me of my childhood.","id":"Setiap kali saya bermain atau berjalan-jalan di taman ini, saya teringat pada masa kecil saya."},{"jp":"春につけ、秋につけ、彼は母校を訪れる。","romaji":"Haru ni tsuke, aki ni tsuke, kare wa bokou wo otozureru.","en":"Whether in spring or autumn, he visits his alma mater.","id":"Baik di musim semi atau musim gugur, dia mengunjungi almamaternya."}]},{"pattern":"～につれて (〜ni tsurete)","meaning":"Expresses the idea that as one thing changes, so does another; 'as', 'along with', 'while'.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan gagasan bahwa ketika satu hal berubah, hal lain juga berubah; 'sebagai', 'bersama', 'sementara'.","formation":"Verb (dictionary form) + につれて, Noun + につれて","formationId":"Kata Kerja (bentuk kamus) + につれて, Kata Benda + につれて","examples":[{"jp":"年を取るにつれて、健康に気をつけなければなりません。","romaji":"Toshi wo toru ni tsurete, kenkou ni ki wo tsukenakereba narimasen.","en":"As you get older, you have to pay more attention to your health.","id":"Seiring bertambahnya usia, Anda harus lebih memperhatikan kesehatan Anda."},{"jp":"春が近づくにつれて、気温が上がる。","romaji":"Haru ga chikazuku ni tsurete, kion ga agaru.","en":"As spring approaches, the temperature rises.","id":"Saat musim semi mendekat, suhu meningkat."},{"jp":"勉強するにつれて、だんだん分かるようになる。","romaji":"Benkyou suru ni tsurete, dandan wakaru you ni naru.","en":"As I study, I gradually come to understand.","id":"Saat saya belajar, saya perlahan-lahan mulai memahaminya."},{"jp":"経験が増えるにつれて、自信もついてくる。","romaji":"Keiken ga fueru ni tsurete, jishin mo tsuite kuru.","en":"As your experience increases, so does your confidence.","id":"Ketika pengalaman Anda meningkat, kepercayaan diri Anda juga meningkat."}]},{"pattern":"～にともなって (〜ni tomonatte)","meaning":"Expresses 'along with' or 'as a result of'; indicates that one event occurs along with another.","meaningId":"Menyatakan 'bersama dengan' atau 'sebagai akibat dari'; menunjukkan bahwa satu peristiwa terjadi bersamaan dengan peristiwa lainnya.","formation":"Noun (event) + にともなって, Verb-casual + にともなって","formationId":"Kata Benda (peristiwa) + にともなって, Kata kerja kasual + にともなって","examples":[{"jp":"人口が増えるにともなって、交通渋滞も悪化しています。","romaji":"Jinkou ga fueru ni tomonatte, koutsuu juutai mo akka shiteimasu.","en":"As the population increases, traffic congestion is also getting worse.","id":"Seiring bertambahnya jumlah penduduk, kemacetan lalu lintas juga semakin parah."},{"jp":"季節の変わり目にともなって、体調を崩しやすくなります。","romaji":"Kisetsu no kawarime ni tomonatte, taichou wo kuzushi yasuku narimasu.","en":"As the seasons change, it's easier to get out of shape.","id":"Saat musim berganti, bentuk tubuh menjadi lebih mudah."},{"jp":"経済の成長にともなって、雇用の機会も増えるでしょう。","romaji":"Keizai no seichou ni tomonatte, koyou no kikai mo fueru deshou.","en":"As the economy grows, employment opportunities will also increase.","id":"Seiring pertumbuhan ekonomi, kesempatan kerja juga akan meningkat."},{"jp":"彼の昇進にともなって、引っ越しをすることになりました。","romaji":"Kare no shoushin ni tomonatte, hikkoshi wo suru koto ni narimashita.","en":"As a result of his promotion, we decided to move.","id":"Sebagai hasil dari promosinya, kami memutuskan untuk pindah."}]},{"pattern":"～にほかならない (〜ni hoka naranai)","meaning":"Express that something is 'nothing but' or 'none other than'.","meaningId":"Nyatakan bahwa sesuatu itu 'tidak lain hanyalah' atau 'tidak lain adalah'.","formation":"Verb-plain + にほかならない, い-Adjective + にほかならない, な-Adjective + にほかならない, Noun + にほかならない","formationId":"Kata Kerja-biasa + にほかならない, い-Kata Sifat + にほかならない, な-Kata Sifat + にほかならない, Kata Benda +にほかならない","examples":[{"jp":"彼の成功は努力にほかならない。","romaji":"Kare no seikou wa doryoku ni hoka naranai.","en":"His success is nothing but hard work.","id":"Kesuksesannya tak lain adalah kerja keras."},{"jp":"この痛みは寒さにほかならない。","romaji":"Kono itami wa samusa ni hoka naranai.","en":"This pain is nothing but the cold.","id":"Rasa sakit ini tidak lain hanyalah rasa dingin."},{"jp":"彼の失敗の原因は慢心にほかならない。","romaji":"Kare no shippai no gen'in wa manshin ni hoka naranai.","en":"The cause of his failure is nothing but overconfidence.","id":"Penyebab kegagalannya hanyalah rasa percaya diri yang berlebihan."},{"jp":"彼女の笑顔は明るさにほかならない。","romaji":"Kanojo no egao wa akarusa ni hoka naranai.","en":"Her smile is none other than brightness.","id":"Senyumannya tidak lain adalah kecerahan."}]},{"pattern":"～にもかかわらず (〜ni mo kakawarazu)","meaning":"Expresses 'despite', 'in spite of' or 'even though'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan 'meskipun', 'meskipun' atau 'meskipun'.","formation":"Verb (any tense/form) + にもかかわらず, い-Adjective + にもかかわらず, な-Adjective (or Noun) + であるにもかかわらず","formationId":"Kata Kerja (bentuk/waktu apa pun) + にもかかわらず, い-Kata Sifat + にもかかわらず, な-Kata Sifat (atau Kata Benda) + であるにもかかわらず","examples":[{"jp":"忙しいにもかかわらず、彼は毎日運動しています。","romaji":"Isogashii ni mo kakawarazu, kare wa mainichi undou shiteimasu.","en":"Despite being busy, he exercises every day.","id":"Meski sibuk, dia berolahraga setiap hari."},{"jp":"雨が降っているにもかかわらず、彼女は散歩に行きました。","romaji":"Ame ga futteiru ni mo kakawarazu, kanojo wa sanpo ni ikimashita.","en":"Even though it was raining, she went for a walk.","id":"Meski hujan, dia tetap berjalan-jalan."},{"jp":"車が古いにもかかわらず、まだよく走ります。","romaji":"Kuruma ga furui ni mo kakawarazu, mada yoku hashirimasu.","en":"In spite of the car being old, it still runs well.","id":"Walaupun mobilnya sudah tua, namun masih bisa berjalan dengan baik."},{"jp":"結果が良くないにもかかわらず、彼は頑張り続けました。","romaji":"Kekka ga yoku nai ni mo kakawarazu, kare wa ganbari tsuzukemashita.","en":"Despite the results not being good, he continued to do his best.","id":"Meski hasilnya kurang bagus, ia terus berupaya semaksimal mungkin."}]},{"pattern":"～により (〜ni yori)","meaning":"Indicates the reason, method, or means by which something happens; 'by', 'through', 'due to'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan alasan, metode, atau cara terjadinya sesuatu; 'oleh', 'melalui', 'karena'.","formation":"Noun + により, Verb + により","formationId":"Kata Benda + により, Kata Kerja + により","examples":[{"jp":"この事故は運転手の不注意により起こりました。","romaji":"Kono jiko wa untenshu no fuchuui ni yori okorimashita.","en":"This accident occurred due to the driver's carelessness.","id":"Kecelakaan ini terjadi karena kecerobohan pengemudi."},{"jp":"その映画は小説により制作されました。","romaji":"Sono eiga wa shousetsu ni yori seisaku saremashita.","en":"The movie was produced based on the novel.","id":"Film ini diproduksi berdasarkan novel."},{"jp":"犯人は警察により逮捕されました。","romaji":"Hannin wa keisatsu ni yori taiho saremashita.","en":"The criminal was arrested by the police.","id":"Penjahat itu ditangkap polisi."},{"jp":"会社の成長は従業員の努力により実現しました。","romaji":"Kaisha no seichou wa juugyouin no doryoku ni yori jitsugen shimashita.","en":"The company's growth was achieved through the efforts of its employees.","id":"Pertumbuhan perusahaan dicapai melalui upaya para karyawannya."}]},{"pattern":"～にわたって (〜ni watatte)","meaning":"Indicates a range or extent; 'over', 'throughout', 'across'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan rentang atau luasnya; 'di atas', 'sepanjang', 'di seberang'.","formation":"Noun + にわたって","formationId":"Kata benda + にわたって","examples":[{"jp":"彼女は一年にわたって日本語を勉強しました。","romaji":"Kanojo wa ichinen ni watatte nihongo wo benkyou shimashita.","en":"She studied Japanese for over a year.","id":"Dia belajar bahasa Jepang selama lebih dari setahun."},{"jp":"このプロジェクトは50キロにわたって道路を建設します。","romaji":"Kono purojekuto wa gojukiro ni watatte douro wo kensetsu shimasu.","en":"This project will construct roads across 50 kilometers.","id":"Proyek ini akan membangun jalan sepanjang 50 kilometer."},{"jp":"彼の著作は数多くの国にわたって読まれている。","romaji":"Kare no chosaku wa kazu ooku no kuni ni watatte yomarete iru.","en":"His writings are read throughout numerous countries.","id":"Tulisannya dibaca di banyak negara."},{"jp":"その秘密は世代にわたって保たれ続けた。","romaji":"Sono himitsu wa sedai ni watatte tamotsu sareta.","en":"The secret was kept over generations.","id":"Rahasianya disimpan selama beberapa generasi."}]},{"pattern":"～に先立ち (〜ni sakidachi)","meaning":"Express an action or event that occurs before another; 'before', 'prior to', 'preceding'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan suatu tindakan atau peristiwa yang terjadi sebelum tindakan atau peristiwa lainnya; 'sebelum', 'sebelum', 'sebelumnya'.","formation":"Noun + に先立ち / Verb-dictionary form + に先立って","formationId":"Kata benda + に先立ち / Bentuk kamus kata kerja + に先立って","examples":[{"jp":"会議に先立ち、資料を確認しましょう。","romaji":"Kaigi ni sakidachi, shiryou wo kakunin shimashou.","en":"Before the meeting, let's check the materials.","id":"Sebelum pertemuan, mari kita periksa materinya."},{"jp":"出発に先立ち、荷物を整理しました。","romaji":"Shuppatsu ni sakidachi, nimotsu wo seiri shimashita.","en":"Before departure, I organized my luggage.","id":"Sebelum berangkat, saya mengatur barang bawaan saya."},{"jp":"就寝に先立ち、歯を磨きます。","romaji":"Shuushin ni sakidachi, ha wo migakimasu.","en":"Before going to bed, I brush my teeth.","id":"Sebelum tidur, saya menyikat gigi."},{"jp":"映画の上映に先立ち、予告編が放映されます。","romaji":"Eiga no jouei ni sakidachi, yokokuhen ga houei saremasu.","en":"Before the movie screening, the trailers are shown.","id":"Sebelum pemutaran film, trailernya ditampilkan."}]},{"pattern":"～に反して (〜ni hanshite)","meaning":"Contrary to, against, in spite of","meaningId":"Bertentangan dengan, menentang, meskipun demikian","formation":"Noun + に反して","formationId":"Kata benda + に反して","examples":[{"jp":"天気予報に反して、今日は雨が降っている。","romaji":"Tenki yohou ni hanshite, kyou wa ame ga futte iru.","en":"Contrary to the weather forecast, it is raining today.","id":"Bertentangan dengan ramalan cuaca, hari ini hujan turun."},{"jp":"彼の予想に反して、試合に勝った。","romaji":"Kare no yosou ni hanshite, shiai ni katta.","en":"We won the match against his prediction.","id":"Kami memenangkan pertandingan melawan prediksinya."},{"jp":"両親の意見に反して、彼と結婚した。","romaji":"Ryoushin no iken ni hanshite, kare to kekkon shita.","en":"I married him against my parents' opinion.","id":"Saya menikah dengannya bertentangan dengan pendapat orang tua saya."},{"jp":"この映画は批評家の評価に反して大ヒットした。","romaji":"Kono eiga wa hihyouka no hyouka ni hanshite daihitto shita.","en":"This movie became a big hit contrary to the critics' ratings.","id":"Film ini menjadi sukses besar bertentangan dengan rating para kritikus."}]},{"pattern":"～に基づいて (〜ni motozuite)","meaning":"Based on, according to, depending on","meaningId":"Berdasarkan, menurut, tergantung pada","formation":"Noun + に基づいて","formationId":"Kata benda + に基づいて","examples":[{"jp":"研究結果に基づいて、新しい治療法が開発されました。","romaji":"Kenkyuu kekka ni motozuite, atarashii chiryouhou ga kaihatsu saremashita.","en":"A new treatment method was developed based on the research results.","id":"Metode pengobatan baru dikembangkan berdasarkan hasil penelitian."},{"jp":"法律に基づいて、犯罪者は逮捕されました。","romaji":"Houritsu ni motozuite, hanzaisha wa taiho saremashita.","en":"The criminal was arrested according to the law.","id":"Penjahat ditangkap sesuai hukum."},{"jp":"そのデータに基づいて、結論を出すことができます。","romaji":"Sono deeta ni motozuite, ketsuron o dasu koto ga dekimasu.","en":"We can draw conclusions based on that data.","id":"Kita bisa menarik kesimpulan berdasarkan data itu."},{"jp":"お客様の要望に基づいて、商品の改善が行われます。","romaji":"Okyakusama no youbou ni motozuite, shouhin no kaizen ga okonawaremasu.","en":"Product improvements will be made based on customer requests.","id":"Penyempurnaan produk akan dilakukan berdasarkan permintaan pelanggan."}]},{"pattern":"～に対して (〜ni taishite)","meaning":"Expresses 'toward', 'against', 'in contrast to', or 'in response to'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan 'ke arah', 'menentang', 'berlawanan dengan', atau 'menanggapi'.","formation":"Noun + に対して","formationId":"Kata benda + に対して","examples":[{"jp":"日本の文化に対して尊敬の念を持っています。","romaji":"Nihon no bunka ni taishite sonkei no nen wo motte imasu.","en":"I have a sense of respect towards Japanese culture.","id":"Saya memiliki rasa hormat terhadap budaya Jepang."},{"jp":"彼に対して無礼な態度を取らないでください。","romaji":"Kare ni taishite burei na taido wo toranaide kudasai.","en":"Please don't have a rude attitude towards him.","id":"Tolong jangan bersikap kasar padanya."},{"jp":"先生の質問に対して、彼女はすぐに答えました。","romaji":"Sensei no shitsumon ni taishite, kanojo wa sugu ni kotaemashita.","en":"In response to the teacher's question, she answered immediately.","id":"Menanggapi pertanyaan guru, dia langsung menjawab."},{"jp":"男性に対して、女性は同じ仕事でも低い給料をもらっている。","romaji":"Dansei ni taishite, josei wa onaji shigoto demo hikui kyuuryou wo moratte iru.","en":"In contrast to men, women receive lower salaries for the same job.","id":"Berbeda dengan laki-laki, perempuan menerima gaji lebih rendah untuk pekerjaan yang sama."}]},{"pattern":"～に応えて (〜ni kotaete)","meaning":"Responding to; living up to; meeting.","meaningId":"Menanggapi; memenuhi; pertemuan.","formation":"Noun + に応えて","formationId":"Kata benda + に応えて","examples":[{"jp":"お客様の要望に応えて、新しいメニューを作りました。","romaji":"Okyaku-sama no youbou ni kotaete, atarashii menyuu o tsukurimashita.","en":"Responding to the customers' requests, we created a new menu.","id":"Menanggapi permintaan pelanggan, kami membuat menu baru."},{"jp":"彼はチームの期待に応えて素晴らしいプレーを見せた。","romaji":"Kare wa chiimu no kitai ni kotaete, subarashii puree o miseta.","en":"He lived up to the team's expectations and showed a great performance.","id":"Dia memenuhi harapan tim dan menunjukkan kinerja yang luar biasa."},{"jp":"政府は国民の声に応えて、新しい法律を制定した。","romaji":"Seifu wa kokumin no koe ni kotaete, atarashii houritsu o seitei shita.","en":"The government enacted a new law in response to the voice of the people.","id":"Pemerintah memberlakukan undang-undang baru sebagai tanggapan atas suara rakyat."},{"jp":"企業は環境問題に応えて、環境に優しい製品を開発している。","romaji":"Kigyou wa kankyou mondai ni kotaete, kankyou ni yasashii seihin o kaihatsu shite iru.","en":"Companies are developing environmentally friendly products in response to environmental issues.","id":"Perusahaan mengembangkan produk ramah lingkungan sebagai respons terhadap masalah lingkungan."}]},{"pattern":"～に応じて (〜ni oujite)","meaning":"In accordance with, depending on, in response to.","meaningId":"Sesuai dengan, tergantung pada, sebagai tanggapan terhadap.","formation":"Noun + に応じて","formationId":"Kata benda + に応じて","examples":[{"jp":"仕事の量に応じて給料が変わります。","romaji":"Shigoto no ryou ni oujite kyuuryou ga kawarimasu.","en":"The salary changes depending on the amount of work.","id":"Gaji berubah tergantung pada jumlah pekerjaan."},{"jp":"季節に応じて服装を選びましょう。","romaji":"Kisetsu ni oujite fukusou wo erabimashou.","en":"Choose your clothes according to the season.","id":"Pilih pakaian Anda sesuai musim."},{"jp":"お客様の希望に応じてプランを提案します。","romaji":"Okyakusama no kibou ni oujite puran wo teian shimasu.","en":"We propose plans according to the customers' wishes.","id":"Kami mengusulkan rencana sesuai dengan keinginan pelanggan."},{"jp":"年齢に応じて健康診断項目が異なります。","romaji":"Nenrei ni oujite kenkou shindan koumoku ga kotonarimasu.","en":"Health check items vary depending on age.","id":"Item pemeriksaan kesehatan berbeda-beda tergantung usia."}]},{"pattern":"～に決まっている (〜ni kimatte iru)","meaning":"Express certainty; 'it is obvious', 'it must be', 'no doubt'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan kepastian; 'sudah jelas', 'pasti ada', 'tidak diragukan lagi'.","formation":"Verb-casual + に決まっている, い-Adjective + に決まっている, な-Adjective + だに決まっている, Noun + だに決まっている","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + に決まっている, い-Kata Sifat + に決まっている, な-Kata Sifat + だに決まっている, Kata Benda +だに決まっている","examples":[{"jp":"こんなに暑い日に運動したら、汗をかくに決まっている。","romaji":"Konna ni atsui hi ni undou shitara, ase wo kaku ni kimatte iru.","en":"It's obvious that you'll sweat if you exercise on such a hot day.","id":"Pastinya Anda akan berkeringat jika berolahraga di hari yang panas."},{"jp":"彼が試験に落ちたら、がっかりするに決まっている。","romaji":"Kare ga shiken ni ochitara, gakkari suru ni kimatte iru.","en":"If he fails the exam, it's obvious he will be disappointed.","id":"Jika dia gagal dalam ujian, jelas dia akan kecewa."},{"jp":"彼女はいつも遅れるから、今日も遅れるに決まっている。","romaji":"Kanojo wa itsumo okureru kara, kyou mo okureru ni kimatte iru.","en":"She's always late, so it's obvious she'll be late today too.","id":"Dia selalu terlambat, jadi jelas dia akan terlambat hari ini juga."},{"jp":"このゲームは楽しいに決まっている。","romaji":"Kono geemu wa tanoshii ni kimatte iru.","en":"It's obvious that this game is fun.","id":"Yang jelas game ini seru."}]},{"pattern":"～に沿って (〜ni sotte)","meaning":"Along with; in accordance with; following","meaningId":"Seiring dengan; menurut; mengikuti","formation":"Noun + に沿って","formationId":"Kata benda + に沿って","examples":[{"jp":"川に沿って歩いていくと、橋が見えてきます。","romaji":"Kawa ni sotte aruite iku to, hashi ga miete kimasu.","en":"If you walk along the river, you will see a bridge.","id":"Jika Anda berjalan di sepanjang sungai, Anda akan melihat sebuah jembatan."},{"jp":"このレシピに沿って料理を作れば、間違いありません。","romaji":"Kono reshipi ni sotte ryouri wo tsukureba, machigai arimasen.","en":"If you cook according to this recipe, there will be no mistakes.","id":"Jika Anda memasak sesuai resep ini, tidak akan ada kesalahan."},{"jp":"規則に沿って行動しなければなりません。","romaji":"Kisoku ni sotte koudou shinakereba narimasen.","en":"We must act in accordance with the rules.","id":"Kita harus bertindak sesuai dengan aturan."},{"jp":"山道に沿って進むと、小さな神社があります。","romaji":"Yamamichi ni sotte susumu to, chiisana jinja ga arimasu.","en":"If you follow the mountain path, there is a small shrine.","id":"Jika Anda mengikuti jalur pegunungan, ada sebuah kuil kecil."}]},{"pattern":"～に過ぎない (〜ni suginai)","meaning":"Expresses that something is 'just' or 'nothing more than'; 'merely', 'only', 'simply'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan bahwa sesuatu itu 'adil' atau 'tidak lebih dari'; 'hanya', 'hanya', 'sederhana'.","formation":"Verb-casual + に過ぎない, い-Adjective + に過ぎない, な-Adjective + に過ぎない, Noun + に過ぎない","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + に過ぎない, い-Kata Sifat + に過ぎない, な-Kata Sifat + に過ぎない, Kata Benda + に過ぎない","examples":[{"jp":"彼の失敗はミスに過ぎない。","romaji":"Kare no shippai wa misu ni suginai.","en":"His failure is nothing more than a mistake.","id":"Kegagalannya tidak lebih dari sebuah kesalahan."},{"jp":"この試験は簡単な問題に過ぎない。","romaji":"Kono shiken wa kantan na mondai ni suginai.","en":"This test is nothing more than a simple question.","id":"Tes ini tidak lebih dari sebuah pertanyaan sederhana."},{"jp":"彼女は友達に過ぎない。","romaji":"Kanojo wa tomodachi ni suginai.","en":"She is nothing more than a friend.","id":"Dia tidak lebih dari seorang teman."},{"jp":"その発言は冗談に過ぎない。","romaji":"Sono hatsugen wa joudan ni suginai.","en":"That remark is nothing more than a joke.","id":"Ucapan itu tidak lebih dari sebuah lelucon."}]},{"pattern":"～に関わって (〜ni kakawatte)","meaning":"Indicates that something is related to or influenced by a certain matter or factor; 'concerning', 'in connection with', 'regarding'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan bahwa sesuatu berkaitan atau dipengaruhi oleh suatu hal atau faktor tertentu; 'mengenai', 'sehubungan dengan', 'mengenai'.","formation":"Verb-casual + に関わって, い-Adjective + に関わって, な-Adjective + に関わって, Noun + に関わって","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + に関わって, い-Kata Sifat + に関わって, な-Kata Sifat + に関わって, Kata Benda + に関わって","examples":[{"jp":"試験の内容に関わって、先生に質問があります。","romaji":"Shiken no naiyou ni kakawatte, sensei ni shitsumon ga arimasu.","en":"I have a question for the teacher regarding the content of the exam.","id":"Saya punya pertanyaan untuk guru mengenai isi ujian."},{"jp":"このプロジェクトに関わって、意見があれば、遠慮なく言ってください。","romaji":"Kono purojekuto ni kakawatte, iken ga areba, enryo naku itte kudasai.","en":"If you have any opinions regarding this project, please feel free to express them.","id":"Jika Anda memiliki pendapat mengenai proyek ini, silakan ungkapkan."},{"jp":"健康に関わって、食生活はとても重要です。","romaji":"Kenkou ni kakawatte, shokuseikatsu wa totemo juuyou desu.","en":"Regarding health, dietary habits are very important.","id":"Dalam bidang kesehatan, pola makan sangatlah penting."},{"jp":"その事件に関わって、彼も少し疑われています。","romaji":"Sono jiken ni kakawatte, kare mo sukoshi utagawarete imasu.","en":"He is also somewhat suspected in connection with the incident.","id":"Dia juga agak dicurigai terkait dengan insiden tersebut."}]},{"pattern":"～に限り (〜ni kagiri)","meaning":"Expresses limitation; 'only', 'limited to', 'exclusive to'.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan batasan; 'hanya', 'terbatas pada', 'eksklusif pada'.","formation":"Noun + に限り","formationId":"Kata benda + に限り","examples":[{"jp":"今日に限り、この商品が半額です。","romaji":"Kyou ni kagiri, kono shouhin ga hangaku desu.","en":"Today only, this product is half price.","id":"Hanya saat ini, produk ini setengah harga."},{"jp":"このクーポンはこの店に限り有効です。","romaji":"Kono kuupon wa kono mise ni kagiri yuukou desu.","en":"This coupon is valid only at this store.","id":"Kupon ini hanya berlaku di toko ini."},{"jp":"会員に限り、無料でこのサービスを利用できます。","romaji":"Kaiin ni kagiri, muryou de kono saabisu wo riyou dekimasu.","en":"Only members can use this service for free.","id":"Hanya anggota yang dapat menggunakan layanan ini secara gratis."},{"jp":"この特典は先着10名に限ります。","romaji":"Kono tokuten wa senchaku 10-mei ni kagirimasu.","en":"This benefit is limited to the first 10 people.","id":"Benefit ini terbatas untuk 10 orang pertama."}]},{"pattern":"～に際して (〜ni saishite)","meaning":"Used to express the moment or the occasion of an action; 'at the time of', 'upon', 'when'.","meaningId":"Digunakan untuk menyatakan momen atau peristiwa suatu tindakan; 'pada saat', 'pada', 'kapan'.","formation":"Noun + に際して","formationId":"Kata benda + に際して","examples":[{"jp":"卒業式に際して、校長先生がスピーチをします。","romaji":"Sotsugyoushiki ni saishite, kouchou sensei ga supiichi wo shimasu.","en":"At the graduation ceremony, the principal gives a speech.","id":"Pada acara wisuda, kepala sekolah memberikan sambutan."},{"jp":"この仕事に際して、責任感が大切です。","romaji":"Kono shigoto ni saishite, sekininkan ga taisetsu desu.","en":"Responsibility is important when doing this job.","id":"Tanggung jawab penting ketika melakukan pekerjaan ini."},{"jp":"留学に際して、ビザの手続きが必要です。","romaji":"Ryuugaku ni saishite, biza no tetsuzuki ga hitsuyou desu.","en":"Visa procedures are necessary when studying abroad.","id":"Prosedur visa diperlukan ketika belajar di luar negeri."},{"jp":"結婚式に際して、両親に感謝の気持ちを伝えました。","romaji":"Kekkonshiki ni saishite, ryoushin ni kansha no kimochi wo tsutaemashita.","en":"At the time of the wedding ceremony, I conveyed my gratitude to my parents.","id":"Pada saat upacara pernikahan, saya menyampaikan rasa terima kasih saya kepada orang tua saya."}]},{"pattern":"～ねばならない (〜neba naranai)","meaning":"Expresses obligation or necessity; 'must', 'have to', 'need to'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan kewajiban atau kebutuhan; 'harus', 'harus', 'perlu'.","formation":"Verb-ない form → (remove い) → ね + ばならない","formationId":"Bentuk kata kerja-ない → (hapus い) → ね + ばならない","examples":[{"jp":"試験に合格するために、もっと勉強せねばならない。","romaji":"Shiken ni goukaku suru tame ni, motto benkyou se neba naranai.","en":"To pass the exam, I must study more.","id":"Untuk lulus ujian, saya harus belajar lebih banyak."},{"jp":"飛行機に間に合うためには、急がねばならない。","romaji":"Hikouki ni maniau tame ni wa, isoga neba naranai.","en":"To catch the flight, I must hurry.","id":"Untuk mengejar penerbangan, saya harus bergegas."},{"jp":"６時までに帰らねばならない。","romaji":"Roku ji made ni kaera neba naranai.","en":"I have to go home by 6 o'clock.","id":"Aku harus pulang jam 6 sore."},{"jp":"この仕事を今日中に終わらせねばならない。","romaji":"Kono shigoto wo kyoujuu ni owarase neba naranai.","en":"I need to finish this work by the end of the day.","id":"Saya harus menyelesaikan pekerjaan ini pada penghujung hari."}]},{"pattern":"～のみならず～も (〜nomi narazu 〜mo)","meaning":"Not only... but also; as well as.","meaningId":"Tidak hanya... tetapi juga; maupun.","formation":"Verb-casual + のみならず + (も), い-Adjective + のみならず + (も), な-Adjective + のみならず + (も), Noun + のみならず + (も)","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + のみならず + (も), い-Kata Sifat + のみならず + (も), な-Kata Sifat + のみならず + (も), Kata Benda + のみならず + (も)","examples":[{"jp":"彼は英語のみならず、フランス語も話せます。","romaji":"Kare wa eigo nomi narazu, furansugo mo hanasemasu.","en":"He can speak not only English but also French.","id":"Dia tidak hanya bisa berbicara bahasa Inggris tetapi juga bahasa Prancis."},{"jp":"このレストランは美味しいのみならず、雰囲気も素晴らしいです。","romaji":"Kono resutoran wa oishii nomi narazu, fun'iki mo subarashii desu.","en":"Not only is this restaurant delicious, but the atmosphere is also great.","id":"Restoran ini tidak hanya enak, tapi suasananya juga enak."},{"jp":"このアプリは便利のみならず、安全性も高いです。","romaji":"Kono apuri wa benri nomi narazu, anzen-sei mo takai desu.","en":"This app is not only convenient but also highly secure.","id":"Aplikasi ini tidak hanya nyaman tetapi juga sangat aman."},{"jp":"彼女は頭が良いのみならず、スポーツも得意です。","romaji":"Kanojo wa atama ga ii nomi narazu, supootsu mo tokui desu.","en":"She is not only smart but also good at sports.","id":"Dia tidak hanya pintar tetapi juga pandai olahraga."}]},{"pattern":"～のももっともだ (〜no mo mottomo da)","meaning":"Express that something is understandable or reasonable.","meaningId":"Nyatakan bahwa sesuatu dapat dimengerti atau masuk akal.","formation":"Verb-casual + のももっともだ, い-Adjective + のももっともだ, な-Adjective + なのももっともだ, Noun + なのももっともだ","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + のももっともだ, い-Kata Sifat + のももっともだ, な-Kata Sifat + なのももっともだ, Kata Benda +なのももっともだ","examples":[{"jp":"彼が緊張するのももっともだ。","romaji":"Kare ga kinchou suru no mo mottomo da.","en":"It's understandable that he is nervous.","id":"Wajar kalau dia gugup."},{"jp":"この問題が難しいのももっともだ。","romaji":"Kono mondai ga muzukashii no mo mottomo da.","en":"It's reasonable that this problem is difficult.","id":"Wajar jika masalah ini sulit."},{"jp":"彼女が幸せなのももっともだ。","romaji":"Kanojo ga shiawase na no mo mottomo da.","en":"It's understandable that she is happy.","id":"Wajar jika dia bahagia."},{"jp":"彼がリーダーなのももっともだ。","romaji":"Kare ga riidaa na no mo mottomo da.","en":"It's reasonable that he is the leader.","id":"Wajar jika dialah pemimpinnya."}]},{"pattern":"〜の上では (〜no ue de wa)","meaning":"Indicates 'on the basis of', 'in terms of', or 'from the standpoint of'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan 'berdasarkan', 'dalam istilah', atau 'dari sudut pandang'.","formation":"Noun or Phrase + の上では","formationId":"Kata Benda atau Frasa + の上では","examples":[{"jp":"効率の上では、この方法が最適です。","romaji":"Kouritsu no ue de wa, kono houhou ga saiteki desu.","en":"In terms of efficiency, this method is the best.","id":"Dari segi efisiensi, cara ini adalah yang terbaik."},{"jp":"法律の上では、彼の行為は違法ではありません。","romaji":"Houritsu no ue de wa, kare no koui wa ihan dewa arimasen.","en":"From a legal standpoint, his actions are not illegal.","id":"Dari segi hukum, perbuatannya tidak melanggar hukum."},{"jp":"味の上では、このレストランは評価が高いです。","romaji":"Aji no ue de wa, kono resutoran wa hyouka ga takai desu.","en":"In terms of taste, this restaurant has a high rating.","id":"Dari segi rasa, restoran ini memiliki rating yang tinggi."},{"jp":"成績の上では、彼はクラスで一番優秀です。","romaji":"Seiseki no ue de wa, kare wa kurasu de ichiban yuushuu desu.","en":"On the basis of grades, he is the most outstanding student in the class.","id":"Berdasarkan nilai, dia adalah siswa paling berprestasi di kelas."}]},{"pattern":"～の下で (〜no shita de)","meaning":"Under the context or condition of; under.","meaningId":"Dalam konteks atau kondisi; di bawah.","formation":"Verb-casual + の下で, い-Adjective + の下で, な-Adjective + の下で, Noun + の下で","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + の下で, い-Kata Sifat + の下で, な-Kata Sifat + の下で, Kata Benda + の下で","examples":[{"jp":"先生の下で勉強するのはとても楽しいです。","romaji":"Sensei no shita de benkyou suru no wa totemo tanoshii desu.","en":"Studying under the teacher is very enjoyable.","id":"Belajar di bawah bimbingan guru sangat menyenangkan."},{"jp":"晴天の下でピクニックをしましょう。","romaji":"Seiten no shita de pikunikku wo shimashou.","en":"Let's have a picnic under the clear sky.","id":"Ayo piknik di bawah langit cerah."},{"jp":"緊張感の下で、彼女はスピーチに成功しました。","romaji":"Kinchoukan no shita de, kanojo wa supiichi ni seikou shimashita.","en":"Under pressure, she succeeded in her speech.","id":"Di bawah tekanan, dia berhasil menyampaikan pidatonya."},{"jp":"親の愛情の下で、子供たちは幸せに育ちます。","romaji":"Oya no aijou no shita de, kodomo-tachi wa shiawase ni sodachimasu.","en":"Under the love of their parents, children grow up happily.","id":"Di bawah kasih sayang orang tuanya, anak-anak tumbuh dengan bahagia."}]},{"pattern":"～ばかりか〜も (〜bakari ka 〜 mo)","meaning":"Expresses 'not only... but also'; emphasizing the extent of something.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan 'tidak hanya... tetapi juga'; menekankan sejauh mana sesuatu.","formation":"Noun/Verb/Adjective + ばかりか + Noun/Verb/Adjective + も","formationId":"Kata Benda/Kata Kerja/Kata Sifat + ばかりか + Kata Benda/Kata Kerja/Kata Sifat + も","examples":[{"jp":"彼はかわいいばかりか、賢くもある。","romaji":"Kare wa kawaii bakari ka, kashikoku mo aru.","en":"He is not only cute but also smart.","id":"Dia tidak hanya lucu tapi juga pintar."},{"jp":"このレストランは味が良いばかりかサービスも素晴らしいです。","romaji":"Kono resutoran wa aji ga yoi bakari ka saabisu mo subarashii desu.","en":"This restaurant not only has great taste but also wonderful service.","id":"Restoran ini tidak hanya memiliki cita rasa yang enak tetapi juga layanan yang luar biasa."},{"jp":"彼女は日本語が上手ばかりか英語も話せる。","romaji":"Kanojo wa nihongo ga jouzu bakari ka eigo mo hanaseru.","en":"She can speak not only Japanese but also English.","id":"Dia tidak hanya bisa berbicara bahasa Jepang tetapi juga bahasa Inggris."},{"jp":"彼は歌が上手いばかりかダンスもうまい。","romaji":"Kare wa uta ga umai bakari ka dansu mo umai.","en":"He is not only good at singing but also dancing.","id":"Ia tidak hanya pandai menyanyi tapi juga menari."}]},{"pattern":"～ばかりだ (〜bakari da)","meaning":"Express a continuing state or negative tendency; 'just', 'only', 'always'.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan keadaan berkelanjutan atau kecenderungan negatif; 'hanya', 'hanya', 'selalu'.","formation":"Verb-てform + ばかりだ, い-Adjective + ばかりだ, な-Adjective + ばかりだ, Noun + ばかりだ","formationId":"Kata Kerja-てbentuk + ばかりだ, い-Kata Sifat + ばかりだ, な-Kata Sifat + ばかりだ, Kata Benda + ばかりだ","examples":[{"jp":"彼は文句を言ってばかりだ。","romaji":"Kare wa monku wo itte bakari da.","en":"He is always complaining.","id":"Dia selalu mengeluh."},{"jp":"この映画は面白くなくて、退屈してばかりだ。","romaji":"Kono eiga wa omoshirokunakute, taikutsu shite bakari da.","en":"This movie isn't interesting, and I'm just bored.","id":"Film ini tidak menarik, dan saya hanya bosan."},{"jp":"彼女は暇でいるばかりだ。","romaji":"Kanojo wa hima de iru bakari da.","en":"She is always just idling around with nothing to do.","id":"Dia selalu bermalas-malasan tanpa melakukan apa pun."},{"jp":"最近、仕事の失敗ばかりだ。","romaji":"Saikin, shigoto no shippai bakari da.","en":"Lately, it’s just been one failure at work after another.","id":"Akhir-akhir ini, yang terjadi hanyalah kegagalan dalam pekerjaan."}]},{"pattern":"～ばかりに (〜bakari ni)","meaning":"Express an undesired situation or result caused by something; 'simply because', 'due to', 'on account of'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan situasi atau akibat yang tidak diinginkan yang disebabkan oleh sesuatu; 'hanya karena', 'karena', 'karena'.","formation":"Verb-casual + ばかりに, い-Adjective + ばかりに, な-Adjective + なばかりに, Noun + なばかりに","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + ばかりに, い-Kata Sifat + ばかりに, な-Kata Sifat + なばかりに, Kata Benda + なばかりに","examples":[{"jp":"雨が降ったばかりに、試合が中止になりました。","romaji":"Ame ga futta bakari ni, shiai ga chuushi ni narimashita.","en":"Simply because it rained, the match was cancelled.","id":"Hanya karena hujan, pertandingan dibatalkan."},{"jp":"彼が遅れたばかりに、私たちも遅刻しました。","romaji":"Kare ga okureta bakari ni, watashitachi mo chikoku shimashita.","en":"Because he was late, we ended up being late too.","id":"Karena dia terlambat, akhirnya kami pun terlambat."},{"jp":"忘れ物をしたばかりに、買い物に戻らなければなりません。","romaji":"Wasuremono wo shita bakari ni, kaimono ni modoranakereba narimasen.","en":"Simply because I forgot something, I have to go back to the store.","id":"Hanya karena saya lupa sesuatu, saya harus kembali ke toko."},{"jp":"彼女が美人なばかりに、みんなが彼女を羨んでいます。","romaji":"Kanojo ga bijin na bakari ni, minna ga kanojo wo urayande imasu.","en":"Just because she is beautiful, everyone is envious of her.","id":"Hanya karena dia cantik, semua orang iri padanya."}]},{"pattern":"～ば～というものでもない (〜ba 〜to iu mono demo nai)","meaning":"Not necessarily true that if A, then B.","meaningId":"Belum tentu benar jika A, maka B.","formation":"Verb-ば form + というものでもない","formationId":"Bentuk kata kerja-ば + というものでもない","examples":[{"jp":"高いものがいいものばかりではない。","romaji":"Takai mono ga ii mono bakari de wa nai.","en":"Expensive things are not always good.","id":"Barang mahal tidak selalu bagus."},{"jp":"英語ができれば、成功するというものでもない。","romaji":"Eigo ga dekireba, seikou suru to iu mono demo nai.","en":"Just because you can speak English doesn’t mean you’ll succeed.","id":"Hanya karena Anda bisa berbahasa Inggris bukan berarti Anda akan sukses."},{"jp":"見た目が美しいからといって、心も美しいというものでもない。","romaji":"Mitame ga utsukushii kara to itte, kokoro mo utsukushii to iu mono demo nai.","en":"Just because someone is beautiful on the outside, it doesn’t mean they’re beautiful on the inside.","id":"Hanya karena seseorang cantik di luar, bukan berarti dia cantik di dalam."},{"jp":"有名大学に入れば、将来が安泰だというものでもない。","romaji":"Yuumei daigaku ni haireba, shourai ga antai da to iu mono demo nai.","en":"Getting into a famous university doesn’t guarantee a secure future.","id":"Masuk universitas terkenal tidak menjamin masa depan yang aman."}]},{"pattern":"～はともかく～は (〜wa tomokaku 〜wa)","meaning":"Used to compare or contrast two elements; 'as for...'.","meaningId":"Digunakan untuk membandingkan atau membedakan dua elemen; 'Adapun...'.","formation":"Noun1 はともかく Noun2 は","formationId":"Kata Benda1 はともかく Kata Benda2 は","examples":[{"jp":"デザインはともかく、機能はこの携帯電話が一番です。","romaji":"Dezain wa tomokaku, kinou wa kono keitai denwa ga ichiban desu.","en":"As for design, the functionality of this phone is the best.","id":"Dari segi desain, fungsionalitas ponsel ini adalah yang terbaik."},{"jp":"彼の容姿はともかく、性格は素晴らしいです。","romaji":"Kare no youshi wa tomokaku, seikaku wa subarashii desu.","en":"Putting aside his looks, his personality is wonderful.","id":"Mengesampingkan penampilannya, kepribadiannya luar biasa."},{"jp":"料理の味はともかく、盛り付けは綺麗です。","romaji":"Ryouri no aji wa tomokaku, moritsuke wa kirei desu.","en":"Putting aside the taste of the food, the presentation is beautiful.","id":"Terlepas dari rasa makanannya, penyajiannya juga indah."},{"jp":"値段はともかく、このバッグの質は良いです。","romaji":"Nedan wa tomokaku, kono baggu no shitsu wa yoi desu.","en":"Ignoring the price, this bag’s quality is good.","id":"Terlepas dari harganya, kualitas tas ini bagus."}]},{"pattern":"～はまだしも (〜wa mada shimo)","meaning":"Expresses that while the first item is somewhat acceptable, the second item is not.","meaningId":"Menyatakan bahwa walaupun item pertama dapat diterima, item kedua tidak.","formation":"Noun1 + はまだしも + Noun2","formationId":"Kata Benda1 + はまだしも + Kata Benda2","examples":[{"jp":"失敗するのはまだしも、やらないで後悔する方がつらい。","romaji":"Shippai suru no wa mada shimo, yaranai de koukai suru hou ga tsurai.","en":"Failing is one thing, but regretting not even trying is worse.","id":"Gagal adalah satu hal, tapi menyesal bahkan tidak mencoba adalah hal yang lebih buruk."},{"jp":"このピザは野菜が少ないのはまだしも、味も悪い。","romaji":"Kono piza wa yasai ga sukunai no wa mada shimo, aji mo warui.","en":"It’s not just that this pizza has few vegetables, it also tastes bad.","id":"Bukan hanya karena sayurannya sedikit, pizza ini juga rasanya tidak enak."},{"jp":"たまに遅刻するのはまだしも、連絡もせずに遅刻するのは許せない。","romaji":"Tama ni chikoku suru no wa mada shimo, renraku mo sezu ni chikoku suru no wa yurusenai.","en":"Being late occasionally might be forgivable, but being late without any contact is unacceptable.","id":"Terlambat sesekali mungkin bisa dimaafkan, tapi terlambat tanpa kontak apa pun tidak bisa diterima."},{"jp":"難しい質問に答えられないのはまだしも、簡単な質問にも答えられないのは問題だ。","romaji":"Muzukashii shitsumon ni kotaerarenai no wa mada shimo, kantan na shitsumon ni mo kotaerarenai no wa mondai da.","en":"It’s one thing not to be able to answer difficult questions, but it’s a real problem if you can’t even answer simple ones.","id":"Tidak dapat menjawab pertanyaan yang sulit adalah satu hal, tetapi akan menjadi masalah nyata jika Anda bahkan tidak dapat menjawab pertanyaan yang sederhana."}]},{"pattern":"～はもとより (〜wa moto yori)","meaning":"Expressing that something is obvious, and there is also something else.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan bahwa ada sesuatu yang jelas, dan ada juga sesuatu yang lain.","formation":"Noun1 + はもとより, Noun2 + も","formationId":"Kata Benda1 + はもとより, Kata Benda2 + も","examples":[{"jp":"英語はもとより、スペイン語も勉強しています。","romaji":"Eigo wa moto yori, supeingo mo benkyou shite imasu.","en":"I'm studying not only English, but also Spanish.","id":"Saya tidak hanya belajar bahasa Inggris, tetapi juga bahasa Spanyol."},{"jp":"彼女は料理はもとより、お菓子作りも得意です。","romaji":"Kanojo wa ryouri wa moto yori, okashi tsukuri mo tokui desu.","en":"She’s not only good at cooking, but also at making sweets.","id":"Dia tidak hanya pandai memasak, tapi juga membuat manisan."},{"jp":"このホテルは部屋の清潔さはもとより、サービスも素晴らしいです。","romaji":"Kono hoteru wa heya no seiketsusa wa moto yori, saabisu mo subarashii desu.","en":"This hotel not only has clean rooms but also great service.","id":"Hotel ini tidak hanya memiliki kamar yang bersih tetapi juga pelayanan yang luar biasa."},{"jp":"彼は音楽はもとより、絵も上手です。","romaji":"Kare wa ongaku wa moto yori, e mo jouzu desu.","en":"He’s not only good at music, but also skilled at drawing.","id":"Dia tidak hanya pandai bermusik, tapi juga terampil menggambar."}]},{"pattern":"～は抜きにして (〜wa nuki ni shite)","meaning":"Leaving aside, excluding.","meaningId":"Mengesampingkan, mengecualikan.","formation":"Noun + は抜きにして","formationId":"Kata benda + は抜きにして","examples":[{"jp":"値段は抜きにして、味は美味しい。","romaji":"Nedan wa nuki ni shite, aji wa oishii.","en":"Leaving aside the price, the taste is delicious.","id":"Terlepas dari harganya, rasanya enak."},{"jp":"彼の性格は抜きにして、彼の実力は認めざるを得ない。","romaji":"Kare no seikaku wa nuki ni shite, kare no jitsuryoku wa mitomezaru o enai.","en":"Putting aside his personality, I have to acknowledge his ability.","id":"Mengesampingkan kepribadiannya, saya harus mengakui kemampuannya."},{"jp":"デザインは抜きにして、この携帯電話の機能は優れています。","romaji":"Dezain wa nuki ni shite, kono keitai denwa no kinou wa sugurete imasu.","en":"Leaving aside the design, this phone’s features are excellent.","id":"Terlepas dari desainnya, fitur ponsel ini luar biasa."},{"jp":"運転の速さは抜きにして、彼女は親切で信頼できる運転手だ。","romaji":"Unten no hayasa wa nuki ni shite, kanojo wa shinsetsu de shinrai dekiru untenshu da.","en":"Leaving aside her driving speed, she's a kind and trustworthy driver.","id":"Terlepas dari kecepatan mengemudinya, dia adalah pengemudi yang baik dan dapat dipercaya."}]},{"pattern":"～べきではない (〜beki dewa nai)","meaning":"Express that an action should not be done; 'should not', 'ought not to'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan bahwa suatu tindakan tidak boleh dilakukan; 'seharusnya tidak', 'seharusnya tidak'.","formation":"Verb-dictionary form + べき + ではない","formationId":"Bentuk kamus kata kerja + べき + ではない","examples":[{"jp":"遅れる理由がないなら、遅れるべきではありません。","romaji":"Okureru riyuu ga nai nara, okureru beki dewa arimasen.","en":"If there's no reason to be late, you shouldn’t be late.","id":"Jika tidak ada alasan untuk terlambat, maka Anda tidak boleh terlambat."},{"jp":"子供に悪口を言うべきではありません。","romaji":"Kodomo ni waruguchi o iu beki dewa arimasen.","en":"You shouldn’t say hurtful things to children.","id":"Anda tidak boleh mengatakan hal-hal yang menyakitkan kepada anak-anak."},{"jp":"この薬は一度に飲みすぎるべきではない。","romaji":"Kono kusuri wa ichido ni nomisugiru beki dewa nai.","en":"You should not take too much of this medicine at once.","id":"Anda sebaiknya tidak meminum obat ini terlalu banyak sekaligus."},{"jp":"知らない人と個人情報を共有するべきではない。","romaji":"Shiranai hito to kojin jouhou o kyouyuu suru beki dewa nai.","en":"You shouldn't share personal information with strangers.","id":"Anda tidak boleh berbagi informasi pribadi dengan orang asing."}]},{"pattern":"～まい (〜mai)","meaning":"Express a negative conjecture or determination; 'probably not' or 'I will not'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan dugaan atau tekad negatif; 'mungkin tidak' atau 'Saya tidak akan'.","formation":"Verb-dictionary form + まい","formationId":"Bentuk kamus kata kerja + まい","examples":[{"jp":"彼は今晩来るまい。","romaji":"Kare wa konban kuru mai.","en":"He probably won't come tonight.","id":"Dia mungkin tidak akan datang malam ini."},{"jp":"こんなに遅れては、電車に間に合うまい。","romaji":"Konnani okurete wa, densha ni maniau mai.","en":"Being this late, I probably won't make it for the train.","id":"Karena selarut ini, aku mungkin tidak akan sampai ke kereta."},{"jp":"あの人は絶対に忘れるまい。","romaji":"Ano hito wa zettai ni wasureru mai.","en":"That person will definitely not forget.","id":"Orang itu pasti tidak akan lupa."},{"jp":"私は二度とその失敗を繰り返すまい。","romaji":"Watashi wa nidoto sono shippai o kurikaesu mai.","en":"I will not repeat that mistake again.","id":"Saya tidak akan mengulangi kesalahan itu lagi."}]},{"pattern":"～まで～て (〜made 〜te)","meaning":"Express doing something until a certain time or condition; 'until', 'to'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan melakukan sesuatu sampai waktu atau kondisi tertentu; 'sampai', 'ke'.","formation":"Time/Noun + まで + Verb(て-form)","formationId":"Waktu/Kata Benda + まで + Kata Kerja(て-bentuk)","examples":[{"jp":"9時まで働いて、その後休憩しました。","romaji":"Ku-ji made hataraite, sono ato kyuukei shimashita.","en":"I worked until 9 o'clock, and then took a break.","id":"Saya bekerja sampai jam 9, lalu istirahat."},{"jp":"夜まで勉強して、試験に合格しました。","romaji":"Yoru made benkyou shite, shiken ni goukaku shimashita.","en":"I studied until night, and passed the exam.","id":"Saya belajar sampai malam, dan lulus ujian."},{"jp":"最後のページまで読んで、本を閉じました。","romaji":"Saigo no peeji made yonde, hon o tojimashita.","en":"I read until the last page, then closed the book.","id":"Aku membaca sampai halaman terakhir, lalu menutup bukunya."},{"jp":"電車が着くまで待って、友達と会いました。","romaji":"Densha ga tsuku made matte, tomodachi to aimashita.","en":"I waited until the train arrived, and then met my friend.","id":"Saya menunggu sampai kereta tiba, lalu bertemu teman saya."}]},{"pattern":"～ままに (〜mama ni)","meaning":"Act according to; leave as is; unchanged.","meaningId":"Bertindak menurut; biarkan apa adanya; tidak berubah.","formation":"Verb-て + まま, い-Adjective + のまま, な-Adjective + なまま, Noun + のまま","formationId":"Kata Kerja-て + まま, い-Kata Sifat + のまま, な-Kata Sifat + なまま, Kata Benda + のまま","examples":[{"jp":"子供が寝ているままに、静かに部屋を出ました。","romaji":"Kodomo ga nete iru mama ni, shizuka ni heya o demashita.","en":"I quietly left the room while the child was still sleeping.","id":"Saya diam-diam meninggalkan kamar saat anak itu masih tidur."},{"jp":"窓が開いたままで、寒くなりました。","romaji":"Mado ga aita mama de, samuku narimashita.","en":"It got cold with the window left open.","id":"Udara menjadi dingin dengan jendela dibiarkan terbuka."},{"jp":"彼は元気なままで老人ホームに入りました。","romaji":"Kare wa genki na mama de roujin hoomu ni hairimashita.","en":"He entered the nursing home while still in good health.","id":"Ia masuk panti jompo dengan kondisi masih dalam keadaan sehat."},{"jp":"昔の思い出のままに、この町に戻りました。","romaji":"Mukashi no omoide no mama ni, kono machi ni modorimashita.","en":"I returned to this town with my old memories intact.","id":"Saya kembali ke kota ini dengan kenangan lama saya yang utuh."}]},{"pattern":"～もかまわず (〜mo kamawazu)","meaning":"Express indifference or disregard; 'without hesitating', 'without worrying about'.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan ketidakpedulian atau pengabaian; 'tanpa ragu-ragu', 'tanpa khawatir'.","formation":"Verb-dictionary form + もかまわず, Noun + もかまわず","formationId":"Bentuk kamus kata kerja + もかまわず, Kata Benda + もかまわず","examples":[{"jp":"彼は周りの人もかまわず、大声で話しました。","romaji":"Kare wa mawari no hito mo kamawazu, oogoe de hanashimashita.","en":"Without worrying about the people around him, he spoke loudly.","id":"Tanpa mengkhawatirkan orang-orang di sekitarnya, dia berbicara dengan lantang."},{"jp":"彼女は時間もかまわず、ゆっくりと本を読み続けました。","romaji":"Kanojo wa jikan mo kamawazu, yukkuri to hon o yomitsuzukemashita.","en":"She kept reading the book leisurely, without worrying about the time.","id":"Dia terus membaca buku itu dengan santai, tanpa mengkhawatirkan waktu."},{"jp":"彼は寒さもかまわず、外で運動しました。","romaji":"Kare wa samusa mo kamawazu, soto de undou shimashita.","en":"He exercised outside without worrying about the cold.","id":"Dia berolahraga di luar tanpa khawatir kedinginan."},{"jp":"彼女は危険もかまわず、火事の中に飛び込んで助けに行きました。","romaji":"Kanojo wa kiken mo kamawazu, kaji no naka ni tobikonde tasuke ni ikimashita.","en":"She jumped into the fire without fear of danger to help.","id":"Dia melompat ke dalam api tanpa takut akan bahaya untuk membantu."}]},{"pattern":"～ものか (〜mono ka)","meaning":"Definitely not; no way; no chance.","meaningId":"Jelas tidak; mustahil; tidak ada kesempatan.","formation":"Verb-casual + ものか, い-Adjective + ものか, な-Adjective + (な)ものか, Noun + (な)ものか","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + ものか, い-Kata Sifat + ものか, な-Kata Sifat + (な)ものか, Kata Benda + (な)ものか","examples":[{"jp":"そんなこと、僕がやりたいものか。","romaji":"Sonna koto, boku ga yaritai mono ka.","en":"No way do I want to do such a thing.","id":"Tidak mungkin aku ingin melakukan hal seperti itu."},{"jp":"こんな仕事、誰が引き受けようものか。","romaji":"Konna shigoto, dare ga hikiukeyou mono ka.","en":"Who on earth would take on a job like this? (No one would!)","id":"Siapa yang mau menerima pekerjaan seperti ini? (Tidak ada yang mau!)"},{"jp":"誰が彼に助けを求めようものか。","romaji":"Dare ga kare ni tasuke o motomeyou mono ka.","en":"Who would ever ask him for help? (Certainly no one!)","id":"Siapa yang akan meminta bantuannya? (Tentu saja tidak ada!)"},{"jp":"この寒い日に外で遊ぶなんて、無理なものか。","romaji":"Kono samui hi ni soto de asobu nante, muri na mono ka.","en":"There's no way we can play outside on a day this cold.","id":"Tidak mungkin kita bisa bermain di luar pada hari sedingin ini."}]},{"pattern":"～ものがある (〜mono ga aru)","meaning":"Express a strong impression or feeling; 'there's something about it that...'","meaningId":"Mengungkapkan kesan atau perasaan yang kuat; 'ada sesuatu tentang itu yang...'","formation":"Verb-casual + ものがある, い-Adjective + ものがある, な-Adjective + なものがある","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + ものがある, い-Kata Sifat + ものがある, な-Kata Sifat + なものがある","examples":[{"jp":"彼のスピーチには心を打たれるものがある。","romaji":"Kare no supiichi ni wa kokoro o utareru mono ga aru.","en":"There's something moving about his speech.","id":"Ada sesuatu yang mengharukan dalam pidatonya."},{"jp":"この映画には考えさせられるものがある。","romaji":"Kono eiga ni wa kangaesaserareru mono ga aru.","en":"There's something about this movie that really makes you think.","id":"Ada sesuatu tentang film ini yang benar-benar membuat Anda berpikir."},{"jp":"彼の言うことにも一理あるものがある。","romaji":"Kare no iu koto ni mo ichiri aru mono ga aru.","en":"There's a certain point in what he says.","id":"Ada maksud tertentu dalam perkataannya."},{"jp":"毎日忙しすぎる生活には少し息苦しいものがある。","romaji":"Mainichi isogashisugiru seikatsu ni wa sukoshi ikigurushii mono ga aru.","en":"There's something a bit suffocating about being so busy every day.","id":"Ada sesuatu yang agak menyesakkan karena begitu sibuknya setiap hari."}]},{"pattern":"～ものだ (〜mono da)","meaning":"Expresses something natural or expected; 'it is normal that...', 'should', 'ought to'.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan sesuatu yang wajar atau diharapkan; 'wajar kalau...', 'seharusnya', 'seharusnya'.","formation":"Verb-dictionary form + ものだ, な-Adjective + なものだ, (Also: Verb-た form + ものだ for recollections)","formationId":"Bentuk kamus kata kerja + ものだ, な-Kata Sifat + なものだ, (Juga: Bentuk kata kerja-た + ものだ untuk kenangan)","examples":[{"jp":"若い時はたくさん遊ぶものだ。","romaji":"Wakai toki wa takusan asobu mono da.","en":"It is natural to have a lot of fun when you are young.","id":"Wajar jika Anda bersenang-senang saat Anda masih muda."},{"jp":"約束をしたら、守るものだ。","romaji":"Yakusoku o shitara, mamoru mono da.","en":"If you make a promise, you should keep it.","id":"Jika Anda membuat janji, Anda harus menepatinya."},{"jp":"お客さんが来ると、お茶を出すものだ。","romaji":"Okyakusan ga kuru to, ocha o dasu mono da.","en":"When guests arrive, it's customary to serve tea.","id":"Saat tamu datang, sudah menjadi kebiasaan untuk menyajikan teh."},{"jp":"人生は困難に立ち向かうものだ。","romaji":"Jinsei wa konnan ni tachimukau mono da.","en":"In life, one ought to face hardships.","id":"Dalam hidup, seseorang harus menghadapi kesulitan."}]},{"pattern":"～ものだから (〜mono dakara)","meaning":"Express the reason or cause for something; 'because', 'since', 'due to'.","meaningId":"Mengungkapkan alasan atau penyebab sesuatu; 'karena', 'sejak', 'karena'.","formation":"Verb-plain + ものだから, い-Adjective + ものだから, な-Adjective + なものだから, Noun + なものだから","formationId":"Kata kerja-biasa + ものだから, い-Kata Sifat + ものだから, な-Kata Sifat + なものだから, Kata Benda + なものだから","examples":[{"jp":"試験が近いものだから、毎日勉強しています。","romaji":"Shiken ga chikai mono dakara, mainichi benkyou shiteimasu.","en":"Because the exam is near, I'm studying every day.","id":"Karena ujiannya sudah dekat, saya belajar setiap hari."},{"jp":"このレストランはとても人気があるものだから、予約しないと席がないかもしれません。","romaji":"Kono resutoran wa totemo ninki ga aru mono dakara, yoyaku shinai to seki ga nai kamoshiremasen.","en":"Because this restaurant is very popular, there might not be any seats if we don't reserve.","id":"Karena restoran ini sangat populer, mungkin tidak akan ada kursi jika kita tidak melakukan reservasi."},{"jp":"彼は若いものだから、まだたくさんの経験を積んでいない。","romaji":"Kare wa wakai mono dakara, mada takusan no keiken wo tsunde inai.","en":"Because he is young, he hasn't accumulated much experience yet.","id":"Karena usianya yang masih muda, ia belum mengumpulkan banyak pengalaman."},{"jp":"今日は寒いものだから、手袋を持って行きましょう。","romaji":"Kyou wa samui mono dakara, tebukuro wo motte ikimashou.","en":"Since it's cold today, let's bring gloves.","id":"Karena hari ini dingin, ayo bawa sarung tangan."}]},{"pattern":"～ものではない (〜mono dewa nai)","meaning":"Expresses a strong negative suggestion or prohibition: 'should not', 'must not'.","meaningId":"Mengungkapkan saran atau larangan negatif yang kuat: 'tidak boleh', 'tidak boleh'.","formation":"Verb-dictionary form + ものではない","formationId":"Bentuk kamus kata kerja + ものではない","examples":[{"jp":"そんなことを言うものではありません。","romaji":"Sonna koto o iu mono dewa arimasen.","en":"You should not say such a thing.","id":"Anda tidak seharusnya mengatakan hal seperti itu."},{"jp":"公共の場で大声を出すものではない。","romaji":"Koukyou no ba de oogoe o dasu mono dewa nai.","en":"You should not raise your voice in public places.","id":"Anda tidak boleh meninggikan suara Anda di tempat umum."},{"jp":"彼の秘密を他の人に教えるものではありません。","romaji":"Kare no himitsu o hoka no hito ni oshieru mono dewa arimasen.","en":"You must not tell his secret to other people.","id":"Anda tidak boleh menceritakan rahasianya kepada orang lain."},{"jp":"安全な場所では遊んでいいが、危険なところで遊ぶものではない。","romaji":"Anzen na basho de wa asonde ii ga, kiken na tokoro de asobu mono dewa nai.","en":"It's okay to play in safe places, but you should not play somewhere dangerous.","id":"Boleh saja bermain di tempat yang aman, namun sebaiknya jangan bermain di tempat yang berbahaya."}]},{"pattern":"～ものなら (〜mono nara)","meaning":"Expresses a conditional wish or unlikely possibility; 'if only', 'if it were possible'.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan keinginan bersyarat atau kemungkinan yang tidak mungkin; 'seandainya saja', 'seandainya mungkin'.","formation":"Verb-(potential/plain) form + ものなら, etc.","formationId":"Bentuk kata kerja-(potensial/polos) + ものなら, dll.","examples":[{"jp":"帰れるものなら、今すぐ国へ帰りたい。","romaji":"Kaereru mono nara, ima sugu kuni e kaeritai.","en":"If I could possibly go back, I'd return to my country right now.","id":"Jika saya bisa kembali, saya akan kembali ke negara saya sekarang."},{"jp":"できるものなら、世界を一周してみたい。","romaji":"Dekiru mono nara, sekai o isshuu shite mitai.","en":"If it were possible, I'd love to travel around the world.","id":"Jika memungkinkan, saya ingin bepergian keliling dunia."},{"jp":"やり直せるものなら、子供の頃に戻りたい。","romaji":"Yarinaoseru mono nara, kodomo no koro ni modoritai.","en":"If I could redo my life, I'd go back to my childhood.","id":"Jika aku bisa mengulang hidupku, aku akan kembali ke masa kecilku."},{"jp":"元気になれるものなら、どんな薬でも試したい。","romaji":"Genki ni nareru mono nara, donna kusuri demo tameshitai.","en":"If it could make me healthy, I'd try any medicine.","id":"Jika itu bisa membuat saya sehat, saya akan mencoba obat apa pun."}]},{"pattern":"～ものの、～ (〜mono no、～)","meaning":"Indicates contrast or contradiction between two clauses; 'although', 'but'.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan kontras atau kontradiksi antara dua klausa; 'walaupun', 'tetapi'.","formation":"Verb-casual + ものの, い-Adjective + ものの, な-Adjective + なものの, Noun + であるものの","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + ものの, い-Kata Sifat + ものの, な-Kata Sifat + なものの, Kata Benda + であるものの","examples":[{"jp":"早起きしたものの、バスに間に合わなかった。","romaji":"Hayaoki shita mono no, basu ni maniawanakatta.","en":"Even though I got up early, I didn't catch the bus in time.","id":"Meskipun saya bangun pagi, saya tidak mengejar bus tepat waktu."},{"jp":"この部屋は広いものの、家具が少ない。","romaji":"Kono heya wa hiroi mono no, kagu ga sukunai.","en":"Although this room is spacious, there isn't much furniture.","id":"Meski ruangan ini luas, namun perabotannya tidak banyak."},{"jp":"彼女は美しいものの、性格が悪い。","romaji":"Kanojo wa utsukushii mono no, seikaku ga warui.","en":"She is beautiful, but her personality is bad.","id":"Dia cantik, tapi kepribadiannya buruk."},{"jp":"彼は有名な歌手であるものの、コンサートにあまり人が来なかった。","romaji":"Kare wa yuumei na kashu de aru mono no, konsaato ni amari hito ga konakatta.","en":"Although he is a famous singer, not many people came to his concert.","id":"Meski merupakan penyanyi terkenal, namun tidak banyak orang yang datang ke konsernya."}]},{"pattern":"～も～ば～も～ (〜mo〜ba〜mo〜)","meaning":"Lists multiple attributes or actions applying to the same subject: 'both…and…', 'not only…but also…'.","meaningId":"Mencantumkan beberapa atribut atau tindakan yang diterapkan pada subjek yang sama: 'keduanya…dan…', 'tidak hanya…tetapi juga…'.","formation":"Noun/Verb/Adjective + も + (Verb/Adjective in ば-form) + も + (Verb/Adjective)","formationId":"Kata Benda/Kata Kerja/Kata Sifat + も + (Kata Kerja/Kata Sifat dalam bentuk ば) + も + (Kata Kerja/Kata Sifat)","examples":[{"jp":"彼は勉強もできればスポーツもできる。","romaji":"Kare wa benkyou mo dekireba supootsu mo dekiru.","en":"He is good at studying and also at sports.","id":"Dia pandai belajar dan juga olahraga."},{"jp":"このレストランは値段も安ければ味もいい。","romaji":"Kono resutoran wa nedan mo yasukereba aji mo ii.","en":"This restaurant is cheap, and the food is also good.","id":"Restoran ini murah, dan makanannya juga enak."},{"jp":"彼女はピアノも弾けばギターも弾く。","romaji":"Kanojo wa piano mo hikeba gitaa mo hiku.","en":"She plays both the piano and the guitar.","id":"Dia memainkan piano dan gitar."},{"jp":"人生には楽しい時もあれば辛い時もある。","romaji":"Jinsei ni wa tanoshii toki mo areba tsurai toki mo aru.","en":"In life, there are both fun times and tough times.","id":"Dalam hidup, ada saat-saat menyenangkan dan saat-saat sulit."}]},{"pattern":"～も同然だ (〜mo douzen da)","meaning":"Indicates 'as good as', 'virtually', or 'practically' the same as something.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan 'sebagus', 'hampir', atau 'praktis' sama dengan sesuatu.","formation":"Noun + (も)同然だ, Verb-casual + (も)同然だ, etc.","formationId":"Kata Benda + (も)同然だ, Kata Kerja-kasual + (も)同然だ, dsb.","examples":[{"jp":"彼とは長い付き合いだから、家族も同然だ。","romaji":"Kare to wa nagai tsukiai dakara, kazoku mo douzen da.","en":"I've known him for so long that he's practically family.","id":"Saya sudah mengenalnya begitu lama sehingga dia bisa dibilang keluarga."},{"jp":"毎日遅刻するなんて、来ていないも同然だ。","romaji":"Mainichi chikoku suru nante, kite inai mo douzen da.","en":"Being late every single day is as good as not coming at all.","id":"Terlambat setiap hari sama saja dengan tidak datang sama sekali."},{"jp":"彼女と私は幼なじみで、姉妹も同然の仲です。","romaji":"Kanojo to watashi wa osananajimi de, shimai mo douzen no naka desu.","en":"She and I are childhood friends, practically like sisters.","id":"Dia dan aku adalah teman masa kecil, bisa dibilang seperti saudara perempuan."},{"jp":"こんなに少ない給料じゃ、ただ働きも同然だ。","romaji":"Konna ni sukunai kyuuryou ja, tadabataraki mo douzen da.","en":"With such a small salary, it's practically like working for free.","id":"Dengan gaji sekecil itu, bisa dibilang bekerja cuma-cuma."}]},{"pattern":"～やら～やら (〜yara〜yara)","meaning":"Expresses various items or actions, 'things like..., and so on'.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan berbagai item atau tindakan, 'hal-hal seperti..., dan seterusnya'.","formation":"Verb-casual + やら, い-Adjective + やら, な-Adjective + やら, Noun + やら","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + やら, い-Kata Sifat + やら, な-Kata Sifat + やら, Kata Benda + やら","examples":[{"jp":"宿題やら掃除やら、やることがたくさんある。","romaji":"Shukudai yara souji yara, yaru koto ga takusan aru.","en":"I have lots of things to do, like homework and cleaning.","id":"Ada banyak hal yang harus aku lakukan, seperti pekerjaan rumah dan bersih-bersih."},{"jp":"野菜やら果物やら、色々な食べ物を買いました。","romaji":"Yasai yara kudamono yara, iroiro na tabemono wo kaimashita.","en":"I bought all sorts of foods, such as vegetables and fruits.","id":"Saya membeli segala macam makanan, seperti sayuran dan buah-buahan."},{"jp":"彼女は歌がうまいやら踊れるやら、本当に多才だ。","romaji":"Kanojo wa uta ga umai yara odoreru yara, hontou ni tasai da.","en":"She’s really talented—she can sing well, dance, and so on.","id":"Dia sangat berbakat—dia bisa menyanyi dengan baik, menari, dan sebagainya."},{"jp":"お店にはバッグやら靴やらアクセサリーやらが置いてある。","romaji":"Omise ni wa baggu yara kutsu yara akusesarii yara ga oite aru.","en":"The store has all kinds of items like bags, shoes, accessories, etc.","id":"Toko ini menjual segala macam barang seperti tas, sepatu, aksesoris, dll."}]},{"pattern":"～ようがない (〜you ga nai)","meaning":"Expresses that there is no way (method) to do something; it's impossible to do.","meaningId":"Menyatakan bahwa tidak ada cara (metode) untuk melakukan sesuatu; itu tidak mungkin dilakukan.","formation":"Verb-ます stem + ようがない","formationId":"Kata kerja-ます batang + ようがない","examples":[{"jp":"彼の連絡先がわからないので、助けようがない。","romaji":"Kare no renrakusaki ga wakaranai node, tasukeyou ga nai.","en":"I don't know his contact information, so there's no way I can help him.","id":"Saya tidak tahu informasi kontaknya, jadi saya tidak bisa membantunya."},{"jp":"ここまで壊れてしまったら、もう直しようがない。","romaji":"Koko made kowarete shimattara, mou naoshiyou ga nai.","en":"Now that it's broken this badly, there's no way to fix it.","id":"Sekarang sudah rusak parah, tidak ada cara untuk memperbaikinya."},{"jp":"証拠が全くないから、彼が犯人だと証明しようがない。","romaji":"Shouko ga mattaku nai kara, kare ga hannin da to shoumeishiyou ga nai.","en":"There’s no evidence at all, so there’s no way to prove he’s the culprit.","id":"Tidak ada bukti sama sekali, jadi tidak ada cara untuk membuktikan bahwa dialah pelakunya."},{"jp":"突然英語で話しかけられて、何と答えればいいか分からず答えようがなかった。","romaji":"Totsuzen eigo de hanashikakerarete, nan to kotaereba ii ka wakarazu kotaeyou ga nakatta.","en":"I was suddenly spoken to in English and didn’t know how to respond, so there was no way for me to reply.","id":"Saya tiba-tiba diajak bicara dalam bahasa Inggris dan tidak tahu bagaimana harus menjawabnya, jadi tidak ada cara bagi saya untuk membalasnya."}]},{"pattern":"～よりほかない (〜yori hoka nai)","meaning":"Express that there is no other choice; 'have no choice but', 'cannot do anything but'.","meaningId":"Nyatakan bahwa tidak ada pilihan lain; 'tidak punya pilihan selain', 'tidak bisa melakukan apa pun kecuali'.","formation":"Verb-dictionary form + よりほかない","formationId":"Bentuk kamus kata kerja + よりほかない","examples":[{"jp":"試験が近いので、勉強するよりほかない。","romaji":"Shiken ga chikai node, benkyou suru yori hoka nai.","en":"Since the exam is near, there is no choice but to study.","id":"Karena ujian sudah dekat, tidak ada pilihan selain belajar."},{"jp":"風邪がひどいので、早く寝るよりほかない。","romaji":"Kaze ga hidoi node, hayaku neru yori hoka nai.","en":"My cold is severe, so I have no choice but to go to bed early.","id":"Pilekku parah, jadi aku tidak punya pilihan selain tidur lebih awal."},{"jp":"バスが来ないので、歩くよりほかない。","romaji":"Basu ga konai node, aruku yori hoka nai.","en":"Since the bus isn't coming, I have no choice but to walk.","id":"Karena bus tidak datang, saya tidak punya pilihan selain berjalan kaki."},{"jp":"お金がないので、安いものを買うよりほかない。","romaji":"Okane ga nai node, yasui mono o kau yori hoka nai.","en":"Since I have no money, I have no choice but to buy cheap things.","id":"Karena saya tidak punya uang, saya tidak punya pilihan selain membeli barang-barang murah."}]},{"pattern":"～わけがない (〜wake ga nai)","meaning":"Expresses 'there’s no way' or 'it’s impossible', indicating a high degree of certainty.","meaningId":"Menyatakan 'tidak mungkin' atau 'tidak mungkin', menunjukkan tingkat kepastian yang tinggi.","formation":"Verb-casual + わけがない, い-Adjective + わけがない, な-Adjective + なわけがない, Noun + のわけがない","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + わけがない, い-Kata Sifat + わけがない, な-Kata Sifat + なわけがない, Kata Benda + のわけがない","examples":[{"jp":"彼が怪我をしたから、試合に勝てるわけがない。","romaji":"Kare ga kega wo shita kara, shiai ni kateru wake ga nai.","en":"He got injured, so there's no way he can win the match.","id":"Dia cedera, jadi tidak mungkin dia bisa memenangkan pertandingan."},{"jp":"嘘ばかり言っている人を、信じるわけがない。","romaji":"Uso bakari itte iru hito wo, shinjiru wake ga nai.","en":"There's no way I can believe someone who constantly lies.","id":"Tidak mungkin aku bisa mempercayai seseorang yang terus-menerus berbohong."},{"jp":"彼女は忙しいから、このパーティーに来るわけがない。","romaji":"Kanojo wa isogashii kara, kono paatii ni kuru wake ga nai.","en":"She's busy, so there's no way she can come to this party.","id":"Dia sibuk, jadi tidak mungkin dia bisa datang ke pesta ini."},{"jp":"昨日はずっと寝ていたから、その事件を知るわけがない。","romaji":"Kinou wa zutto nete ita kara, sono jiken wo shiru wake ga nai.","en":"I was asleep all day yesterday, so there's no way I could know about that incident.","id":"Aku tertidur sepanjang hari kemarin, jadi tidak mungkin aku tahu tentang kejadian itu."}]},{"pattern":"～わけだ (〜wake da)","meaning":"Express a logical conclusion or reason; 'it means', 'no wonder', 'the reason is'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan kesimpulan atau alasan yang logis; 'artinya', 'tidak heran', 'alasannya'.","formation":"Verb-casual + わけだ, い-Adjective + わけだ, な-Adjective + なわけだ, Noun + のわけだ","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + わけだ, い-Kata Sifat + わけだ, な-Kata Sifat + なわけだ, Kata Benda + のわけだ","examples":[{"jp":"彼女が遅れたのは、電車が遅れたわけだ。","romaji":"Kanojo ga okureta no wa, densha ga okureta wake da.","en":"The reason she was late is that the train was delayed.","id":"Alasan dia terlambat adalah karena keretanya tertunda."},{"jp":"授業が面白かったから、みんな熱心に聞いていたわけだ。","romaji":"Jugyou ga omoshirokatta kara, minna nesshin ni kiiteita wake da.","en":"The class was interesting, so that's why everyone was listening intently.","id":"Kelasnya menarik, jadi itulah sebabnya semua orang mendengarkan dengan penuh perhatian."},{"jp":"彼はとても忙しいですから、休みがほとんどないわけだ。","romaji":"Kare wa totemo isogashii desu kara, yasumi ga hotondo nai wake da.","en":"He's really busy, which is why he hardly has any time off.","id":"Dia sangat sibuk, itulah sebabnya dia hampir tidak punya waktu istirahat."},{"jp":"この問題が難しいから、全然わからないわけだ。","romaji":"Kono mondai ga muzukashii kara, zenzen wakaranai wake da.","en":"This problem is tough, so no wonder I don't understand it at all.","id":"Soal ini berat, jadi tidak heran saya tidak memahaminya sama sekali."}]},{"pattern":"～わけではない (〜wake dewa nai)","meaning":"Not necessarily; it doesn't mean that ~.","meaningId":"Belum tentu; bukan berarti begitu~.","formation":"Verb-plain + わけではない, い-Adjective + わけではない, な-Adjective + だわけではない, Noun + だわけではない","formationId":"Kata Kerja-biasa + わけではない, い-Kata Sifat + わけではない, な-Kata Sifat + だわけではない, Kata Benda + だわけではない","examples":[{"jp":"彼が勉強しないわけではないが、成績があまり良くない。","romaji":"Kare ga benkyou shinai wake dewa nai ga, seiseki ga amari yoku nai.","en":"It's not that he doesn't study, but his grades aren't very good.","id":"Bukannya dia tidak belajar, tapi nilainya tidak terlalu bagus."},{"jp":"このレストランが高いわけではないけど、毎日通うには少し高いね。","romaji":"Kono resutoran ga takai wake dewa nai kedo, mainichi kayou ni wa sukoshi takai ne.","en":"It's not that this restaurant is expensive, but it's a bit too pricey to go there every day.","id":"Bukan karena restoran ini mahal, tapi agak terlalu mahal untuk pergi ke sana setiap hari."},{"jp":"彼女が優しくないわけではないが、時々話し方がきついことがある。","romaji":"Kanojo ga yasashikunai wake dewa nai ga, tokidoki hanashikata ga kitsui koto ga aru.","en":"It's not that she's unkind, but sometimes her manner of speaking can be harsh.","id":"Bukannya dia tidak baik, tapi terkadang cara bicaranya bisa kasar."},{"jp":"彼が忙しいわけではないが、時間を上手に使えていないようだ。","romaji":"Kare ga isogashii wake dewa nai ga, jikan o jouzu ni tsukaete inai you da.","en":"It's not that he's busy; he just doesn't seem to use his time effectively.","id":"Bukan karena dia sibuk; dia sepertinya tidak menggunakan waktunya secara efektif."}]},{"pattern":"～わけにはいかない (〜wake ni wa ikanai)","meaning":"Expresses that one cannot (or must not) do something due to responsibility, social pressure, etc.","meaningId":"Mengungkapkan bahwa seseorang tidak dapat (atau tidak boleh) melakukan sesuatu karena tanggung jawab, tekanan sosial, dll.","formation":"Verb-dictionary form + わけにはいかない","formationId":"Bentuk kamus kata kerja + わけにはいかない","examples":[{"jp":"試験が近いから、遊ぶわけにはいかない。","romaji":"Shiken ga chikai kara, asobu wake ni wa ikanai.","en":"Since the exam is close, I can't afford to just play around.","id":"Karena ujiannya sudah dekat, saya tidak bisa hanya bermain-main."},{"jp":"田中さんが待っているので、遅れるわけにはいかない。","romaji":"Tanaka-san ga matteiru node, okureru wake ni wa ikanai.","en":"Mr. Tanaka is waiting, so I absolutely must not be late.","id":"Pak Tanaka sedang menunggu, jadi saya tidak boleh terlambat."},{"jp":"子供たちのために、この仕事を辞めるわけにはいかない。","romaji":"Kodomo-tachi no tame ni, kono shigoto o yameru wake ni wa ikanai.","en":"For the sake of my kids, I can't afford to quit this job.","id":"Demi anak-anakku, aku tidak mampu berhenti dari pekerjaan ini."},{"jp":"この問題は重要だから、無視するわけにはいかない。","romaji":"Kono mondai wa juuyou dakara, mushi suru wake ni wa ikanai.","en":"This issue is important, so I can't simply ignore it.","id":"Masalah ini penting, jadi saya tidak bisa mengabaikannya begitu saja."}]},{"pattern":"～をきっかけに (〜wo kikkake ni)","meaning":"Indicates that something serves as a trigger or starting point for another action/event.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan bahwa sesuatu berfungsi sebagai pemicu atau titik awal untuk tindakan/peristiwa lain.","formation":"Noun + をきっかけに","formationId":"Kata benda + をきっかけに","examples":[{"jp":"結婚をきっかけに、彼は真剣に仕事を頑張り始めた。","romaji":"Kekkon o kikkake ni, kare wa shinken ni shigoto o ganbarihajimeta.","en":"Getting married was the catalyst for him to start working seriously.","id":"Menikah adalah katalis baginya untuk mulai bekerja dengan serius."},{"jp":"あの出会いをきっかけに、私たちは友達になりました。","romaji":"Ano deai o kikkake ni, watashitachi wa tomodachi ni narimashita.","en":"That encounter led us to become friends.","id":"Pertemuan itu membuat kami menjadi teman."},{"jp":"コンサートをきっかけに、彼女は音楽の道に進むことを決めました。","romaji":"Konsaato o kikkake ni, kanojo wa ongaku no michi ni susumu koto o kimemashita.","en":"Inspired by the concert, she decided to pursue music.","id":"Terinspirasi oleh konser tersebut, dia memutuskan untuk menekuni musik."},{"jp":"留学をきっかけに、私の外国語スキルが向上しました。","romaji":"Ryuugaku o kikkake ni, watashi no gaikokugo sukiru ga koujou shimashita.","en":"Studying abroad gave me the chance to improve my foreign language skills.","id":"Belajar di luar negeri memberi saya kesempatan untuk meningkatkan kemampuan bahasa asing saya."}]},{"pattern":"～を～として (〜wo〜toshite)","meaning":"Express 'as', 'in the capacity of', or 'taking something as...'.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan 'sebagai', 'dalam kapasitas', atau 'menganggap sesuatu sebagai...'.","formation":"Noun1 + を + Noun2 + として","formationId":"Kata Benda1 + を + Kata Benda2 + として","examples":[{"jp":"彼は教師を職業として働いています。","romaji":"Kare wa kyoushi o shokugyou toshite hataraite imasu.","en":"He works as a teacher.","id":"Dia bekerja sebagai guru."},{"jp":"彼女はリーダーを役割として受け入れました。","romaji":"Kanojo wa riidaa o yakuwari toshite ukeiremashita.","en":"She accepted the role of leader.","id":"Dia menerima peran sebagai pemimpin."},{"jp":"私たちは彼を仲間として信頼しています。","romaji":"Watashitachi wa kare o nakama toshite shinrai shite imasu.","en":"We trust him as one of our own (a close companion).","id":"Kami memercayainya sebagai salah satu dari kami (teman dekat)."},{"jp":"このアーティストは伝統を基盤として作品を作ります。","romaji":"Kono aatisuto wa dentou o kiban toshite sakuhin o tsukurimasu.","en":"This artist creates works with tradition as the foundation.","id":"Seniman ini menciptakan karya dengan tradisi sebagai landasannya."}]},{"pattern":"～を中心に (〜wo chuushin ni)","meaning":"Indicates that something is centered around or focused on a main topic or area.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan bahwa sesuatu berpusat atau terfokus pada topik atau area utama.","formation":"Noun + を中心に","formationId":"Kata benda + を中心に","examples":[{"jp":"このイベントは音楽を中心に楽しまれています。","romaji":"Kono ibento wa ongaku o chuushin ni tanoshimarete imasu.","en":"This event is mainly enjoyed for its music.","id":"Acara ini terutama dinikmati karena musiknya."},{"jp":"彼の仕事は東京を中心に行われています。","romaji":"Kare no shigoto wa Toukyou o chuushin ni okonawarete imasu.","en":"His work is primarily conducted in and around Tokyo.","id":"Karyanya terutama dilakukan di dalam dan sekitar Tokyo."},{"jp":"彼女は健康を中心に本を書いています。","romaji":"Kanojo wa kenkou o chuushin ni hon o kaite imasu.","en":"She’s writing a book focusing on health.","id":"Dia sedang menulis buku yang berfokus pada kesehatan."},{"jp":"最近の研究は環境保護を中心に行われている。","romaji":"Saikin no kenkyuu wa kankyou hogo o chuushin ni okonawarete iru.","en":"Recent research is being carried out with a primary focus on environmental protection.","id":"Penelitian terbaru sedang dilakukan dengan fokus utama pada perlindungan lingkungan."}]},{"pattern":"～を問わず (〜wo towazu)","meaning":"Means 'regardless of' or 'irrespective of'.","meaningId":"Berarti 'terlepas dari' atau 'terlepas dari'.","formation":"Noun + を問わず","formationId":"Kata benda + を問わず","examples":[{"jp":"このイベントは、年齢を問わず、誰でも参加できます。","romaji":"Kono ibento wa, nenrei o towazu, dare demo sanka dekimasu.","en":"This event is open to everyone, regardless of age.","id":"Acara ini terbuka untuk semua orang tanpa memandang usia."},{"jp":"このスーパーは、日曜日を問わず、毎日開いています。","romaji":"Kono suupaa wa, nichiyoubi o towazu, mainichi aite imasu.","en":"This supermarket is open every day, regardless of Sunday.","id":"Supermarket ini buka setiap hari, terlepas dari hari Minggu."},{"jp":"彼女は、暑さ寒さを問わず、毎朝散歩をしています。","romaji":"Kanojo wa, atsusa samusa o towazu, maiasa sanpo o shite imasu.","en":"She takes a walk every morning, no matter the heat or cold.","id":"Dia berjalan-jalan setiap pagi, tidak peduli panas atau dingin."},{"jp":"社長は、国籍を問わず、すべての社員を平等に扱っています。","romaji":"Shachou wa, kokuseki o towazu, subete no shain o byoudou ni atsukatte imasu.","en":"The company president treats all employees equally, regardless of nationality.","id":"Presiden perusahaan memperlakukan semua karyawan secara setara, tanpa memandang kebangsaan."}]},{"pattern":"～を込めて (〜wo komete)","meaning":"To express that something is done with a certain feeling, intention, or emotion.","meaningId":"Untuk menyatakan bahwa sesuatu dilakukan dengan perasaan, niat, atau emosi tertentu.","formation":"Feeling/emotion/intention Noun + を + 込めて + Verb","formationId":"Perasaan/emosi/niat Kata Benda + を + 込めて + Kata Kerja","examples":[{"jp":"愛を込めて料理を作りました。","romaji":"Ai wo komete ryouri wo tsukurimashita.","en":"I cooked the meal with love.","id":"Saya memasak makanan dengan cinta."},{"jp":"感謝を込めて先生にお礼の手紙を書きました。","romaji":"Kansha wo komete sensei ni orei no tegami wo kakimashita.","en":"I wrote a thank-you letter to my teacher, filled with gratitude.","id":"Saya menulis surat ucapan terima kasih kepada guru saya, penuh dengan rasa terima kasih."},{"jp":"彼は全力を込めて最後の瞬間まで戦いました。","romaji":"Kare wa zenryoku wo komete saigo no shunkan made tatakaimashita.","en":"He fought until the last moment with all his strength.","id":"Dia bertarung hingga saat terakhir dengan seluruh kekuatannya."},{"jp":"彼女は悲しみを込めて友達へ別れの言葉を伝えました。","romaji":"Kanojo wa kanashimi wo komete tomodachi e wakare no kotoba wo tsutaemashita.","en":"She conveyed her farewell words to her friend with sadness.","id":"Dia menyampaikan kata-kata perpisahannya kepada temannya dengan sedih."}]},{"pattern":"～を通じて (〜wo tsuujite)","meaning":"Expresses 'through', 'throughout', or 'during'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan 'melalui', 'sepanjang', atau 'selama'.","formation":"Noun + を通じて","formationId":"Kata benda + を通じて","examples":[{"jp":"インターネットを通じて友達と連絡を取ります。","romaji":"Intaanetto wo tsuujite tomodachi to renraku wo torimasu.","en":"I keep in touch with my friends through the internet.","id":"Saya tetap berhubungan dengan teman-teman saya melalui internet."},{"jp":"彼は一日を通じて熱心に働いています。","romaji":"Kare wa ichinichi wo tsuujite nesshin ni hataraite imasu.","en":"He works diligently throughout the day.","id":"Dia bekerja dengan rajin sepanjang hari."},{"jp":"このイベントは週末を通じて開催されます。","romaji":"Kono ibento wa shuumatsu wo tsuujite kaisai saremasu.","en":"This event will take place throughout the weekend.","id":"Acara ini akan berlangsung sepanjang akhir pekan."},{"jp":"その花は春を通じて咲いています。","romaji":"Sono hana wa haru wo tsuujite saiteimasu.","en":"The flowers bloom throughout the spring.","id":"Bunganya mekar sepanjang musim semi."}]},{"pattern":"～を頼りに (〜wo tayori ni)","meaning":"To rely on or depend on something or someone.","meaningId":"Untuk mengandalkan atau bergantung pada sesuatu atau seseorang.","formation":"Noun + を頼りに","formationId":"Kata benda + を頼りに","examples":[{"jp":"彼女は地図を頼りに旅行をしている。","romaji":"Kanojo wa chizu wo tayori ni ryokou wo shite iru.","en":"She is traveling relying on a map.","id":"Dia bepergian dengan mengandalkan peta."},{"jp":"多くの人が彼の力を頼りに生活している。","romaji":"Ooku no hito ga kare no chikara wo tayori ni seikatsu shite iru.","en":"Many people are living depending on his strength.","id":"Banyak orang yang hidup bergantung pada kekuatannya."},{"jp":"このプロジェクトでは、君のスキルを頼りにしています。","romaji":"Kono purojekuto de wa, kimi no sukiru wo tayori ni shiteimasu.","en":"In this project, we are counting on your skills.","id":"Dalam proyek ini, kami mengandalkan keahlian Anda."},{"jp":"彼は友達の助けを頼りに問題を解決しようとした。","romaji":"Kare wa tomodachi no tasuke wo tayori ni mondai wo kaiketsu shiyou to shita.","en":"He tried to solve the problem relying on his friend's help.","id":"Dia mencoba menyelesaikan masalahnya dengan mengandalkan bantuan temannya."}]},{"pattern":"～一方 (〜ippou)","meaning":"Indicates that while one action or situation is happening, another action or situation is also occurring or is in contrast.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan bahwa ketika satu tindakan atau situasi sedang terjadi, tindakan atau situasi lain juga sedang terjadi atau sebaliknya.","formation":"Verb-casual + 一方(で), い-Adjective + 一方(で), な-Adjective + な/である一方(で), Noun + である一方(で)","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + 一方(で), い-Kata Sifat + 一方(で), な-Kata Sifat + な/である一方(で), Kata Benda + である一方(で)","examples":[{"jp":"技術が進化する一方、生活が忙しくなっている。","romaji":"Gijutsu ga shinka suru ippou, seikatsu ga isogashiku natte iru.","en":"While technology advances, life is getting busier.","id":"Seiring kemajuan teknologi, kehidupan semakin sibuk."},{"jp":"日本語が上達する一方、英語力が下がっている気がする。","romaji":"Nihongo ga joutatsu suru ippou, eigo-ryoku ga sagatte iru ki ga suru.","en":"While my Japanese improves, I feel like my English ability is declining.","id":"Ketika bahasa Jepang saya meningkat, saya merasa kemampuan bahasa Inggris saya menurun."},{"jp":"この料理は美味しい一方、ちょっと高いです。","romaji":"Kono ryouri wa oishii ippou, chotto takai desu.","en":"While this dish is delicious, it’s a bit expensive.","id":"Meskipun hidangan ini enak, harganya agak mahal."},{"jp":"彼は優しい一方、厳しい面もある。","romaji":"Kare wa yasashii ippou, kibishii men mo aru.","en":"While he is kind, he also has a strict side.","id":"Meskipun dia baik, dia juga memiliki sisi tegas."}]},{"pattern":"～一方だ (〜ippou da)","meaning":"Expresses that a situation or condition is continuing to increase or decrease in one direction.","meaningId":"Menyatakan bahwa suatu situasi atau kondisi terus meningkat atau menurun dalam satu arah.","formation":"Verb-dictionary form + 一方だ","formationId":"Bentuk kamus kata kerja + 一方だ","examples":[{"jp":"世界の人口は増える一方だ。","romaji":"Sekai no jinkou wa fueru ippou da.","en":"The world's population continues to increase.","id":"Populasi dunia terus meningkat."},{"jp":"この町の治安は悪化する一方だ。","romaji":"Kono machi no chian wa akka suru ippou da.","en":"Public safety in this town is getting worse and worse.","id":"Keamanan publik di kota ini semakin buruk."},{"jp":"僕の日本語は上達する一方だ。","romaji":"Boku no nihongo wa joutatsu suru ippou da.","en":"My Japanese keeps improving.","id":"Bahasa Jepang saya terus meningkat."},{"jp":"夏になると、暑さが厳しくなる一方だ。","romaji":"Natsu ni naru to, atsusa ga kibishiku naru ippou da.","en":"As summer arrives, it just keeps getting hotter.","id":"Saat musim panas tiba, cuaca semakin panas."}]},{"pattern":"～上で (〜ue de)","meaning":"Used to express that something is done after or on the basis of something else; 'after', 'upon'.","meaningId":"Digunakan untuk menyatakan bahwa sesuatu dilakukan setelah atau berdasarkan sesuatu yang lain; 'setelah', 'setelah'.","formation":"Verb-ますstem + 上で, Noun + の上で","formationId":"Kata Kerja-ますbatang + 上で, Kata Benda + の上で","examples":[{"jp":"調査を行った上で、結論を出しましょう。","romaji":"Chousa wo okonatta ue de, ketsuron wo dashimashou.","en":"Let's draw a conclusion after conducting the investigation.","id":"Mari kita ambil kesimpulan setelah melakukan penyelidikan."},{"jp":"就職活動を終えた上で、進学するかどうか決めます。","romaji":"Shuushoku katsudou wo oeta ue de, shingaku suru ka dou ka kimemasu.","en":"I will decide whether to continue my studies after finishing my job hunting.","id":"Saya akan memutuskan apakah akan melanjutkan studi saya setelah menyelesaikan pencarian pekerjaan saya."},{"jp":"試着した上で、この服を買うかどうか考えます。","romaji":"Shichaku shita ue de, kono fuku wo kau ka dou ka kangaemasu.","en":"I'll think about whether to buy these clothes after trying them on.","id":"Saya akan memikirkan apakah akan membeli pakaian ini setelah mencobanya."},{"jp":"経験者の意見を聞いた上で、プロジェクトの方向性を決定しましょう。","romaji":"Keiken sha no iken wo kiita ue de, purojekuto no houkousei wo kettei shimashou.","en":"Let's decide the direction of the project after listening to those with experience.","id":"Mari kita putuskan arah proyek setelah mendengarkan mereka yang berpengalaman."}]},{"pattern":"～上に (〜ue ni)","meaning":"Express 'in addition to', 'besides', 'not only... but also'.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan 'selain', 'selain', 'tidak hanya... tetapi juga'.","formation":"Verb-plain + 上に, い-Adjective + 上に, な-Adjective + な上に, Noun + の上に","formationId":"Kata kerja-biasa + 上に, い-Kata Sifat + 上に, な-Kata Sifat + な上に, Kata Benda + の上に","examples":[{"jp":"彼は頭がいい上に、スポーツも得意です。","romaji":"Kare wa atama ga ii ue ni, supo-tsu mo tokui desu.","en":"In addition to being smart, he is also good at sports.","id":"Selain pintar, ia juga pandai berolahraga."},{"jp":"このドレスは美しい上に、値段も安いです。","romaji":"Kono doresu wa utsukushii ue ni, nedan mo yasui desu.","en":"This dress is not only beautiful but also affordable.","id":"Gaun ini tidak hanya cantik tetapi juga terjangkau."},{"jp":"彼女は優しい上に、料理も上手です。","romaji":"Kanojo wa yasashii ue ni, ryouri mo jouzu desu.","en":"Besides being kind, she is also good at cooking.","id":"Selain baik hati, dia juga pandai memasak."},{"jp":"彼は社長の上に、有名な作家でもある。","romaji":"Kare wa shachou no ue ni, yuumei na sakka demo aru.","en":"Not only is he a company president, but he is also a famous writer.","id":"Dia tidak hanya seorang presiden perusahaan, tetapi dia juga seorang penulis terkenal."}]},{"pattern":"～上は","meaning":"Expresses 'now that', 'since', or 'once'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan 'sekarang itu', 'sejak', atau 'sekali'.","formation":"Verb-casual + 上は, い-Adjective + 上は, な-Adjective + な上は, Noun + の上は","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + 上は, い-Kata Sifat + 上は, な-Kata Sifat + な上は, Kata Benda + の上は","examples":[{"jp":"試験に合格した上は、パーティーを開こう。","romaji":"Shiken ni goukaku shita ue wa, paatii wo hirakou.","en":"Now that I've passed the exam, let's have a party.","id":"Sekarang aku sudah lulus ujian, mari kita berpesta."},{"jp":"この仕事を引き受けた上は、最後までやり遂げるつもりだ。","romaji":"Kono shigoto wo hikiuketa ue wa, saigo made yaritogeru tsumori da.","en":"Now that I have taken on this job, I intend to see it through to the end.","id":"Sekarang setelah saya mengambil pekerjaan ini, saya bermaksud untuk menyelesaikannya sampai akhir."},{"jp":"親切だと言われた上は、手伝ってあげよう。","romaji":"Shinsetsu da to iwareta ue wa, tetsudatte ageyou.","en":"Since you said I'm kind, I'll help you out.","id":"Karena kamu bilang aku baik, aku akan membantumu."},{"jp":"甘いものが好きな上は、このデザートをきっと気に入るでしょう。","romaji":"Amai mono ga suki na ue wa, kono dezaato wo kitto ki ni iru deshou.","en":"Now that you like sweets, you'll surely enjoy this dessert.","id":"Sekarang Anda menyukai makanan manis, Anda pasti akan menikmati makanan penutup ini."}]},{"pattern":"～以上 (〜ijou)","meaning":"Expresses 'since' or 'as long as' in a conditional context.","meaningId":"Menyatakan 'sejak' atau 'selama' dalam konteks bersyarat.","formation":"Verb-casual + 以上, い-Adjective + 以上, な-Adjective + な以上, Noun + の以上","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + 以上, い-Kata Sifat + 以上, な-Kata Sifat + な以上, Kata Benda + の以上","examples":[{"jp":"彼は忙しい以上、手伝いに行っても無駄だろう。","romaji":"Kare wa isogashii ijou, tetsudai ni itte mo muda darou.","en":"Since he's busy, it would be pointless to try helping him.","id":"Karena dia sibuk, tidak ada gunanya mencoba membantunya."},{"jp":"約束した以上、守るべきだ。","romaji":"Yakusoku shita ijou, mamoru beki da.","en":"Since I made a promise, I should keep it.","id":"Karena aku sudah berjanji, aku harus menepatinya."},{"jp":"締め切りが近い以上、全力で仕事をしなければならない。","romaji":"Shimekiri ga chikai ijou, zenryoku de shigoto wo shinakereba naranai.","en":"As long as the deadline is near, I have to work with all my might.","id":"Selama tenggat waktunya dekat, saya harus bekerja sekuat tenaga."},{"jp":"彼女は大学生である以上、勉強が優先されるべきだ。","romaji":"Kanojo wa daigakusei de aru ijou, benkyou ga yuusen sareru beki da.","en":"Since she's a college student, studying should be her priority.","id":"Karena dia seorang mahasiswa, belajar harus menjadi prioritasnya."}]},{"pattern":"～以来 (〜irai)","meaning":"Indicates something happening 'since', 'ever since', or 'after' a particular time.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan sesuatu yang terjadi 'sejak', 'sejak', atau 'setelah' waktu tertentu.","formation":"Verb-past + 以来, い-Adjective + 以来, Noun + 以来","formationId":"Kata kerja-masa lalu + 以来, い-Kata Sifat + 以来, Kata Benda + 以来","examples":[{"jp":"卒業以来、彼女に会っていない。","romaji":"Sotsugyou irai, kanojo ni atte inai.","en":"I haven't seen her since we graduated.","id":"Aku belum melihatnya lagi sejak kami lulus."},{"jp":"子供が生まれて以来、忙しくなった。","romaji":"Kodomo ga umarete irai, isogashiku natta.","en":"I've been busy ever since my child was born.","id":"Saya sibuk sejak anak saya lahir."},{"jp":"東京に引っ越して以来、友達が増えた。","romaji":"Toukyou ni hikkoshite irai, tomodachi ga fueta.","en":"I've made more friends since I moved to Tokyo.","id":"Saya mendapat lebih banyak teman sejak saya pindah ke Tokyo."},{"jp":"あの映画を見た以来、彼女は怖がりになった。","romaji":"Ano eiga wo mita irai, kanojo wa kowagari ni natta.","en":"She's been easily frightened ever since she watched that movie.","id":"Dia mudah ketakutan sejak dia menonton film itu."}]},{"pattern":"～切る (〜kiru)","meaning":"To do something completely or thoroughly.","meaningId":"Untuk melakukan sesuatu secara lengkap atau menyeluruh.","formation":"Verb-stem + 切る","formationId":"Batang kata kerja + 切る","examples":[{"jp":"彼は試験勉強をがんばり切るつもりだ。","romaji":"Kare wa shiken benkyou o ganbari kiru tsumori da.","en":"He intends to give his absolute all to exam study.","id":"Dia bermaksud memberikan segalanya untuk belajar ujian."},{"jp":"この仕事を終わり切るまで、帰らないでください。","romaji":"Kono shigoto o owari kiru made, kaeranai de kudasai.","en":"Please don't go home until you've completely finished this job.","id":"Tolong jangan pulang sampai Anda menyelesaikan pekerjaan ini sepenuhnya."},{"jp":"友達と喧嘩して、何も言い切れなかった。","romaji":"Tomodachi to kenka shite, nanimo iikirenakatta.","en":"I argued with my friend and couldn't say everything I wanted to say.","id":"Saya berdebat dengan teman saya dan tidak bisa mengatakan semua yang ingin saya katakan."},{"jp":"彼らは、そのゲームをやり切ることができました。","romaji":"Karera wa, sono geemu o yarikiru koto ga dekimashita.","en":"They were able to complete that game thoroughly.","id":"Mereka mampu menyelesaikan permainan itu dengan tuntas."}]},{"pattern":"～反面 (〜hanmen)","meaning":"Express contrast between two aspects; 'on the one hand', 'on the other hand'.","meaningId":"Mengungkapkan kontras antara dua aspek; 'di satu sisi', 'di sisi lain'.","formation":"Verb-casual + 反面, い-Adjective + 反面, な-Adjective + である反面, Noun + である反面","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + 反面, い-Kata Sifat + 反面, な-Kata Sifat + である反面, Kata Benda + である反面","examples":[{"jp":"この車は速い反面、燃費が悪いです。","romaji":"Kono kuruma wa hayai hanmen, nenpi ga warui desu.","en":"On the one hand, this car is fast, but on the other hand, it has poor fuel efficiency.","id":"Di satu sisi mobil ini cepat, namun di sisi lain efisiensi bahan bakarnya buruk."},{"jp":"彼は頭がいい反面、運動が苦手です。","romaji":"Kare wa atama ga ii hanmen, undou ga nigate desu.","en":"On the one hand, he is smart, but on the other hand, he's not good at sports.","id":"Di satu sisi dia pintar, tapi di sisi lain dia kurang pandai dalam olahraga."},{"jp":"彼女は親切である反面、面倒見が良すぎることがある。","romaji":"Kanojo wa shinsetsu de aru hanmen, mendoumi ga yoi sugiru koto ga aru.","en":"On the one hand, she is kind, but on the other hand, she can be too helpful.","id":"Di satu sisi, dia baik, tapi di sisi lain, dia terlalu membantu."},{"jp":"この仕事は給料が高い反面、ストレスがたくさんあります。","romaji":"Kono shigoto wa kyuuryou ga takai hanmen, sutoresu ga takusan arimasu.","en":"On the one hand, this job pays well, but on the other hand, it's quite stressful.","id":"Di satu sisi, pekerjaan ini bergaji tinggi, namun di sisi lain cukup membuat stres."}]},{"pattern":"～向け (〜muke)","meaning":"Indicating target or intended audience.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan target atau audiens yang dituju.","formation":"Noun + 向け","formationId":"Kata benda + 向け","examples":[{"jp":"この雑誌は若者向けです。","romaji":"Kono zasshi wa wakamono-muke desu.","en":"This magazine is aimed at young people.","id":"Majalah ini ditujukan untuk generasi muda."},{"jp":"スーパーで家族向けの食品セットが売っています。","romaji":"Suupaa de kazoku-muke no shokuhin setto ga utte imasu.","en":"The supermarket sells food sets intended for families.","id":"Supermarket menjual set makanan yang ditujukan untuk keluarga."},{"jp":"このアプリは初心者向けに作られています。","romaji":"Kono apuri wa shoshinsha-muke ni tsukurarete imasu.","en":"This application is designed for beginners.","id":"Aplikasi ini dirancang untuk pemula."},{"jp":"このレストランはビーガン向けのメニューが充実しています。","romaji":"Kono resutoran wa bi-gan-muke no menyu ga juujitsu shite imasu.","en":"This restaurant has an extensive menu aimed at vegans.","id":"Restoran ini memiliki menu beragam yang ditujukan untuk vegan."}]},{"pattern":"～恐れがある (〜osore ga aru)","meaning":"Express a concern or fear that something undesirable might occur.","meaningId":"Ekspresikan kekhawatiran atau ketakutan bahwa sesuatu yang tidak diinginkan akan terjadi.","formation":"Verb-dictionary form + 恐れがある","formationId":"Bentuk kamus kata kerja + 恐れがある","examples":[{"jp":"地震が来る恐れがあるため、避難所に行ってください。","romaji":"Jishin ga kuru osore ga aru tame, hinanjo ni itte kudasai.","en":"Please go to the evacuation center because there is a risk of an earthquake.","id":"Silakan ke pusat evakuasi karena ada risiko gempa."},{"jp":"彼は事故に遭う恐れがあるので、注意して運転してください。","romaji":"Kare wa jiko ni au osore ga aru node, chuui shite unten shite kudasai.","en":"There's a possibility he might have an accident, so please drive carefully.","id":"Ada kemungkinan dia mengalami kecelakaan, jadi harap berkendara dengan hati-hati."},{"jp":"この薬を飲みすぎると、副作用の恐れがある。","romaji":"Kono kusuri wo nomisugiru to, fukusayou no osore ga aru.","en":"If you take too much of this medicine, there is a risk of side effects.","id":"Jika Anda mengonsumsi obat ini terlalu banyak, ada risiko efek samping."},{"jp":"低い予算でこのプロジェクトを進めると、品質が低くなる恐れがある。","romaji":"Hikui yosan de kono purojekuto wo susumeru to, hinshitsu ga hikuku naru osore ga aru.","en":"If we proceed with this project on a low budget, the quality may suffer.","id":"Jika kami melanjutkan proyek ini dengan anggaran rendah, kualitasnya mungkin menurun."}]},{"pattern":"～折には (〜ori ni wa)","meaning":"Expresses 'when' or 'in case of' specific situations or timings.","meaningId":"Mengekspresikan 'kapan' atau 'jika terjadi' situasi atau waktu tertentu.","formation":"Verb-dictionary form + 折には, Verb-た form + 折には, い-Adjective + 折には, な-Adjective + な折には, Noun + の折には","formationId":"Bentuk kamus kata kerja + 折には, Bentuk kata kerja-た + 折には, い-Kata Sifat + 折には, な-Kata Sifat + な折には, Kata Benda + の折には","examples":[{"jp":"喉が渇く折には、このペットボトルの水を飲んでください。","romaji":"Nodo ga kawaku ori ni wa, kono pettobotoru no mizu o nonde kudasai.","en":"When you get thirsty, please drink water from this bottle.","id":"Saat Anda haus, silakan minum air dari botol ini."},{"jp":"この地域に来る折には、この神社に必ずお参りしましょう。","romaji":"Kono chiiki ni kuru ori ni wa, kono jinja ni kanarazu omairi shimashou.","en":"When you visit this area, make sure to go to this shrine.","id":"Ketika Anda mengunjungi daerah ini, pastikan untuk pergi ke kuil ini."},{"jp":"彼が元気じゃない折には、具合が悪いか尋ねてください。","romaji":"Kare ga genki ja nai ori ni wa, guai ga warui ka tazunete kudasai.","en":"If he doesn't seem well, please ask if he's feeling sick.","id":"Jika dia tampak tidak sehat, tanyakan apakah dia merasa sakit."},{"jp":"チャンスがある折には、躊躇せずに行動しましょう。","romaji":"Chansu ga aru ori ni wa, chuucho sezu ni koudou shimashou.","en":"When you have an opportunity, act without hesitation.","id":"Ketika Anda mempunyai kesempatan, bertindaklah tanpa ragu-ragu."}]},{"pattern":"～末","meaning":"Express the outcome after a period of time or series of actions; 'after', 'as a result of'.","meaningId":"Menyatakan hasil setelah jangka waktu tertentu atau serangkaian tindakan; 'setelah', 'akibat dari'.","formation":"Noun + 末","formationId":"Kata benda + 末","examples":[{"jp":"長い議論の末、ようやく意見がまとまった。","romaji":"Nagai giron no sue, youyaku iken ga matomatta.","en":"After a long discussion, we finally reached a consensus.","id":"Setelah berdiskusi panjang, akhirnya kami mencapai konsensus."},{"jp":"一週間の勉強の末、試験に合格した。","romaji":"Isshuukan no benkyou no sue, shiken ni goukaku shita.","en":"After a week of studying, I passed the exam.","id":"Setelah seminggu belajar, saya lulus ujian."},{"jp":"何度も失敗の末、成功を手に入れた。","romaji":"Nando mo shippai no sue, seikou wo te ni ireta.","en":"After many failures, I finally achieved success.","id":"Setelah banyak kegagalan, akhirnya saya mencapai kesuksesan."},{"jp":"彼との別れの末、新しい人生を始めた。","romaji":"Kare to no wakare no sue, atarashii jinsei wo hajimeta.","en":"After breaking up with him, I started a new life.","id":"Setelah putus dengannya, saya memulai hidup baru."}]},{"pattern":"～次第 (〜shidai)","meaning":"Expresses 'as soon as' (when used with Verb-ますstem) or 'depending on' (when used with a noun).","meaningId":"Menyatakan 'segera' (bila digunakan dengan kata kerja-ますstem) atau 'tergantung pada' (bila digunakan dengan kata benda).","formation":"Verb-ますstem + 次第, Noun + 次第","formationId":"Kata kerja-ますbatang + 次第, Kata Benda + 次第","examples":[{"jp":"仕事が終わり次第、帰ります。","romaji":"Shigoto ga owari shidai, kaerimasu.","en":"I will go home as soon as I finish work.","id":"Saya akan pulang segera setelah saya selesai bekerja."},{"jp":"お客様のご意見次第で、サービスを改善します。","romaji":"Okyakusama no goiken shidai de, saabisu wo kaizen shimasu.","en":"We will improve our services depending on customer feedback.","id":"Kami akan meningkatkan layanan kami tergantung pada umpan balik pelanggan."},{"jp":"彼の返事次第で、パーティーに行くかどうか決めます。","romaji":"Kare no henji shidai de, paatii ni iku ka dou ka kimemasu.","en":"I will decide whether or not to go to the party depending on his answer.","id":"Saya akan memutuskan apakah akan pergi ke pesta atau tidak tergantung pada jawabannya."},{"jp":"天気次第で、ピクニックを予定しています。","romaji":"Tenki shidai de, pikunikku wo yotei shite imasu.","en":"We are planning a picnic depending on the weather.","id":"Kami merencanakan piknik tergantung cuaca."}]},{"pattern":"～次第で (〜shidai de)","meaning":"Indicates 'depending on; based on' a certain factor or situation.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan 'tergantung pada; berdasarkan pada faktor atau situasi tertentu.","formation":"Noun + 次第で","formationId":"Kata benda + 次第で","examples":[{"jp":"仕事の終わり次第で、家に帰る時間が変わります。","romaji":"Shigoto no owari shidai de, ie ni kaeru jikan ga kawarimasu.","en":"Depending on when I finish work, the time I go home may change.","id":"Tergantung kapan saya selesai bekerja, waktu pulang saya mungkin berubah."},{"jp":"天気次第で、ピクニックに行く予定です。","romaji":"Tenki shidai de, pikunikku ni iku yotei desu.","en":"We plan to go on a picnic depending on the weather.","id":"Kami berencana untuk pergi piknik tergantung cuaca."},{"jp":"彼の気分次第で、パーティーに参加するかどうか決まります。","romaji":"Kare no kibun shidai de, paatii ni sanka suru ka dou ka kimarimasu.","en":"Whether he participates in the party depends on his mood.","id":"Apakah dia berpartisipasi dalam pesta itu tergantung pada suasana hatinya."},{"jp":"会議の進行次第で、決定が変わるかもしれません。","romaji":"Kaigi no shinkou shidai de, kettei ga kawaru kamoshiremasen.","en":"The decision may change depending on how the meeting progresses.","id":"Keputusan dapat berubah tergantung pada bagaimana pertemuan berlangsung."}]},{"pattern":"～次第です (〜shidai desu)","meaning":"A polite/formal way to say 'it depends on...' or 'as soon as...', often used in concluding statements.","meaningId":"Cara sopan/formal untuk mengatakan 'itu tergantung pada...' atau 'segera...', sering digunakan dalam pernyataan penutup.","formation":"Verb-ますstem + 次第です (or Noun + 次第です)","formationId":"Kata Kerja-ますbatang + 次第です (atau Kata Benda + 次第です)","examples":[{"jp":"天気次第ですが、明日はピクニックに行こうと思います。","romaji":"Tenki shidai desu ga, ashita wa pikunikku ni ikou to omoimasu.","en":"It depends on the weather, but I’m thinking of going for a picnic tomorrow.","id":"Tergantung cuaca, tapi aku berencana pergi piknik besok."},{"jp":"試験の結果次第ですが、留学したいと考えています。","romaji":"Shiken no kekka shidai desu ga, ryuugaku shitai to kangaete imasu.","en":"It depends on my exam results, but I'm considering studying abroad.","id":"Itu tergantung pada hasil ujianku, tapi aku sedang mempertimbangkan untuk belajar di luar negeri."},{"jp":"お客様のご意見次第で新メニューを追加する次第です。","romaji":"Okyakusama no goiken shidai de shin menyuu wo tsuika suru shidai desu.","en":"We intend to add a new menu item depending on our customers’ feedback.","id":"Kami bermaksud menambahkan item menu baru tergantung pada masukan pelanggan kami."},{"jp":"申請が完了次第ですので、手続きが終わったらパスポートを受け取れます。","romaji":"Shinsei ga kanryou shidai desu no de, tetsudzuki ga owattara pasupooto wo uketoremasu.","en":"As soon as the application is completed, you'll be able to receive your passport.","id":"Segera setelah aplikasi selesai, Anda akan dapat menerima paspor Anda."}]},{"pattern":"～気味 (〜gimi)","meaning":"Indicates a slight feeling or tendency toward a particular state.","meaningId":"Menunjukkan sedikit perasaan atau kecenderungan terhadap keadaan tertentu.","formation":"Noun + 気味 (e.g., 風邪気味, 寝不足気味, 緊張気味)","formationId":"Kata benda + 気味 (misalnya, 風邪気味, 寝不足気味, 緊張気味)","examples":[{"jp":"最近寝不足気味で、ちょっと疲れています。","romaji":"Saikin nebusoku gimi de, chotto tsukarete imasu.","en":"Lately, I'm feeling somewhat sleep-deprived and a bit tired.","id":"Akhir-akhir ini, saya merasa agak kurang tidur dan sedikit lelah."},{"jp":"この部屋は暗い気味だから、もっと明るい照明をつけよう。","romaji":"Kono heya wa kurai gimi dakara, motto akarui shoumei wo tsukeyou.","en":"This room is a bit dark, so let's install brighter lighting.","id":"Ruangan ini agak gelap, jadi mari kita pasang pencahayaan yang lebih terang."},{"jp":"彼女は緊張気味で話していました。","romaji":"Kanojo wa kinchou gimi de hanashite imashita.","en":"She was speaking somewhat nervously.","id":"Dia berbicara dengan agak gugup."},{"jp":"彼の声は風邪気味だったね。","romaji":"Kare no koe wa kaze gimi datta ne.","en":"His voice sounded like he might have a slight cold.","id":"Suaranya terdengar seperti dia mungkin sedang flu."}]},{"pattern":"～限り (〜kagiri)","meaning":"Expresses 'as long as', 'while', or 'to the extent that' a certain condition holds true.","meaningId":"Menyatakan 'selama', 'sementara', atau 'sejauh' suatu kondisi tertentu benar.","formation":"Verb-casual + 限り, い-Adjective + 限り, な-Adjective + な限り, Noun + の限り","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + 限り, い-Kata Sifat + 限り, な-Kata Sifat + な限り, Kata Benda + の限り","examples":[{"jp":"元気な限り、運動し続けます。","romaji":"Genki na kagiri, undou shi tsuzukemasu.","en":"As long as I'm healthy, I'll keep exercising.","id":"Selama saya sehat, saya akan terus berolahraga."},{"jp":"お金がある限り、旅行を楽しみたい。","romaji":"Okane ga aru kagiri, ryokou o tanoshimitai.","en":"As long as I have money, I'd like to travel.","id":"Selama saya punya uang, saya ingin bepergian."},{"jp":"彼が話し続ける限り、このプロジェクトのメリットが伝わるでしょう。","romaji":"Kare ga hanashi tsudzukeru kagiri, kono purojekuto no meritto ga tsutawaru deshou.","en":"As long as he keeps talking about it, the benefits of this project will be conveyed.","id":"Selama dia terus membicarakannya, manfaat proyek ini akan tersampaikan."},{"jp":"勉強する限り、試験に合格できる可能性が高まります。","romaji":"Benkyou suru kagiri, shiken ni goukaku dekiru kanousei ga takamarimasu.","en":"As long as you study, you'll have a higher chance of passing the exam.","id":"Selama Anda belajar, Anda akan memiliki peluang lebih tinggi untuk lulus ujian."}]},{"pattern":"～際に (〜sai ni)","meaning":"Means 'when', 'while', or 'on the occasion of' a certain event or situation.","meaningId":"Berarti 'ketika', 'sementara', atau 'pada saat' suatu peristiwa atau situasi tertentu.","formation":"Verb-casual + 際に, い-Adjective + 際に, な-Adjective + な際に, Noun + の際に","formationId":"Kata Kerja-kasual + 際に, い-Kata Sifat + 際に, な-Kata Sifat + な際に, Kata Benda + の際に","examples":[{"jp":"出発の際に、パスポートを忘れないでください。","romaji":"Shuppatsu no sai ni, pasupooto wo wasurenai de kudasai.","en":"When departing, please don't forget your passport.","id":"Saat berangkat, mohon jangan lupa paspor Anda."},{"jp":"地震が起こる際に、すぐに避難してください。","romaji":"Jishin ga okoru sai ni, sugu ni hinan shite kudasai.","en":"When an earthquake occurs, please evacuate immediately.","id":"Apabila terjadi gempa, harap segera mengungsi."},{"jp":"日本へ来る際に、お土産をたくさん買うつもりです。","romaji":"Nihon e kuru sai ni, omiyage wo takusan kau tsumori desu.","en":"When I come to Japan, I plan to buy lots of souvenirs.","id":"Ketika saya datang ke Jepang, saya berencana untuk membeli banyak oleh-oleh."},{"jp":"面接の際に、スーツを着用してください。","romaji":"Mensetsu no sai ni, suutsu wo chakuyou shite kudasai.","en":"Please wear a suit when attending the interview.","id":"Harap mengenakan jas saat menghadiri wawancara."}]}]
